"\n"
"你试着动了动，浑身上下却无一处不疼。你想忍住不出声，还是不由得呻吟了一声，引起了她的注"
"意。她望向你，眼神里透着……关切。要不是她和丈夫刚刚还想杀了你，你几乎会相信那是真心的。她"
"放下怀里的木柴，快步赶到床边。你不由自主地打了个寒战。她几次欲言又止，最后叹了口气，轻轻"
"笑了一声。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Given [Companion Name] and I's reception, I see that peaceful nature has died out."
msgstr "看你们招待我和[Companion Name]的方式，这地方如今也没多平和了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I won't ask for either of you to forgiven Talm and I's transgressions against you, only "
"explain why we chose this path."
msgstr "我不会求你们原谅我和塔尔姆的所作所为，只想解释我们为什么选择这么做。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My people sought to ascertain the fates through communion with the stars, as you've "
"gathered by now. Our use of summoning itself was rather limited, and focused on the "
"practical, usually creating messengers to help us made sense of the fates."
msgstr ""
"你应该已经知道，我的族人会与群星沟通，借此探知命运。我们很少使用召唤术，用途也大多很实"
"际。通常只是召出一些信使，帮我们解读命运。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We were called the Fateseekers, and we learned of the calamity far before it ever was "
"set into motion."
msgstr "我们被称为寻命者。早在灾难开始酝酿之前，我们就已预见了它。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You'll hear more of this calamity as you rest here, I promise you that."
msgstr "你在这里休养的这段日子，会慢慢了解那场灾难。我向你保证。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Nevertheless. The Fateseekers' visions all culminated in one final premonition of the "
"future."
msgstr "说回正题。寻命者看到的种种幻象，最终都指向了同一个未来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A creature so vile, born of a nation of sacrificed life. As it let out its first "
"breath, the world in its entirety twisted and died."
msgstr ""
"举国生灵被献祭，孕育出一个邪恶至极的怪物。它吐出第一口气息时，整个世界便随之扭曲、灭亡。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My people's visions can be esoteric at times, but this was seen with perfect clarity "
"across my entire clan."
msgstr "族人们看到的幻象有时晦涩难懂，但这一次，全族上下都看得清清楚楚。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is what the calamity would culminate in."
msgstr "那就是灾难最终会带来的结局。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But this 'calamity' you cannot speak of happened already, no? That's why there aren't "
"many summoners left, outside of the Soulsmiths."
msgstr ""
"可你不能说的那场“灾难”，不是早就发生了吗？所以除了炼魂师，如今才没剩下几个召唤师。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Unless the world underwent some kind of rebirth afterward, assuming your clan was even "
"correct in the first place, what does this have to do with why you attacked us?"
msgstr ""
"先不说你们预言得准不准，总不能是世界毁灭之后又重生了吧？而且，这跟你们袭击我们有什么关"
"系？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...My people were correct. The only thing we were unsure of was the timeframe."
msgstr "……我的族人没有看错。我们唯一无法确定的，是它发生的时间。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This creature... It is what the Soulsmiths seek to bring about."
msgstr "那个怪物……正是炼魂师想要造出来的东西。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...why?"
msgstr "……为什么？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Before you can understand, you must learn this history of Respite."
msgstr "想明白这一点，你得先了解安歇之境的过去。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But I've already kept you so long, I thank you for your patience. I'll explain more to "
"you, in time, but please, acquaint yourself with this place first. Leave if you must, "
"just come and find me. You may always return later."
msgstr ""
"不过，我已经拉着你说了这么久，谢谢你耐心听我讲完。往后我会继续向你解释。现在，先熟悉一下"
"这里吧。如果非得离开，就来找我。以后你随时都可以回来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Era rises from the bedside and offers a small curtsy. Your next question is answered "
"before it even leaves your mouth. [Companion Name] is in the next room over, but hasn't "
"yet awakened.\n"
"\n"
"You follow Era out, who wanders off down the hall. You knock on [Companion Name]'s door "
"before letting yourself in. Like you were, she rests in a large bed and is seemingly "
"unharmed, but you see that she's restless, perhaps having strange dreams like yours "
"before you awoke.\n"
"\n"
"You go to her and speak her name softly, and hold her hand. You feel the first bit of "
"relief you have since you woke, Era's earlier words having more of the opposite effect "
"on you.\n"
"\n"
"You stay for a long while, before heading to the window and pulling open the curtain. "
"You weren't sure what you'd find, but you weren't expecting... endless rows of white "
"lily-like flowers amidst a field of grey grass that stretch out further than you can "
"see. In their own small clusters are other flowers, almost always another distinct "
"color. You see blues, greens, browns, and occasional bright reds as well. They all seem "
"pristine, and the field of dark grass is free from any other growth.\n"
"\n"
"As you look at the sky, the dark purple sky feels alien to you, the stars burn a deep, "
"lush green, their patterns completely unfamiliar to you."
msgstr ""
"艾拉从床边起身，微微屈膝行礼。你还没来得及问出下一个问题，她便给出了答案。[Companion "
"Name]就在隔壁，只是还没醒。\n"
"\n"
"你跟着艾拉走出房间，她随后沿着走廊离开了。你敲了敲[Companion Name]的房门，推门进去。和刚"
"才的你一样，她躺在一张大床上，看起来没有受伤，却睡得并不安稳。也许她也和你醒来前一样，正"
"做着奇怪的梦。\n"
"\n"
"你走到床边，轻声唤她的名字，握住她的手。醒来之后，你头一次稍稍放下心来。艾拉先前那番话，"
"反倒让你更不安了。\n"
"\n"
"你陪了她很久，才起身走到窗边，拉开窗帘。你不知道窗外会是什么景象，却怎么也没想到……灰色的"
"草地上，一片片形似百合的白花绵延不绝，直铺到视线尽头。其间还散布着一小簇一小簇的花，每一"
"簇几乎都是另一种鲜明的颜色。有蓝的、绿的、褐色的，偶尔还能看见一抹鲜红。每一朵花都完好无"
"瑕，暗色的草地上也没有别的杂草杂木。\n"
"\n"
"你抬头望去，深紫色的天空陌生得让你恍若身处异世。群星闪着浓郁的绿光，排列成你从未见过的模"
"样。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Bring me back to what you wish to show me. (Divination)"
msgstr "带我回去吧，让我看看你想让我看见的。（占卜）"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just... hope I can understand it. (Divination)"
msgstr "我只希望……这次能看懂。（占卜）"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you practice the divination methods Era taught you back in her tower, the green "
"stars push themselves into your mind. Unlike your out-of-body experience then, you find "
"yourself... back in your earlier dream. The bone crown feels more comfortable on your "
"head now, and you feel more... at peace.\n"
"\n"
"You walk amongst the bodies and realize that they aren't corpses. Yet. They lay "
"somewhere between life and death, much like the plane you currently reside.\n"
"\n"
"This was the dream your people, the Lifebinders, chose for themselves. To fall into an "
"endless, beautiful dream, far removed from the horrors the world faces.\n"
"\n"
"Alongside your people are others, from more clans. Respite was open to all who chose "
"it.\n"
"\n"
"You want so desperately to lay down and join them in the grass, but... you know you "
"can't. The ritual isn't complete, and you're the only one who can see it to its end.\n"
"\n"
"You'll pulled out of the dream as you feel a hand on your real shoulder. [Companion "
"Name] looks at you with concern."
msgstr ""
"你按照艾拉在塔里教过的方法开始占卜，绿色的群星随即涌入脑海。这次，你没有像当初那样灵魂出"
"窍，而是……回到了先前的梦中。头上的骨冠似乎不再那么别扭，你的心也……平静了些。\n"
"\n"
"你从那些躺倒的人之间走过，才意识到他们并不是尸体。至少还不是。他们徘徊在生死之间，正如你"
"此刻身处的这片天地。\n"
"\n"
"这是你的族人，生命缚誓者，为自己选择的梦。沉入永不终结的美梦，远离世间的一切苦难。\n"
"\n"
"躺在族人身旁的，还有来自其他氏族的人。只要愿意，任何人都能来到安歇之境。\n"
"\n"
"你恨不得也在草地上躺下，加入他们。可是……你知道自己不能。仪式还没有完成，而能将它完成的，"
"只剩下你。\n"
"\n"
"有人把手搭在了你现实中的肩上，将你从梦中唤回。[Companion Name]正担忧地望着你。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[Player Name]? Oh... I'm so happy to see you."
msgstr "[Player Name]？啊……能见到你真好。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Are you okay? Why are you crying?"
msgstr "你没事吧？怎么哭了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... I don't know. But I'm so glad that you're okay."
msgstr "我……我不知道。不过，你没事真是太好了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You are okay, right?"
msgstr "你没事，对吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I think Era killed me."
msgstr "……我觉得，艾拉把我杀了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"She clearly didn't do a good enough job, though, since I'm still... here. Wherever here "
"is."
msgstr "不过她显然没杀彻底，不然我怎么还在……这里。虽然我也不知道这是哪儿。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Back in that dark chamber, after that flesh monster?"
msgstr "是在那间黑漆漆的大厅里？咱们逃过那头血肉怪物之后？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yeah. She ran her claws through my chest. But uh... I don't seem to have so much as a "
"scratch on me."
msgstr "嗯。她的爪子刺穿了我的胸口。可，呃……我身上好像连道伤口都没有。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We saw Talm bring Era back from the dead, or close to it. Maybe they did the same for "
"you?"
msgstr "咱们见过塔尔姆把艾拉救活。就算她当时没死，也差不多了。也许他们对你做了同样的事？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I passed out shortly after fighting Talm off."
msgstr "我抵挡住塔尔姆之后，没过多久就昏过去了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So, you beat your opponent, huh? You're gonna make me look bad."
msgstr "这么说，你还打赢了？这可显得我太没用了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...You know, for a dead woman, you seem to be taking things in stride."
msgstr "……你这刚死过一回的人，倒是挺想得开。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, I feel like I've gotten the best sleep I've had in months, and you're here, so... "
"I figure we're somewhat safe."
msgstr ""
"我感觉自己好几个月都没睡得这么舒服了，而且你也在，所以……我想，咱们暂时应该还算安全。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But I do hope you'll fill me in on how exactly we got here."
msgstr "不过，咱们到底是怎么到这儿来的，你可得跟我说说。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You wipe your face and join [Companion Name] on the bed, and do your best to fill her "
"in on everything you know. She nods along, and asks dozens of questions that you don't "
"have the answers to. Yet, you hope to yourself.\n"
"\n"
"You talk about your dreams, and [Companion Name] speaks of hers. She has seen flashes "
"of time, all over the world in lands neither of you can even begin to guess the "
"location of. In each, clans of summoners from endless walks of life all fighting to "
"survive against... each other.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] describes battle after battle. Some with large armies of man and "
"beast, others... darkly similar to the attack on Azamire, but with creatures far "
"different to those of the Soulsmiths'.\n"
"\n"
"When she finishes, she mentions how it feels like she's been stopped mid-sentence, and "
"needs to know how the stories end. She figures that if you continued to dream while "
"looking at the stars outside, she plans to do the same soon.\n"
"\n"
"You both return to the window and find that the sky has shifted from purple to a hazy "
"pink, with the stars taking on a lighter hue. Whether it's due to the passage of time "
"or what, you cannot begin to tell, but as you gaze at them together, you feel the same "
"draw as before."
msgstr ""
"你擦了擦脸，和[Companion Name]一起坐到床边，尽力把知道的事都告诉她。她边听边点头，问了一"
"大堆你答不上来的问题。但愿只是暂时答不上来，你心想。\n"
"\n"
"你说起了自己的梦，[Companion Name]也讲起了她的。她梦见了世界各地不同时刻的片段，那些地方"
"究竟在哪里，你们谁也猜不出来。每一个片段里，都有不同出身的召唤师氏族为了生存而战。他们的"
"敌人……正是彼此。\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name]讲了一场又一场战斗。有的是人与野兽组成的大军交锋，有的……则像极了阿扎米尔"
"遇袭时的惨状，只是其中的怪物与炼魂师造出的截然不同。\n"
"\n"
"讲完之后，她说那感觉就像话听到一半突然断了，非得知道后面的结局才行。既然你望着窗外的群"
"星，就能继续先前的梦，她也打算尽快试试。\n"
"\n"
"你们一同回到窗边，发现天空已由紫色变成朦胧的粉色，星光也淡了些。你无从判断这是时间流逝所"
"致，还是另有原因。不过，当你们一同仰望群星时，你再次感受到了先前那股牵引。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"After a long while, you're able to urge yourself back into your dream, but find "
"yourself in a distant land, completely unfamiliar to you. \n"
"\n"
"You clutch a wooden railing tight enough to splinter the wood as you look out over the "
"city in front of you.\n"
"\n"
"Brightly painted wooden structures fly high above a jungle canopy, suspended in the air "
"as if held on strings tied to passing clouds. People float to-and-fro, passing between "
"buildings calmly, living their lives blissfully untouched by the battles their people "
"raged against your own halfway across the world. You're the last of the Lifebinders, "
"all others now peacefully awaiting you to deliver to them the paradise they were "
"promised. An endless dream where they'll never again be subject to the ongoing horrors "
"of the world.\n"
"\n"
"As you withdraw the black gemstone from your cloak, you know you're dooming these "
"people. It doesn't stop you. With shaking hands, you piece the stone with a blackened "
"dagger made exclusively for this day. Dark mist begins to leak from the stone, curling "
"around your hands and forming a thick cloud in front of you. It's not enough for you to "
"release it.\n"
"\n"
"The hungry beast needs guidance. Direction.\n"
"\n"
"You will it forward."
msgstr ""
"过了很久，你终于设法重回梦中，却发现自己身处一片遥远而陌生的土地。\n"
"\n"
"你望着眼前的城市，双手紧紧扣住木栏，几乎要把木头捏裂。\n"
"\n"
"漆着鲜艳色彩的木制建筑高悬在丛林树冠之上，仿佛有细线将它们系在飘过的云朵上。人们在楼宇之"
"间悠然飘行，过着安逸的生活。半个世界之外，他们的族人正与你的族人厮杀，可战火丝毫没有波及"
"这里。你是最后一位生命缚誓者。其他人如今都已安然睡去，等着你将他们送入许诺中的乐园。在那"
"里，美梦永不终结，他们也再不必承受世间无休无止的苦难。\n"
"\n"
"你从斗篷里取出那颗黑色宝石，知道自己将给眼前这些人带来灭顶之灾。可你没有停手。你双手颤"
"抖，用那把专为今日打造的乌黑匕首刺入宝石。黑雾从宝石中渗出，缠上你的双手，在面前聚成一团"
"浓雾。只是放出它，还不够。\n"
"\n"
"这头饥饿的野兽需要引导。需要一个方向。\n"
"\n"
"你用意念驱使它向前。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ19"
msgstr "MQ19"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The Price of Paradise - Little by little, Respite has begun to show you what it took to "
"build, yet, you've only scratched the surface of what summoning has wrought upon the "
"land."
msgstr ""
"乐园的代价——安歇之境正一点点向你揭示建造它所付出的代价。然而，召唤术究竟给这片大地带来了"
"什么，你所知的仍只是冰山一角。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Damn him."
msgstr "这个混蛋。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That should be enough."
msgstr "这些应该够了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You feel... wrong. The body you inhabited was doubtlessly Talm's, though untold "
"centuries past. What... how could someone be so driven to do something they know is so "
"horrifically wrong. You felt his very being recoil as he carved into the gemstone, "
"but... it didn't stop him.\n"
"\n"
"You need to know.\n"
"\n"
"You leave the room and [Companion Name] behind you, who still seems lost within her own "
"mind.\n"
"\n"
"The halls are lined with endless murals and depictions of the world, but you hardly see "
"them as you're driven forward with righteous purpose. You find yourself outside. The "
"monster you seek sits far out in the field of grey grass, in front of a set of two "
"white flowers.\n"
"\n"
"The path through the grass is well-worn, seemingly travelled countless times."
msgstr ""
"你心里……很不是滋味。梦中你附身的那个人，无疑就是塔尔姆，只是不知道那是多少个世纪以前的"
"他。怎么……怎么会有人明知一件事错得如此可怕，还执意去做？匕首刺入宝石时，你分明感到他从心"
"底抗拒着这一切，可……他还是没有停手。\n"
"\n"
"你非弄清楚不可。\n"
"\n"
"你离开房间，留下[Companion Name]独自待着。她似乎仍沉浸在自己的思绪中。走廊两侧满是壁画，"
"描绘着世间的种种景象，可你几乎无心去看，只一心想找他问个明白。不知不觉，你已走到了外面。"
"你要找的那个怪物坐在远处的灰色草地里，面前是两朵白花。\n"
"\n"
"草间的小径已被踩得平整，显然有人在这里走过无数次。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...What did you do?"
msgstr "……你究竟做了什么？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm afraid you'll need to be a bit more specific than that."
msgstr "恐怕得说清楚些，我才知道你指什么。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The floating city. The gemstone. I saw it."
msgstr "那座浮在空中的城市。那颗宝石。我都看见了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ah. And here I thought you'd be a bit more interested in why I tried to kill you."
msgstr "啊。我还以为，你会更想知道我为什么要杀你。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll get to that."
msgstr "这笔账待会儿再算。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I can't even recall the name of the city anymore."
msgstr "我已经记不起那座城叫什么了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But the people, the Brazi..."
msgstr "但那里的人，布拉齐人……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Amongst the dozens of clans my people fought, none were more... through in their "
"eradication on the Lifebinders."
msgstr ""
"当年与我们交战的氏族有几十个，可论起对生命缚誓者的赶尽杀绝，没有哪个比他们更……彻底。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You've seen what I've done for Era, back in the tower. My people were exceptional "
"healers."
msgstr "在塔里，你见过我是怎么救艾拉的。我的族人很擅长治愈之术。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Lifebinders focused more on the body than the Soulsmiths, who focus more on the... "
"Well. You can puzzle that one out."
msgstr "生命缚誓者更注重肉体，炼魂师则更注重……唉。这个你自己也猜得到。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But our control of one's spirit was quite impressive as well. These skills made us "
"incredibly sought after allies in the calamity."
msgstr "不过，我们操控灵魂的本事也相当了得。正因如此，灾难期间，许多氏族都争着拉拢我们。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Get to the point."
msgstr "说重点。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Better yet. How about you ask my people yourself?"
msgstr "这样吧。你何不亲自问问我的族人？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"After all this time, I'm sure they're quite tired of having me as their sole point of "
"contact with the outside world."
msgstr "这么多年，他们只能通过我与外界联系，想必也早就腻了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...what? "
msgstr "……什么？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You want to learn, don't you?"
msgstr "你不是想知道吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll tell you whatever you want to know after you speak to the Dreamers."
msgstr "先跟入梦者聊聊。聊完之后，你想知道什么，我都告诉你。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't want to do this, but I doubt you'll listen to me otherwise..."
msgstr "我不想这么做，可不这样，你恐怕不会听我的……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Sit."
msgstr "坐下。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"All thoughts of resistance vanish as you find yourself dropping to your knees against "
"your will after Talm snaps his fingers, the muscles in your legs giving out completely. "
"Talm slowly cups one of the white flowers in front of him and plucks several petals "
"from it with a mix of reverence and practiced effort, as though he's done it a million "
"times before. He waves you off, telling you to go gather as many as wish. Just as you "
"consider telling him to do it himself, he sighs, saying that it's 'for your own good'."
msgstr ""
"塔尔姆打了个响指，你双腿的肌肉顿时失了力，不由自主地跪倒在地，反抗的念头也随之消散。塔尔"
"姆缓缓托起面前的一朵白花，摘下几片花瓣。他的动作郑重而娴熟，仿佛已经做过无数次。他挥挥"
"手，让你也去采些，想采多少就采多少。你正想叫他自己去，他却叹了口气，说这是“为你好”。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The Dreamers... what can they teach me?"
msgstr "入梦者……他们能教我什么？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You thought multiple times about ripping the flowers from the ground as you delicately "
"plucked a few petals from each, but felt like you'd look more like a rebelling child "
"than properly offering any form of legitimate resistance. You move throughout the "
"fields efficiently, taking care not to step on any of the flowers, and return once "
"you've gathered a sizeable number of petals."
msgstr ""
"你小心地从每朵花上摘下几片花瓣，好几次都想干脆把花连根拔起。可那样看起来更像是小孩子闹脾"
"气，根本算不上什么反抗。你利落地穿行在花田间，小心避开脚下的花，采了不少花瓣后才回去。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There. What do you want these for?"
msgstr "喏。你要这些做什么？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I told you. To speak with the Dreamers."
msgstr "我说过了。用来和入梦者交谈。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Take my hand, I'll show you."
msgstr "握住我的手，我教你。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Please?"
msgstr "好吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm raises his hand once again, preparing to snap, but you begrudgingly sigh and take "
"the man's hand. He slowly walks you through the process of... bringing Dreamers forth "
"from the petals. Talm does so in seconds, and a pale, wispy silhouette of a young girl "
"dances forth from one of the petals he took from you. She greets Talm warmly, asking "
"how long it's been for him since the last she awoke. The two go back and forth for a "
"time until the girl notices you, and she excitedly runs through more questions than you "
"can possibly keep up with, all before you even get your name out.\n"
"\n"
"Talm calms her, saying that you're there to learn about the Dreamers, and to tell the "
"others within the Dream to prepare themselves. Her silhouette dissipates a second "
"later.\n"
"\n"
"The man walks you through the process, and you find it very similar to summoning "
"creatures, but a lot harder than anything you've done before. Talm's effortless display "
"earlier clearly came from an untold amount of practice."
msgstr ""
"塔尔姆再次抬手，作势要打响指。你不情愿地叹了口气，握住他的手。他一步步教你如何……从花瓣中"
"唤出入梦者。塔尔姆只花了几秒。从你采来的其中一片花瓣里，一个小女孩的身影轻盈地飘了出来，"
"苍白而缥缈。她亲热地向塔尔姆打招呼，问他距离自己上次醒来，他那边已经过了多久。两人聊了一"
"阵，小女孩才注意到你。你连名字都还没来得及报上，她就兴奋地问了一连串问题，让你根本招架不"
"住。\n"
"\n"
"塔尔姆安抚住她，说你是来了解入梦者的，让她回去通知梦境中的其他人，好做些准备。片刻后，她"
"的身影消散了。\n"
"\n"
"塔尔姆带着你一步步尝试。你发现这与召唤生物十分相似，却比你以往做过的任何召唤都难得多。他"
"刚才做得那么轻松，显然是不知练习了多少次的结果。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#. Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[Exclusive Content Agility] X/X [Exclusive Content Agility]"
msgstr "[Exclusive Content Agility] X/X [Exclusive Content Agility]"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The last petal withers away in your hand, the last Dreamer you spoke with having left "
"to go check on her child somewhere deep within the Dream. You feel... exhausted. You're "
"unsure of just how long passed, as time within Respite doesn't seem to move like it "
"does in the real world. You feel no hunger, no fatigue, but time does seem to pass. At "
"the very least, the sky changes colors, though not in any pattern you were able to "
"notice. It could have been hours, or it could have been months since you started "
"talking to the Dreamers, you simply don't know or have any way of telling.\n"
"\n"
"The Dreamers you spoke with all shared the same initial excitement the first girl had "
"at seeing a stranger, and countless questions about what the world was like. Like Talm "
"had said, it'd seem that he's the only one they've talked to outside of the dream since "
"they first entered. [Companion Name] eventually came out to join some of the "
"conversations, and then once she was shown the process, have her own. Not everyone was "
"from the Lifebinders... dozens of names were given, all in-line with some different "
"discipline or school of thought, all joined the Lifebinders here in Respite to escape.\n"
"\n"
"They told you what Era and Talm couldn't. What they lived through.\n"
"\n"
"The Titan Wars.\n"
"\n"
"That was the calamity they spoke of.\n"
"\n"
"Titans were beasts that dwarved even the Ivory Athenaeum by several magnitudes of size. "
"What the Dreamers described sounded more like forces of nature or vengeful Gods rather "
"than anything a group of people could bring forth. When the Titans of two rival "
"summoning clans fought, it was heard across the continent. Mountains were crushed to "
"dust, a quarter of the mainland was buried under water, lakes of fire rose from the "
"ground and killed thousands... \n"
"\n"
"Clans that did not raise their own Titan for protection were quickly destroyed by those "
"that did. Each clan saw one another as a threat that could generate a world-changing "
"force, and the only way to stay alive was to have your own and use it against the "
"others, or create a plane of existence like Respite and lose the metaphorical key.\n"
"\n"
"Talm approaches quietly as the last Dreamer fades away."
msgstr ""
"最后一片花瓣在你手中枯萎。最后那位与你交谈的入梦者已返回梦境深处，去看望她的孩子。你感"
"到……心力交瘁。你不知道究竟过了多久。安歇之境里的时间，似乎与现实世界不同。你既不饿，身体"
"也不觉得疲倦，可时间显然仍在流逝。至少天空一直在变换颜色，只是你看不出其中有什么规律。从"
"你开始与入梦者交谈到现在，也许过了几小时，也许过了几个月。你无从得知，也无从判断。\n"
"\n"
"与你交谈的每一位入梦者，见到陌生人时都和最初那个小女孩一样兴奋。他们有无数个问题，想知道"
"外面的世界如今是什么模样。正如塔尔姆所说，自从进入梦境，他们似乎就只与他这个外界来客说过"
"话。[Companion Name]后来也出来加入了交谈。学会方法后，她也开始自己唤出入梦者。他们并不全"
"是生命缚誓者。你听到了几十个不同氏族的名字，各自有不同的专长或理念，却都为了逃难，随生命"
"缚誓者一同来到了安歇之境。\n"
"\n"
"他们告诉了你艾拉和塔尔姆无法说出口的事，那些他们亲身经历过的往事。\n"
"\n"
"泰坦战争。\n"
"\n"
"那就是两人口中的灾难。\n"
"\n"
"泰坦是庞大无比的野兽，即使象牙藏书院，在它们面前也渺小得不值一提。听着入梦者的描述，你觉"
"得那些更像是天灾，或是降下怒火的神明，根本不像人力所能召出的东西。两个敌对召唤师氏族的泰"
"坦一旦交战，整片大陆都能听见。山岳被碾成齑粉，四分之一的大陆沉入水下，烈焰从地底涌出，汇"
"成火湖，吞噬了成千上万人的性命……\n"
"\n"
"没有召出自己的泰坦来保护族人的氏族，很快便被那些拥有泰坦的氏族消灭了。在每个氏族眼中，其"
"他氏族都是潜在的威胁，随时可能召出足以改变世界的力量。想活下去，就只能掌握同样的力量，用"
"它对付其他氏族。或者，另辟一个像安歇之境这样的世界，进去后再把“钥匙”扔掉。\n"
"\n"
"最后一位入梦者消散时，塔尔姆悄悄走了过来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#. [待复核] Excel 里该行原文已被破坏，译文按行序对应，请核对
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... I don't know what to say."
msgstr "我……我不知道该说什么。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Assuming this isn't all one horrid trick... that each of these people truly are... "
"somewhere... in this Dream."
msgstr "如果这不是一场可怕的骗局……如果刚才那些人真的都在……梦境里的某个地方……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I know."
msgstr "我明白。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The calamity was so horrid, and the dangers of the outside world so prevalent, my "
"people decided to never face it again."
msgstr "那场灾难太可怕，外面的世界又处处是危险。我的族人决定，再也不去面对这一切。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No living summoner from my time can speak of it, but you know what we faced. We "
"couldn't compete. We wouldn't have wanted to even if we could."
msgstr ""
"与我同时代、如今仍活着的召唤师，都无法谈论那段往事。但现在，你知道我们当年面对的是什么"
"了。我们无力与他们抗衡。就算有那个能力，我们也不愿变成那样。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And so, the Dream was born."
msgstr "于是，梦境诞生了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The book from the Archive is a history book. How Respite came to be and... the Dream we "
"were building towards."
msgstr ""
"你们从藏书院拿到的那本书，是一本史书。它记载了安歇之境的由来，还有……我们想要创造的梦境。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"A world without war. Without death. Without wondering if we'd make it through the next "
"year. That book let kids hold onto hope for a better future."
msgstr ""
"一个没有战争的世界。没有死亡。也不必担心自己能否活到下一年。那本书让孩子们还能盼着一个更"
"好的未来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The city you attacked... they had people that wished for the same, I'm sure."
msgstr "你袭击的那座城里……肯定也有人盼着同样的未来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I know that. Do you think for a moment that I don't know that?"
msgstr "我知道。你真以为我不知道吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There's never a night where my actions don't haunt me."
msgstr "没有一个夜晚，我能摆脱那些往事。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Then how could you do it?"
msgstr "那你怎么还下得了手？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Their souls."
msgstr "他们的灵魂。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I needed a source of power to enact the ritual that let my people enter the Dream."
msgstr "让族人进入梦境的仪式，需要力量来支撑。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Other clans got their power in other ways, but it always came from somewhere."
msgstr "其他氏族有别的办法获取力量，但力量总得有个来源。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A forest clan, the Vieshar, when they brought forth their... you know."
msgstr "有个生活在森林里的氏族，叫维沙尔。他们召出自己的……你知道我说的是什么。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The energy it required caused all of the plant-life across half the continent to wither "
"and die. Millions starved when their plants couldn't grow as the ground was fallow for "
"a decade."
msgstr ""
"那需要的力量，让一半大陆上的植物全部枯萎、死去。土地整整十年寸草不生，庄稼种不出来，数百"
"万人活活饿死。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That doesn't mean-"
msgstr "可这也不代表……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My people gave so much to create Respite, but it wasn't enough. There's a reason we "
"have that beast at the front. We were still pursued by those who sought our power."
msgstr ""
"为了建成安歇之境，我的族人已经付出了太多，可还是不够。我们把那头野兽放在入口，是有原因"
"的。觊觎我们力量的人，仍在穷追不舍。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We tried so hard to be left in peace. My people needed a place where they could never "
"be hurt again."
msgstr "我们费尽心力，只想求个安宁。我的族人需要一个永远不会再受到伤害的地方。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...I killed thousands all those years ago. I will never not feel the weight of what I "
"did."
msgstr "……多年前，我杀了上千人。这份罪孽，我永远也卸不下来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But now, my people, my kids, are safe. So are thousands of others. Each and every "
"single one of these flowers was a person saved through what I did that day."
msgstr ""
"可如今，我的族人，我的孩子，都安全了。还有成千上万的其他人。这里的每一朵花，都是因为我那"
"天所做的事，才得以保全的一条生命。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...I don't expect you to understand. But I do want you to know that what I did was "
"hardly even a footnote in history."
msgstr ""
"……我不指望你能理解。但我想让你知道，我所做的那些事，在那段历史里，甚至都算不上值得一提。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Why did you and Era bring us here, Talm?"
msgstr "塔尔姆，你和艾拉为什么要把我们带到这里？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Go ask Era yourselves. She'll be waiting where you entered. There's nothing more for us "
"to show you."
msgstr "你们自己去问艾拉吧。她会在你们进来的地方等着。我们已经没有别的东西能给你们看了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I mean this sincerely, good luck."
msgstr "祝你们好运。这句话，我是真心的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm takes a shaky breath and waves you and [Companion Name] off, looking back down at "
"the two flowers you first saw him tending to. The two of you look to each other, not "
"even knowing where to begin with everything dropped on you. [Companion Name] brings you "
"to a tower that stretches endlessly into the sky, and once you enter, you realize the "
"circular platform was the one you fought Era and Talm on.\n"
"\n"
"After a ride to the top, the horrid, fleshy hallway you were chased in stretches out in "
"front of you. Only one way out, it'd seem."
msgstr ""
"塔尔姆颤抖着吸了口气，挥手示意你和[Companion Name]离开，又低下头，望着你最初见他照料的那"
"两朵花。你们面面相觑。一下子知道了这么多事，谁也不知道该从何说起。[Companion Name]带你来"
"到一座直入天际的高塔前。走进去后，你才发现，里面那座圆形平台，正是你们与艾拉、塔尔姆交战"
"的地方。\n"
"\n"
"平台载着你们升到顶端。先前被野兽追赶时跑过的那条血肉通道，再次出现在眼前。看来只有这一条"
"出路了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This 'ought to be good!"
msgstr "这下可有得受了！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That's the best I've felt in a while."
msgstr "好久没这么舒坦过了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The fetid hallway offers more resistance than it did before. Arms of twisted, mottled "
"flesh grasp at the pair of you as you run by, narrow passages threaten to crush you as "
"you pass. No beast chases you this time, but the urgency you feel to leave is no lesser "
"for it.\n"
"\n"
"True to Talm's word, Era waits for you by the exit with a sad smile."
msgstr ""
"恶臭的通道比先前更加难以通过。你们奔跑时，一条条由斑驳血肉扭成的手臂伸来抓挠。狭窄的通路"
"不断挤压，仿佛要把你们碾碎。这次没有野兽追在身后，可你们想逃出去的心情丝毫不减。\n"
"\n"
"塔尔姆没有骗你们。艾拉正等在出口，脸上带着一丝伤感的笑。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I saw that you two and Talm talked..."
msgstr "我看见你们和塔尔姆谈过了……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I trust that you're ready to leave?"
msgstr "想必已经准备好离开了吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yes. We learned of... The Titan Wars, and bringing forth the Dreamers was... "
"enlightening when it came to practicing Summoning."
msgstr "是。我们知道了……泰坦战争的事。唤出入梦者，也让我们对召唤术……有了不少领悟。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Though I don't know if I want anything to do with it after... all of this."
msgstr "不过，经历了……这一切，我不知道自己还想不想碰它。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Running from your pet was great for cardio, and when you ran me through with your "
"claws, I learned an important lesson about never trusting summoners again."
msgstr ""
"被你们的宠物追着跑，倒是挺练体力的。至于你那一爪穿胸，也给我上了重要的一课：再也别相信召"
"唤师。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What we don't get is... why. Why all of this? If you fought so hard to bring us here, "
"why are you just... letting us go?"
msgstr ""
"可我们还是不明白……为什么？为什么要做这些？你们费这么大力气把我们弄到这里，现在却又……放我"
"们走？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "To prepare you."
msgstr "为了让你们做好准备。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I've seen what you two must face as you continue to face off against the Soulsmiths."
msgstr "我已经看见了，你们继续与炼魂师对抗，将会面对什么。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"What was... described to you by the Dreamers is nothing compared to what the "
"Fateseekers saw all those years ago, at the end of the calamity."
msgstr ""
"多年前，寻命者曾预见那场灾难最终的结局。与那个结局相比，入梦者向你们……讲述的那些，根本不"
"算什么。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Going off of what Talm was saying..."
msgstr "照塔尔姆的说法……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Bringing forth a Titan comes at an enormous cost to the world, but it wouldn't outright "
"end it. "
msgstr "召出一头泰坦，会让世界付出极其惨重的代价，却不会直接毁掉整个世界。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is true... if the Soulsmiths intended to stop there."
msgstr "没错……前提是炼魂师愿意就此收手。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They will go further than any clan of my time ever could, as there are none who can "
"keep them in check."
msgstr "他们会比我那个时代的任何氏族都走得更远，因为已经没有人能制衡他们。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The calamity my people lived through shaped the world into what it is today. Despite "
"the devastation, there was a delicate balance between the clans."
msgstr ""
"我的族人经历的那场灾难，将世界变成了如今的模样。尽管破坏如此惨烈，当时的氏族之间仍维持着"
"微妙的平衡。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Each had clan a... the same level of power. After decades of war, the world was nearly "
"uninhabitable."
msgstr "每个氏族都有……相当的力量。几十年战乱之后，世界已几乎无法生存。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "To prevent their own extinction, those that remained released their..."
msgstr "为了不让自己也走向灭亡，幸存的氏族将各自的……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Titans..."
msgstr "泰坦……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yes. Back to the world. Plants grew again. The winds blew through the trees. Rain fell "
"anew. The world began to heal with its natural power restored."
msgstr ""
"是。将它们释放，让力量回归天地。于是草木重新生长。风再次吹过林间。雨水重新落下。自然的力"
"量得以归还，世界也开始慢慢恢复。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...But what does this have to do with us?"
msgstr "……可这跟我们有什么关系？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] and I... We came to the capitol chasing after ghosts, wanting to know "
"why our home was burnt to the ground by the Soulsmiths. To make them pay, and return "
"our people if they still lived."
msgstr ""
"我和[Companion Name]……我们来到都城，追查那些渺茫的线索，只想知道炼魂师为什么要把我们的家"
"烧成废墟。让他们付出代价。如果我们的乡亲还活着，就把他们带回来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Why did you and Talm test us? To what end?"
msgstr "你和塔尔姆为什么要考验我们？目的是什么？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your people will be used as fuel for the Soulsmith's beast. Like thousands... no... "
"millions, of others will be."
msgstr ""
"你们的乡亲，会成为炼魂师孕育那头野兽的养料。还有成千上万……不，数以百万计的人，也会遭遇同"
"样的命运。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The two of you are the first new summoners to learn the art within centuries, outside "
"of the Soulsmiths themselves."
msgstr "几百年来，除炼魂师之外，你们是最早学会召唤术的两个新人。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"How and why could we ever hope to stop them? Why does this fall on us, and not you and "
"Talm?"
msgstr "可就凭我们，怎么可能阻止他们？为什么这事要落在我们头上，而不是你和塔尔姆？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Talm and I have been around for centuries, child."
msgstr "孩子，我和塔尔姆已经活了几百年。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"In the few years the two of you have existed on this world in comparison, you've "
"already long-since exceeded our potential."
msgstr "相比之下，你们来到这世上才短短几年，却早已展现出远超我们的潜力。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I will never expect you to understand or forgive our appearent betrayal, but I promise "
"you..."
msgstr "我不指望你们理解或原谅我们这番近乎背叛的所作所为。但我向你们保证……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This was the fastest, most effective way we could see to help you continue to surpass "
"us."
msgstr "这是我们能想到的最快、最有效的办法，能让你们继续成长，超越我们。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...We didn't ask for this."
msgstr "……可我们根本没想过要承担这些。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I wish with all my heart that this was not your burden to bare."
msgstr "我也打心底里希望，这副重担不必落在你们肩上。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But the world is unkind to us all, some more than others."
msgstr "可这世道不肯善待任何人，有些人受的苦还要更多。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...What if we just... stopped? What then? Went back to Azamire, settled down, and never "
"thought about any of this ever again?"
msgstr "……如果我们就此……收手呢？然后呢？回阿扎米尔，安安稳稳地过日子，再也不去想这些事？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Could you, knowing that there's even a sliver of a chance I'm correct?"
msgstr "只要我说的还有一丝可能是真的，你们真能放得下吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Where would we even begin, without you and Talm?"
msgstr "……可没有你和塔尔姆帮忙，我们又该从哪儿着手？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Far to the west are the Perilous Peaks, as I'm sure you know. Deep within, the Nalidasi "
"Dwarves maintain archives that far predate even the oldest human civilizations."
msgstr ""
"你们应该知道，遥远的西方有一片险恶山脉。山脉深处，纳里达西矮人保存着古老的文献。最早的人"
"类文明出现时，那些文献就已存在。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...That's where I would start."
msgstr "……换作是我，就先去那里找线索。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"For what it's worth, I'm sorry that this what Talm and I could offer you. I wish we had "
"more time to do this the right way."
msgstr ""
"不管这声道歉还有没有用，我都很抱歉。我和塔尔姆只能用这样的方式帮你们。要是时间再充裕些，"
"我们就能用更妥当的办法了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] seems like she may have more to say, but turns a second later and "
"reaches upward. The moment her hand touches the still, reflected pool of water that "
"brought you into Respite, she bolts upward and out of the plane. You look to Era for "
"only a moment before following after her.\n"
"\n"
"The trek back to the mainland is much calmer than the one here, especially now with "
"experience. You and [Companion Name] hardly share a word the entire trip back.\n"
"\n"
"You sail further south than Tidebreak, heading back towards the capitol, unsure of what "
"to do or where to go. Both of you go through the motions as you arrive at port, "
"register your vessel, and pay for it to remain docked for some time. Checking with "
"locals and accounting for travel to and from Gloomstone, it'd seem you were only in "
"Respite for an hour, but you know it was much longer than that, and you guess that time "
"moves differently there.\n"
"\n"
"You wander the streets for a while before [Companion Name] suggests a nearby tavern. "
"The two of you share a room, feeling a bit too unsteady to be apart for now. You don't "
"even know where to begin, and your best friend seems to feel similarly, until she "
"tosses your weapon to you. She's determined not to let anyone get the best of her "
"again, and wants to spar. You smile for the first time in a while."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name]似乎还想说什么，但片刻后，她转过身，向上伸出手。她的手刚碰到那片带你们进"
"入安歇之境、如倒影般悬在上方的平静池水，整个人便倏地向上冲去，离开了这片天地。你只看了艾"
"拉一眼，便跟了上去。\n"
"\n"
"返回大陆的航程比来时平静得多，有了先前的经验，这一路也顺利了不少。整个返程途中，你和"
"[Companion Name]几乎一句话也没说。\n"
"\n"
"你们没有停在破浪镇，而是继续向南，朝都城驶去。至于接下来该做什么、该去哪里，你们心里都没"
"有答案。抵港、登记船只、交钱让船停泊一阵子，你们心不在焉地办完了这些事。向当地人打听过时"
"间，再扣除往返幽暗之石的航程，你们算出自己似乎只在安歇之境待了一个小时。可你知道，自己在"
"那里度过的时间远不止这些。想来，那里的时间与外界流逝得并不一样。\n"
"\n"
"你们在街上漫无目的地走了一阵，[Companion Name]提议去附近一家酒馆。你们要了一间房。这会儿"
"两人都还有些心神不定，不愿分开。你满腹心事，却不知从何说起。你最好的朋友似乎也一样，直到"
"她把你的武器抛给了你。她不愿再输给任何人，想和你切磋切磋。你终于露出了久违的笑容。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your time in Respite left you shaken and unsure of yourself. You definitely grew in the "
"untold amount of time you stayed there, but if you were to follow the path laid out for "
"you, is there any amount of growth that'd prepare you for what's to come? These "
"thoughts come and go as you clash with [Companion Name]. As the two of you duel into "
"the night, doubtlessly disturbing the other guests, you slowly let your time in Respite "
"wash away from your mind.\n"
"\n"
"Whatever tomorrow brings will be tomorrow's problem. For now, [Companion Name] is safe, "
"alive, and so are you.\n"
"\n"
"And for now, that's enough."
msgstr ""
"安歇之境的经历让你心有余悸，也让你对自己生出了怀疑。你不知道在那里究竟待了多久，但自己的"
"确长进了不少。可若真要沿着他们指明的路走下去，无论变得多强，就真能应付接下来的一切吗？你"
"一边与[Companion Name]过招，一边胡思乱想。你们一直切磋到深夜，想必没少打扰其他住客。而安"
"歇之境的那些经历，也渐渐被你抛到了脑后。\n"
"\n"
"明天会怎样，就留到明天再操心吧。至少此刻，[Companion Name]还好好地活着，平安无事。你也一"
"样。\n"
"\n"
"这就够了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ20"
msgstr "MQ20"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Path to the Peaks - The next leg of your journey has been laid out before you. The "
"Perilous Peaks lay far to the north, the surrounding lands mostly untouched by "
"civilization, but with no better leads, it remains your best path forward."
msgstr ""
"通往群峰之路——下一段旅程的方向已经明确。险恶山脉远在北方，周围大多是人迹罕至的荒野。不"
"过，既然没有更好的线索，眼下还是去那里最有希望。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I've got first watch, I suppose."
msgstr "看来今晚得我先守夜了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Something's out there!"
msgstr "外面有东西！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Stocked up on provisions and as mentally prepared as you can be, you and [Companion "
"Name], set off, leaving the capitol far behind. Things remain in this strange state "
"of... flux, where the both of you try your best to pretend the weight of everything "
"that happened in Respite hasn't been weighing on your shoulders.\n"
"\n"
"As you sit by this night's campfire, several days into your journey now, [Companion "
"Name] drives her hatchet into a log she was splitting for kindling and turns to face "
"you."
msgstr ""
"备足补给，也尽可能做好心理准备后，你和[Companion Name]踏上旅途，将都城远远甩在身后。你们"
"之间始终有种说不清的……别扭。两人都竭力装作若无其事，仿佛安歇之境里发生的一切，并没有一直"
"压在心头。\n"
"\n"
"出发几天后的一晚，你坐在篝火旁。[Companion Name]正在劈柴，准备引火。她忽然把手斧往木头上"
"一嵌，转过身来看着你。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I loathe this, [Player Name]."
msgstr "我受够了，[Player Name]。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't mind splitting the wood tonight, just give me a sec-"
msgstr "今晚我来劈也行，等我一下……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You know that's not what I mean."
msgstr "你知道我说的不是这个。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This whole... funk. It's like we both died a little in Respite and have been little "
"walking corpses ever since."
msgstr ""
"我是说……咱们现在这副样子。就像在安歇之境丢了半条魂，出来以后，一直活得像行尸走肉。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I haven't been me, and you... haven't been you."
msgstr "我不像我，你也……不像你了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I know."
msgstr "……我知道。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't know... how we're meant to act, now."
msgstr "我不知道……现在该怎么办才好。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I feel so deep in over my head. We came out here to find a couple people from Azamire "
"and now we're..."
msgstr ""
"这些事，已经远远超出我能应付的范围了。咱们出来，只是想找到几个阿扎米尔的乡亲，结果现在"
"却……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What, heading to the home of the Dwarves to learn about Summoning? To what end?"
msgstr "怎么就要去矮人的地盘，打听召唤术的事了？目的是什么？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I always knew that you'd leave Azamire and do something great, but me?"
msgstr "我一直知道，你迟早会离开阿扎米尔，干出一番大事。可我呢？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You've gone through everything I have, and I'd argue more. "
msgstr "我经历过的事，你一样都没落下。真要说起来，你经历的还更多。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I have no idea if what Era says is true. I truly hope it isn't."
msgstr "我不知道艾拉说的是不是真的。说实话，我希望不是。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But... Despite how stupid their little test was, and how much I wish they would have "
"just been honest from the get go..."
msgstr "但……他们那场考验再怎么荒唐，我再怎么希望他们一开始就把话说清楚……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Era is right, at least about needing to help. I've seen too much to just... go back "
"home."
msgstr "至少有一点艾拉没说错，我们得帮忙。见过这么多事，我没法就这样……回家。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I mean, how could we? I feel that our days back in Azamire, even before the attack, are "
"so far behind us."
msgstr ""
"咱们怎么可能做得到呢？我总觉得，在阿扎米尔的日子，连同遇袭前的一切，都已经离咱们很远了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just... don't know where we belong anymore."
msgstr "我只是……不知道哪里才是咱们的归处了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Believe me, I'm in the same boat..."
msgstr "相信我，我也一样……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't want to lose ourselves while we figure out where that is."
msgstr "可在找到那个地方之前，我不想咱们先把自己弄丢了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You leave it there as [Companion Name] sits beside you on your log-turned-seat and "
"rests her head on your shoulder. You feel... lighter, and only hope that you find your "
"place in all this mess. You shift a bit, getting ready to stand before you hear "
"[Companion Name] start to snore."
msgstr ""
"你们没再说下去。[Companion Name]在你身旁的木头上坐下，把头靠在你肩上。你心里……轻松了些。"
"只盼在这一团乱麻之中，终究能找到属于自己的位置。你挪了挪身子，正准备站起来，却听见"
"[Companion Name]打起了呼噜。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It looks like a whole pack has come out to greet us."
msgstr "看来是一整群来迎接咱们了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're gonna have to move camp."
msgstr "这营地是待不下去了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your mind wasn't playing tricks on you. The small snap of a branch here, something "
"disturbing the underbrush there. It's always difficult to differentiate between the "
"general comings and goings of creatures in the night, and when something is actively "
"stalking you.\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, this is the later. You bolt upright and draw your weapon, waking "
"[Companion Name] in the process as a particularly large Rockwolf charges right for you."
msgstr ""
"先前那些动静，并不是你的错觉。一会儿是树枝轻轻折断的脆响，一会儿又是灌木丛里的窸窣声。夜"
"里的野兽四处走动，和有什么东西正在悄悄跟踪你，往往很难分清。\n"
"\n"
"不幸的是，这次是后者。一头格外庞大的石狼径直扑来。你猛地起身，拔出武器，也惊醒了"
"[Companion Name]。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ughhh, what... are you doing?"
msgstr "唔……你……干什么呢？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[Companion Name] wake up!"
msgstr "[Companion Name]，快醒醒！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Dinner came to us tonight, it looks like."
msgstr "看来今晚的晚饭自己送上门了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Seeing you prepared for it, the beast diverts its charge and instead runs past you, and "
"darting back into the woods, outside of the light of your campfire.\n"
"\n"
"Just outside of the clearing you can see the firelight reflect off of eyes. Lots of "
"eyes."
msgstr ""
"见你已有防备，那野兽猛地转向，从你身边掠过，又窜回篝火照不到的树林里。空地边缘，一双双眼"
"睛映着火光。多得惊人。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This is some of the toughest meat I've worked with..."
msgstr "这肉可真够韧的，我还没处理过几次这么难下刀的……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This smells and looks way better than expected."
msgstr "这卖相，这香味，可比想象中好多了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Huffing and puffing the cool night air, you hold your weapon aloft, challenging more of "
"the beasts to come out. Far fewer of the pack remain, and those that do decide that "
"they've bitten off more than they can chew once the biggest of them lies dead at your "
"feet and dart off into the trees, but not before one grabs your pack of provisions out "
"of the tree it was hung up in. No one had said anything about wolves about the size of "
"horses, so you didn't think to hang your food that high."
msgstr ""
"你大口喘着气，吸入夜间的凉意，同时高举武器，等着还有哪头野兽敢上前。狼群已所剩无几。见最"
"大的那头倒在你脚下，剩下的终于知道惹错了对手，纷纷逃进树林。可临走前，还是有一头叼走了你"
"挂在树上的补给袋。又没人告诉过你，这里的狼能长得跟马一样大，你自然没想到要把食物挂得那么"
"高。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well... good morning, [Companion Name]."
msgstr "呃……早啊，[Companion Name]。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You know how I always told you I wanted a dog?"
msgstr "还记得我总说想养条狗吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I might get a cat instead."
msgstr "我看还是养猫吧。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Don't bring that evil on us, I know there's some scary kitties up in the Peaks."
msgstr "可别招这种祸，我听说山里有些猫也吓人得很。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Knowing our luck, we'd wake up with one nibbling one of our arms."
msgstr "就咱们这运气，说不定一觉醒来，它正抱着咱们的胳膊啃呢。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A girl can dream."
msgstr "想想总行吧。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wolves took our food, didn't they?"
msgstr "那些狼把咱们的吃的叼走了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If they just wanted that, they could have grabbed it and been gone without trying to go "
"for our throats."
msgstr "要是只冲着吃的来，拿了就走不就行了，何必非咬断咱们的脖子？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think they just took it as a consolation prize."
msgstr "我看是没吃着咱们，顺手拿点东西安慰一下自己。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They'll need some consoling after eating it. Hardtack and some... absolutely foul "
"pemmican isn't exactly the height of camping food."
msgstr ""
"等吃过袋子里的东西，它们才真需要安慰。硬饼干，还有那股味儿……难以下咽的油脂肉干，实在算不"
"上什么野餐美味。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, we do still have to eat something. Nothing stopping us from having them, right?"
msgstr "不过，咱们总得吃点东西。吃它们也没什么不行吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gotta do something with the bodies."
msgstr "这些尸体总得处理。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I've never had wolf before, but they have to be stringy right?"
msgstr "我还没吃过狼肉，不过肯定又老又柴吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And I don't know how keen I am on eating something that has maybe eaten a person before."
msgstr "而且，万一它们吃过人，我可有点下不去嘴。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's a rare day someone comes this far north, I'd say the odds they've eaten someone "
"are low."
msgstr "平时哪有人跑到这么北边来。要我说，它们吃过人的可能性不大。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "That doesn't sound like zero."
msgstr "可也不是完全没有。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But well, when in Emor."
msgstr "不过嘛，入乡随俗呗。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Where's that?"
msgstr "……随哪门子的俗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Dunno. Something I heard people in the capitol saying."
msgstr "……不知道。听都城的人这么说的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You get some rest, I'll work on getting all these bodies prepared."
msgstr "你歇会儿吧，我来处理这些尸体。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Surely nothing will get attracted by all the corpses."
msgstr "这么多尸体堆着，肯定不会招来什么东西吧。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Surely."
msgstr "肯定不会。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll feed you to them first, if you just jinxed us."
msgstr "你要是真把什么招来了，我就先把你喂给它们。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I will never expect you to understand or forgive our apparent betrayal, but I promise "
"you..."
msgstr "我不指望你们理解或原谅我们这番近乎背叛的所作所为。但我向你们保证……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's almost like they don't want people coming up here!"
msgstr "他们这是压根不想让人上来吧！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Surely they'll be glad to see us."
msgstr "见到咱们，他们肯定高兴。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The magic-enhanced tools you picked up back in the capitol help you make quick work of "
"the pile, at least compared to what it'd usually take you. [Companion Name] takes the "
"freshly cooked steaks as you finish with them and gives them a bit of extra love and "
"seasoning once you're done. With fresh food and better spirits, you pack up camp and "
"head further towards the peaks.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you nibble smoked strips of rockwolf as you walk. It's very crunchy."
msgstr ""
"你在都城买的那些附魔工具派上了用场，处理起这堆狼尸，比平时快了不少。你每煎好一块肉，"
"[Companion Name]便接过去，再添些调料，细细料理一番。有了新鲜食物，心情也好了些。你们收拾"
"营地，继续朝山脉进发。\n"
"\n"
"你们边走边嚼着熏好的石狼肉条。咬起来嘎嘣脆。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wow, this is... really good!"
msgstr "哇，这……还真好吃！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think every meal is made a little better if it tried to eat you first."
msgstr "我觉得，想吃你的东西，吃起来就是格外香。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I mean, really, it's only fair when you think about it. Spite tastes good."
msgstr "你想啊，它想吃咱们，咱们吃它，谁也不亏。解气，还解馋。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Though, these herbs you found definitely help. "
msgstr "不过，你找到的这些香草也功不可没。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The forest provides. Makes me wonder what other kinds of creatures taste like."
msgstr "林子里好东西可不少。说得我都想尝尝别的怪物是什么味儿了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I really liked that Stonehopper back in the Broken Pass, too."
msgstr "之前在破碎关口吃的石跳兽，我也挺喜欢的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, both these and the wolves are pretty much just bigger, scarier versions of "
"creatures we already know."
msgstr "嗯，石跳兽也好，石狼也好，其实都是咱们熟悉的动物长大、变凶了些。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I didn't expect to like the wolf this much, but what about some weird stuff?"
msgstr "我倒没想到狼肉这么好吃。那要是再古怪一点的呢？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Like... Slimes?"
msgstr "比如……史莱姆？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ooo, that's interesting. Maybe they'd be like some kind of... gelatin?"
msgstr "哦，这倒有意思。说不定吃起来像……某种果冻？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I hope so."
msgstr "……但愿吧。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If we run out of food, maybe we go check out a dungeon and see what kind of creatures "
"we can find?"
msgstr "等食物吃完了，要不要找个地牢逛逛，看看里面有什么怪物？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Might be delicious, might poison us and we die horribly."
msgstr "没准是美味，也没准有毒，吃完就死得惨兮兮的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm down."
msgstr "我看行。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you travel onward, the dense forest gives way to rocky slopes. Little by little you "
"find yourselves walking less and scrambling more, until the journey has turned into an "
"outright climb. The entrance to the Dwarves' home is not one they wanted visitors to "
"get to easily, it'd seem."
msgstr ""
"继续前行，茂密的森林渐渐被岩石遍布的山坡取代。脚下的路越来越难走，你们不得不手脚并用，到"
"后来，干脆一路都在往上爬。看来，矮人并不想让访客轻轻松松就找到家门。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You and [Companion Name] take turns lugging your gear up the mountainside. You're sure "
"you were told the entrance to the dwarven capitol was somewhere around here, but "
"\"lower eastern side of those mountains over there\" weren't exactly prime directions "
"from a group of what seemed to be well-meaning schoolkids. They said the entrance was "
"hidden, and that those seeking the dwarves would likely have to climb for days or "
"weeks, to find the entrance. Nevertheless, blissfully far from the peak but still not "
"easy to access, a large gate carved into the stone stands before you, presumably "
"leading deeper into the mountain. On a low wall flanking either side of the gate, a "
"squat dwarf with a short-trimmed blond beard naps soundly, resting his chin on the "
"pommel of his large maul in what appears to be a heavily practiced position.\n"
"\n"
"You clear your throat a couple of times, trying to get his attention, but to no avail. "
"So, you walk up and his helmet with your knuckle, just barely able to reach him atop "
"the wall. He wakes with a shout, wide-eyed and startled by your presence, so much so "
"that he careens backward off the wall. You quickly scramble after him and find the "
"dwarf unconscious - but breathing - on the other side.\n"
"\n"
"You don't know how you're going to explain this to the rest of the dwarves."
msgstr ""
"你和[Companion Name]轮流背着装备，沿山坡往上攀爬。你记得有人说过，矮人都城的入口就在这附"
"近。给你们指路的是一群学生，看着倒是热心，可一句“就在那边几座山的东侧，靠山脚的地方”，实"
"在让人摸不着头脑。他们说入口藏得很隐蔽，想找到矮人，多半得在山里爬上几天，甚至几个星期。"
"好在，虽然这地方也不好找，却远不用爬到山顶。一扇凿在岩壁上的大门终于出现在你们面前，门后"
"想必通往山体深处。大门两旁各有一段矮墙。其中一段墙上，一个矮墩墩的矮人正睡得香甜。他留着"
"修剪整齐的金色短胡须，下巴搁在大槌的柄端上。这姿势，看着就知道不是头一回了。\n"
"\n"
"你清了几次嗓子，想引起他的注意，可他毫无反应。于是，你走近矮墙，勉强伸手够到他的头盔，用"
"指节敲了敲。他惊叫着醒来，瞪大眼睛看着你，吓得往后一仰，直接从墙上翻了下去。你赶紧翻过去"
"查看，发现矮人已经昏了，好在还有呼吸。\n"
"\n"
"这下，你可不知道该怎么向其他矮人解释了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ21"
msgstr "MQ21"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Dwarf Blood - With the sole Nalidasi guard unconscious at your feet and a gate blocking "
"your path, you're going to have some explaining to do."
msgstr ""
"矮人之血——唯一的纳里达西守卫昏倒在你脚边，大门又挡住了去路。这下，你可得好好解释一番了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It it a pull door..?"
msgstr "这门是往外拉的……？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ah! A push door! Oh... wait, no."
msgstr "啊！原来是往里推！哦……等等，也不对。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You quickly look around as [Companion Name] scrambles up the low wall after you. She "
"lightly thumps your back once she stands beside you, then bends down to check the dwarf."
msgstr ""
"你赶紧环顾四周，[Companion Name]也跟着你翻过矮墙。她在你身旁站稳，轻轻拍了一下你的背，随"
"后俯身查看矮人的情况。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They should consider making you an ambassador, truly remarkable work [Player Name]."
msgstr "真该派你来当大使。干得漂亮啊，[Player Name]。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "He was sleeping, I just wanted to wake him up!"
msgstr "他睡着了，我只是想叫醒他！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Just giving you a hard time."
msgstr "逗你呢。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Unfortunately - intentions aside - it looks like you've had a bit of the opposite "
"effect."
msgstr "不过，不管你本来想干什么……现在看来，好像适得其反了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I guess we'll have to let ourselves in, and then find some way of explaining... this."
msgstr "看来咱们只能自己进去了，再想办法解释……这件事。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You look over the gate and wall and just barely spot it. A small stone hatch, likely "
"more typically used as an entrance so they don't have to open and close the main gate "
"all the time. Though, with a path like the one you travelled, it's a wonder they made "
"such a gate in the first place.\n"
"\n"
"As expected the hatch is shut and locked, with no apparent keyhole or method of "
"opening. You get to work trying to open it regardless while [Companion Name] wraps the "
"dwarf's head."
msgstr ""
"你仔细打量大门和围墙，好不容易才发现一处不起眼的地方。那里有一扇小石门，平日里大概都从这"
"里进出，省得总要开关大门。不过，来时的路难走成那样，你倒很好奇，他们当初为什么还要造这么"
"大一扇门。\n"
"\n"
"不出所料，小石门关得严严实实，已经锁上了。门上既看不到钥匙孔，也找不到开门的机关。你还是"
"动手试着开门，[Companion Name]替矮人包扎头部。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Let's see what this dwarf has got!"
msgstr "来，让我见识见识这位矮人的本事！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not bad, not bad."
msgstr "不错，不错。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You try half a dozen methods of opening the hatch until you realize that it's magically "
"imbued. While there are methods for figuring out the words for opening magic locks, you "
"hardly feel you have the time to do so. Eventually you give up on any gentle method of "
"opening and just jam your tools through the side and start to pry while saying every "
"version of 'open' you can think of.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually, it gives way, and you're not sure about what worked specifically, but it "
"hardly matters. You peer down the hatch to find a squat tunnel. You grab the "
"unconscious dwarf and throw him over your shoulder, then head down the tunnel with "
"[Companion] just behind you.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually the tunnel opens up into a small chamber with two dwarves cheerfully playing "
"some form of dice game. The two look at you with shock, the shorter of the two runs for "
"the door leading out and latches it - keeping you from progressing further - while the "
"one who is more stout hefts a large blade in your direction and frowns."
msgstr ""
"你试了五六种办法，才意识到这扇小门施过魔法。虽说有办法找出开启魔法锁的口令，可眼下实在没"
"那个工夫。最后，你放弃了温柔的办法，直接把工具塞进门缝，动手硬撬，嘴里还把能想到的各种"
"“开门”口令念了个遍。\n"
"\n"
"门总算开了。究竟是哪一招起了作用，你也说不清，不过这会儿已经不重要了。你朝门内探头望去，"
"下面是一条低矮的通道。你把昏迷的矮人扛上肩，沿通道往下走，[Companion]紧随其后。\n"
"\n"
"走了一段，通道通向一间小屋。里面有两个矮人，正兴高采烈地玩着某种骰子游戏。两人惊愕地看着"
"你。个子较矮的那个冲到另一扇门前，插上门闩，堵住了去路；更壮实的那个则皱起眉，举起大刀对"
"准你。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oi! What are you doin' with Humphrey?"
msgstr "喂！你们把汉弗莱怎么了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Attackers! Thought you'd pull a fast one on us, eh?"
msgstr "有入侵者！想打我们个措手不及，是吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "No, no! Easy now, I'm not here to hurt anyone."
msgstr "不，不是！别冲动，我不想伤害任何人。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Little late for that, don't ya think?"
msgstr "这话说得有点晚了吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I-"
msgstr "我……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Your friend was so startled by seeing two humans pop up over the cliff that he fell off "
"the wall he was sitting on."
msgstr "你们的朋友看见两个大活人突然从崖边冒出来，吓了一跳，从坐着的墙上摔下去了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Ah."
msgstr "……哦。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Yeah, that sounds like our Humphrey. Thanks for haulin' him down here"
msgstr "嗯，这确实像汉弗莱干得出来的事。多谢你们把他背下来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So, are we okay?"
msgstr "那……没事了吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Suppose so. I'm Tee, human. Short one over there is Pout."
msgstr "应该没事了。人类，我叫提。那边那个矮点的叫波特。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What're your names?"
msgstr "你们叫什么？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's a pleasure, sorry we gave you and your friend quite the start."
msgstr "很高兴认识你们。抱歉，把你们和你们的朋友都吓了一跳。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Meh, it's good to get the heart racing every once in a while."
msgstr "嗐，偶尔受点惊吓，心跳快些也挺好。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Gotta ask ya though, why'd you come up through our expedition entrance?"
msgstr "不过得问一句，你们怎么从我们的探险通道进来了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...is there a different entrance?"
msgstr "……还有别的入口？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh yeah, just another stone's throw north. Got it all freshly paved n' everything."
msgstr "当然有，再往北一点就是。路都刚铺好，别提多平整了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's real nice, you shoulda gone there. We don't get visitors often, especially not "
"humans."
msgstr "那边可好走了，你们该从那儿来的。我们这儿不常有访客，人类就更少了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This one is for our... well, don't know if we can share that. But suffice to say, it's "
"mainly an exit. "
msgstr "这条通道是给我们的……嗯，这个好像不能随便说。总之，主要是用来出去的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Honestly surprised you even found it, let alone climbed up here!"
msgstr "你们居然找到了这里，还一路爬上来了，真够厉害的！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll buy ya a drink later if we see ya, wanna hear about that climb!"
msgstr "回头碰上了，请你们喝一杯，好好讲讲是怎么爬上来的！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm going to find those kids when we get back to the capitol."
msgstr "等回了都城，我非找那几个孩子算账不可。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well! It's a pleasure to meet you both. Shall we leave Humphry with you, then?"
msgstr "好了！很高兴认识二位。那汉弗莱就交给你们了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...Well, we'll bring ya to the capitol, but we need to go ask around first. I think the "
"two of you are the first human visitors we've had in a few years at least!"
msgstr "……嗯，我们会带你们去都城，不过得先去问问。你们恐怕是这几年头一回来的人类访客了！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Tee nods at the statement and unlatches the door and heads out to whether it may lead. "
"Pout fishes around in a pouch on his waist and withdraws a flask and wafts it under "
"Humphrey's nose, who groggily comes to. He takes the flask and takes a sip, instantly "
"regaining his ruddy complexion. As he looks around in a daze, he blushes, embarrassed "
"by the whole endeavor.\n"
"\n"
"As the four of you wait, Humphrey asks if you'd give him a chance to regain a bit of "
"his pride with a little bout."
msgstr ""
"提点点头，拔开门闩走了出去，也不知道是去哪里。波特在腰间的小袋里摸索一番，掏出一个酒壶，"
"放到汉弗莱鼻子下面晃了晃。汉弗莱迷迷糊糊地醒了过来。他接过酒壶喝了一口，脸上立刻恢复了红"
"润。他茫然地看看四周，随即想起刚才的窘事，立刻涨红了脸。\n"
"\n"
"你们四个等候时，汉弗莱问你愿不愿意陪他过两招，让他挽回点面子。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Don't have much of a choice now, do we?"
msgstr "看来也由不得咱们了，是吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Even the king?!"
msgstr "……连国王也来？！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Every time you knock the dwarf down, he sips a bit from the flask again and gets right "
"back up, ready to go again. He's a good fighter, and though you are better, it feels "
"like you are fighting a small platoon one-by-one. [Companion Name] steps in a few times "
"as well, either looking to give you a break or flex her own skills.\n"
"\n"
"Despite the fact that the chamber is well-lit and Pout dragged all the furniture out of "
"the way, the low ceilings make for a cramped fighting place for the two of you, and you "
"have to spend a lot of mental energy to not bash your head or weapons on the ceiling "
"while dodging the dwarf's blows.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually Tee re-enters the room with another dwarf alongside him. The newcomer has a "
"bushy white beard that nearly trails down to the floor, and sits atop a floating disk "
"of metal, lit by intricate patterns of runes and glowing engravings all throughout its "
"surface. You hardly have the time to inspect it before the newcomer clears his throat."
msgstr ""
"每次被你打倒，矮人便喝一小口酒，立刻又爬起来，准备再战。他身手不错，虽然还不是你的对手，"
"可一场接一场打下来，你简直像是轮番打了一小队人。[Companion Name]也上场接了几回，或许是想"
"让你歇口气，或许只是想活动活动筋骨。\n"
"\n"
"屋里光线充足，波特也把家具全拖到了一边，可对你们来说，屋顶还是太低，打起来束手束脚。你既"
"得躲开矮人的攻击，又得时刻留神，别让脑袋或武器撞上天花板。\n"
"\n"
"过了一阵，提带着另一个矮人回来了。来者蓄着浓密的白胡子，几乎垂到地上。他坐在一块悬空的金"
"属圆盘上，圆盘表面布满繁复的符文和雕纹，流光闪烁。你还没来得及细看，他便清了清嗓子。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"*Ahem*. Greetings, tall-folk. I am the grand Archivist and royal advisor to the king."
msgstr "*呃哼*。你们好，高个子们。我是首席典藏官，也是国王的御前顾问。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I bring tidings from our 37th ruler, Oyadazminis, who welcomes you into our home to "
"look upon our works, cherish our history, and hopefully... and I quote, \"drink until "
"you hit the floor.\""
msgstr ""
"我奉我国第三十七任君主奥亚达兹米尼斯之命，欢迎二位来到我们的国度，欣赏我们的造物，领略我"
"们的历史，并希望你们……以下是国王的原话：“喝到趴下为止。”"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If you have any other desires or aspirations while visiting Koganusan, they may be "
"granted, should we deem you worthy of such requests."
msgstr "二位在科加努桑若还有其他愿望或诉求，只要我们认为你们有此资格，也可酌情满足。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"This may be too lofty of an ask - please forgive our trespasses if so - but we hear the "
"Nalidasi Archives are quite the sight to behold."
msgstr "接下来的请求或许有些冒昧，还请见谅。我们听说，纳里达西典藏馆非常值得一看。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...is that so? I can count the number of times a human has been allowed into our "
"archives on one hand since Koganusan was just a hole in the dirt."
msgstr ""
"……是吗？从科加努桑还只是地上一个洞的时候算起，允许进入典藏馆的人类，一只手就数得过来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "So, forgive me if I think you're full of silt."
msgstr "所以，恕我直言，我觉得你们在胡扯。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...They've almost doubtlessly changed their names through the years, but do Era and "
"Talm ring a bell?"
msgstr "……过了这么多年，他们多半换过名字。不过，艾拉和塔尔姆，这两个名字您听过吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not even remotely."
msgstr "从来没有。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What about two ageless Sum-"
msgstr "那，两个长生不老的召……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As the word starts to leave your mouth, the Archivist's eyes go wide and he snaps his "
"fingers, and you find the words silent as they leave your mouth. He chuckles and bids "
"the guards farewell, then snaps again. You find yourselves in front of a grand throne "
"that's equal parts imposing and gaudy. In it sits a dwarf you'd guess is middle aged, "
"with a dark beard studded with gemstones and clasps of metal, similar to the crown atop "
"his head.\n"
"\n"
"You've been brought into what would seem to be a lavish banquet as table after table of "
"divine looking food and immaculately dressed dwarves fill the throne room.\n"
"\n"
"The guests look at your studden entrance with curiosity and excitement, which you "
"consider to be better than suspicion and fear. The Archivist floats up to the king and "
"whispers in his ear, and his eyes go from interest, to shock, and then... excitement. "
"He claps his hands once and hands before the room, then announces to everyone that the "
"entertainment has arrived.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you are ushered into the center of the room, then, one by one, several of "
"the more rugged nobles in the room, along with their guards, encircle you.\n"
"\n"
"The king announces that you're not to be killed, only to be given a proper welcome to "
"the kingdom, whatever that may mean. You don't know if it particularly matters based on "
"how quickly you're swarmed by the nobles and their guards."
msgstr ""
"你刚要说出那个词，典藏官便瞪大双眼，打了个响指。你嘴唇还在动，却发不出任何声音。他轻笑一"
"声，向守卫告辞，又打了个响指。转眼间，你们已站在一座宏伟的王座前。那王座气势十足，也浮夸"
"得毫不含糊。王座上坐着一名看起来正值中年的矮人。他深色的胡须间缀满宝石与金属饰扣，与头上"
"的王冠颇为相配。\n"
"\n"
"你们似乎被直接带进了一场盛大的宴会。王座大厅里，一桌桌珍馐美食令人垂涎，衣着考究的矮人宾"
"客满堂皆是。对于你们的突然出现，宾客们显得既好奇又兴奋。你觉得，这总比猜疑和恐惧要好。典"
"藏官飘到国王身旁，在他耳边低语了几句。国王的眼神由好奇转为震惊，接着又变成了……兴奋。他拍"
"了一下手，站起身，向满厅宾客宣布：助兴的节目来了。\n"
"\n"
"你们被领到大厅中央。随后，几位长相粗犷的贵族带着各自的护卫，陆续围了上来。\n"
"\n"
"国王宣布，不许伤及你们的性命，只须好好欢迎二位来到王国。至于这“欢迎”究竟是什么意思，你也"
"不清楚。不过，贵族和守卫一拥而上，你已经没工夫琢磨这话管不管用了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Nothing too scary, then?"
msgstr "那应该没什么吓人的吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "She seems pleased."
msgstr "她看起来挺满意。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you beat down the guards and nobles who look at you expectantly, you wouldn't have "
"guessed the king himself would have risen to join in on the fun, but through no small "
"deal of effort, he fell like the rest of his people. You tried your best to not kill "
"the man, but with how hard he hit the ground, you wonder if you overdid it.\n"
"\n"
"You clutch your weapon, covered in more blood than you ever would have expected for a "
"'friendly' bout. With the Nalidaian king at your feet, you eye the Archivist, worried "
"that despite the promise of this just being for 'entertainment,' you'd find yourself at "
"the hands of a much more upset populace. Instead, he shrugs towards you and gives a "
"small nod.\n"
"\n"
"Oyadazminis groans and pushes himself up, he beams with a giant smile, several of his "
"missing teeth having been replaced by intricately carved gemstones. If this is "
"'entertainment' to these dwarves, you're surprised he's not missing more.\n"
"\n"
"He waves to the nobles and grabs you and [Companion Name] by your shoulders, dragging "
"you off behind the throne room to an lavishly decorated room, with the Archivist "
"following closely behind. The floating man waves his hand over the door, causing the "
"entrance to vanish entirely under a waterfall of blue sparks."
msgstr ""
"你接连打倒那些跃跃欲试的守卫和贵族，却没想到国王本人也会起身加入这场热闹。费了好一番力气"
"后，他也和自己的臣民一样倒下了。你已经尽量留手，可见他摔得那么重，还是不免担心自己是不是"
"打过了头。\n"
"\n"
"你紧握武器，身上沾满鲜血，远远超出了你对一场“友好切磋”的预期。纳里达西的国王就倒在你脚"
"边。你看向典藏官，心里有些发虚：虽说事先讲好了只是“助兴”，可这些矮人真不会翻脸吗？他却只"
"是朝你耸耸肩，微微点了点头。\n"
"\n"
"奥亚达兹米尼斯呻吟着撑起身，咧嘴大笑。他缺了几颗牙，镶着雕工精细的宝石。要是这些矮人平时"
"就靠这个“助兴”，你倒奇怪他怎么还有这么多牙。\n"
"\n"
"他朝贵族们挥挥手，一手揽住你，一手揽住[Companion Name]，把你们带进王座大厅后方一间装饰华"
"丽的房间。典藏官紧随其后。悬在空中的典藏官抬手一挥，蓝色火花如瀑布般倾泻而下，整扇门随即"
"消失得无影无踪。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Haven't had a proper bout like that in half a dozen years!"
msgstr "足足六年没打得这么痛快了！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Don't get visitors with as much fire n' 'em as the both of you everyday. Thanks for "
"indulging my people, they'll like you a lot more for that."
msgstr ""
"像你们俩这么有劲头的客人，可不是天天都能碰上。多谢你们陪大家尽兴。这一场打完，他们肯定更"
"喜欢你们了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It didn't seem that any of you were particularly keen on letting us not participate."
msgstr "可我看，你们也没打算让我们拒绝吧。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You could have gone crying to your mothers at any moment, but you would have been "
"laughed out of the courtroom."
msgstr "你们随时都能哭着回去找妈妈，不过那样的话，就得一路被笑出大厅了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The Archivist told me what you seek. At least, part of it."
msgstr "典藏官把你们的来意告诉我了。至少说了一部分。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If I were to let anyone into the Archives, they'd have to work their stones off for "
"half a human lifetime to even glimpse the outermost door."
msgstr "换了别人，想进典藏馆，非得卖命干上半个人类的寿命，才有资格看一眼最外面那扇门。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't imagine the two of you have the time for such things, if you're telling the "
"truth about our... mutual acquaintances."
msgstr "不过，关于我们那两位……共同的熟人，你们要是没撒谎，想必也没工夫等那么久。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I don't know if I'd call them that at this point..."
msgstr "事到如今，我可不知道还该不该把他们当熟人……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But the two of you are familiar with Talm and Era, then?"
msgstr "这么说，你们二位认识塔尔姆和艾拉？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Aye. They translated half the... special materials we've got in the Archives long ago."
msgstr "对。很久以前，他们替我们翻译过典藏馆里一半的……特殊资料。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Decided that as payment, they'd take the other half. So many years of history lost..."
msgstr "然后决定拿走另一半，作为报酬。那么多古老的史料，就这么没了……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Under normal circumstances I'd agree, but if those books had anything to do with the "
"nastiness that tall fella could do..."
msgstr "换作别的东西，我也会心疼。可那些书要是跟那个高个子使的邪门手段有关……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Good riddance, I say."
msgstr "依我看，拿走了才好。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We got rather well acquainted with it ourselves. "
msgstr "那些手段，我们也算亲自领教过了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Why we need to get into the Archives is a long story, but... it was under their "
"recommendation."
msgstr "我们为什么要进典藏馆，说来话长。不过……确实是他们指点我们来的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I believe that, which is the only reason I didn't toss you out the second it was "
"mentioned."
msgstr "这我信。不然，你们一提这件事，就已经被我赶出去了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That whole art... It's dangerous. Most everyone at my level of station across the "
"continent is at least loosely aware of Summoning."
msgstr "那门法术……极其危险。整个大陆上，地位与我相当的人，大多多少少都知道些召唤术的事。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Mostly because each nation has their own collection of histories and magic under lock "
"and key. Too treacherous to share. Using it is out of the question."
msgstr ""
"主要是因为，各国都把与之有关的史料和魔法典籍严密封存着。公开太危险。使用就更不必说了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"To be honest, your arrival and need for said materials has us more... concerned more "
"than anything."
msgstr "说实话，你们突然到访，还要查阅那些资料，我们更多的是……担忧。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Talm and Era are two of the most trusted individuals to the kingdom, but we cannot "
"simply give the materials to you."
msgstr "塔尔姆和艾拉深受王国信任，但我们也不能就这么把资料交给你们。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Aye. We trust their judgement, but both protocol and public perception hold a lot of "
"sway here."
msgstr "对。我们信得过他们。不过，该守的规矩得守，也得让大家心服口服。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Can we do anything else that doesn't involve public beatdowns or ballroom brawls to "
"earn our way in, then?"
msgstr "那除了当众打一架、把宴会厅闹个底朝天，我们还能做点什么，换个进去的资格？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yes, and it'll be your great pleasure to do so. My lovely daughter will be your ward. "
"You couldn't find yourself in better hands if you tried."
msgstr "当然有，而且是件美差。我的宝贝女儿就托付给你们了。有她帮忙，你们尽管放心。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As Oyadazminis finishes, there's a shimmer in the corner of the room. A young red "
"haired dwarf steps out from seemingly thin air, a cloak of woven blue metal thread "
"billowing out around her. She introduces herself as Redilok and gives a small curtsy "
"and mentions she enjoyed watching you give her father quite the wallop out in the "
"ballroom. The king turns about as red as his daughter's hair and shakes his head before "
"motioning for the Archivist to rematerialize the door, then the two of them depart.\n"
"\n"
"The princess opens a new door in a different section of wall and motions for the two of "
"you to follow. You pass through the doorway and find yourselves on the balcony of a "
"large tower connected to - what you presume is - the castle you were just in. The "
"balcony overlooks the whole of Koganusan, the whole of the capitol fitting within an "
"unbelievable hollow under the Perilous Peaks. You hardly have the time to take it in "
"before the princess starts running through its extensive history, and that of their "
"western neighbors, a smaller kingdom of dwarves who live under a large volcanic "
"mountain range.\n"
"\n"
"What she wants your assistance with is no small task. Connecting the two kingdoms via a "
"magical transport line that allows a stone platform to accelerate to incredible speeds. "
"The 'Stoneway' as she calls it is already well underway, but still needs an "
"extraordinary amount of work. Before you're allowed to begin though, you must show her "
"how you go about summoning creatures, purely to satisfy her curiosity. If she's to "
"vouch for you, she wants to know just what secrets her father intends to give away to "
"humans."
msgstr ""
"奥亚达兹米尼斯刚说完，房间角落便闪过一阵微光。一个年轻的红发矮人女孩凭空走了出来，身上那"
"件用蓝色金属丝织成的斗篷随之飘动。她微微屈膝行礼，介绍自己叫雷迪洛克，又说刚才看你们在宴"
"会厅把她父亲狠狠揍了一顿，实在过瘾。国王的脸涨得几乎和女儿的头发一样红。他摇摇头，示意典"
"藏官把门变回来，随后两人一同离开了。\n"
"\n"
"公主在另一面墙上打开一扇门，招呼你们跟上。你们穿过门，来到一座高塔的阳台上。这座塔连着一"
"座城堡，想必就是你们刚才待的地方。站在阳台上，整座科加努桑尽收眼底。险恶山脉下的洞窟大得"
"不可思议，竟容纳了整座都城。你还没看上几眼，公主便开始讲述这座城市漫长的历史，接着又说起"
"西边的邻国。那是一个较小的矮人王国，建在一大片火山山脉之下。\n"
"\n"
"她想请你们帮忙的事，着实不小。她打算修建一条连接两国的魔法运输线，让石台沿着线路飞速行"
"驶。这条被她称作“石道”的线路已经修了一大段，可要做的事仍然堆积如山。不过，动工之前，她想"
"先看看你们是怎么召唤生物的。没别的，就是好奇。既然要为你们担保，她总得弄清楚，父亲究竟准"
"备把什么秘密交给人类。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Since she was in the room when her father mentioned the closely guarded art of "
"Summoning, you don't find any harm in indulging the princess's request. You and "
"[Companion Name] show princess Redilok several of the creatures you've learned to "
"create over your journey here, much to her pleasure. She takes several sketches of the "
"beasts, and asks for you to make them perform... all manner of things, some practical, "
"some a bit silly. She questions you on your journey here throughout the 'tests' as she "
"calls them. You fill her in. The Soulsmiths, your travels. Talm and Era's trials. She "
"listens without a single comment, enraptured by your tales.\n"
"\n"
"After a long while and the summoning of several more creatures, Redilok closes her "
"notepad and makes it vanish, much like the Archivist did with the door, earlier. She "
"thanks you for your time and asks you to make yourself at home, and that she'll be in "
"touch very soon regarding the Stoneway, then promptly slips off the balcony backward "
"and disappears.\n"
"\n"
"After confirming you didn't just witness the princess fall to her untimely death, you "
"enter what seems to be 'your' room from the balcony and find a room that likely cost "
"several thousand gold just to furnish, let alone build. A two plush four poster beds, a "
"pool of steaming water kept warm by some arcane source you're unfamiliar with. Thick "
"carpet, beautiful silken drapes, and various pieces of artwork depicting lands you've "
"never seen nor heard of.\n"
"\n"
"The sight is made a bit warmer by the fact that [Companion Name] has already launched "
"herself at the nearest bed and started to snore before even making contact with the "
"pillow, a sentiment you cannot help but share moments later."
msgstr ""
"先前她父亲谈起召唤术这门严守的秘术时，她就在房间里。既然如此，你觉得给她看看也无妨。你和"
"[Companion Name]召出几种一路上学会创造的生物，让雷迪洛克公主看了个够。她兴致勃勃地给这些"
"野兽画了几张速写，又让你们指挥它们做这做那。有些要求还算实用，有些就纯粹是在逗着玩了。她"
"把这些叫作“测试”，还一边看，一边问起你们来这里之前的经历。你将一路上的事告诉了她。炼魂"
"师，还有你们四处奔波的经历。还有塔尔姆和艾拉设下的考验。她听得入神，一句也没有插嘴。\n"
"\n"
"又过了好一阵，你们还多召了几种生物给她看。雷迪洛克这才合上笔记本，让它凭空消失，就像典藏"
"官先前变走那扇门一样。她谢过你们花时间演示，让你们把这里当自己家，又说很快会来找你们商量"
"石道的事。说完，她便向后一仰，翻下阳台，没了踪影。\n"
"\n"
"确认公主并没有就这么摔死，你们才从阳台走进似乎是为你们安排的客房。单看里面的陈设，恐怕就"
"花了几千金币，还不算建造房间的费用。两张柔软的四柱床，一池冒着热气的水。池水靠某种你不熟"
"悉的魔法保持着温热。脚下铺着厚地毯，窗边垂着精美的丝绸帷幔，四周摆着各式艺术品，描绘的都"
"是你从未见过、甚至从未听说过的地方。\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name]早已扑向最近的那张床，头还没挨上枕头就打起了呼噜。看她这副模样，你也觉得"
"这里亲切了几分。没过多久，你便和她一样，倒头睡着了"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ22"
msgstr "MQ22"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Stoneway Yourway - After a warm welcome to the kingdom of the Nalidasi Dwarves, "
"Princess Redilok is primed to accept your help in finishing the last of the Stoneway, "
"which will earn your entry into the Royal Archives."
msgstr ""
"石道通途——在纳里达西矮人王国受到一番热情款待后，你们即将协助雷迪洛克公主完成石道的最后一"
"段工程。作为回报，你们将被允许进入皇族典藏馆。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I've been working on the Stoneeeeway~"
msgstr "我在石道上干活哟～"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "All the live long... is it daytime down here?"
msgstr "从早一直忙到……这底下现在算白天吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You wake to find breakfast floating towards you, with Princess Redilok floating just "
"behind it. She pours over a large scroll, as your meal assembles itself on a silver "
"tray inches above your lap. You feel horrendously underdressed and disheveled to be in "
"the presence of royalty, but she hardly seems to notice. Her fault for coming "
"unannounced. You still do your best to make yourself marginally more presentable, then "
"lightly pick at the meal in front of you. You glance towards [Companion Name] who seems "
"even more flustered by the princess's sudden arrival. You catch her eye and lightly "
"wipe at the corner of your mouth, trying to get her to wipe the drool away. She hardly "
"contains a groan before doing so as subtly as she can.\n"
"\n"
"Once satisfied with whatever she was looking through, Redilok looks up to address you "
"both, her smile as sweet as the flaky pastry you bite into."
msgstr ""
"你一觉醒来，发现早餐正朝你飘来，雷迪洛克公主就飘在后面。她埋头研究着一卷大卷轴，早餐则自"
"行摆上银托盘，悬在你腿上方。在公主面前，你这副衣衫不整、睡眼惺忪的模样实在有失体面，可她"
"似乎毫不在意。谁让她来之前也不打声招呼呢。你还是尽量收拾了一下，让自己看起来像点样子，才"
"慢慢吃起面前的早餐。你朝[Companion Name]瞥了一眼。公主突然到访，她看起来比你还窘迫。等她"
"看向你，你轻轻擦了擦嘴角，示意她把口水擦掉。她差点呻吟出声，赶紧尽可能不动声色地擦了擦"
"嘴。\n"
"\n"
"雷迪洛克终于看完卷轴，满意地抬起头。她朝你们一笑，笑容甜得就像你刚咬下的那口酥点。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Please, you two. If you couldn't tell by the way my father welcomed you to our home "
"with a kerfuffle by all the top-brass in the kingdom, we do things a bit differently "
"here."
msgstr ""
"哎呀，你们两个。我父亲拉上王国里一众大人物，跟你们打了一架当作欢迎。你们还没看出来吗？我"
"们这儿的规矩跟外面不太一样。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Your human modesty and decorum will only get you funny looks here. Dig in!"
msgstr "你们人类那套拘谨的礼数，在这里反倒让人觉得奇怪。放开吃！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...We're honored, princess."
msgstr "……多谢公主款待。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Tsk tsk. What'd I just say?"
msgstr "啧啧。我刚才说什么来着？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"None of that stuffy business. You need to eat up if you're going to help our Stoneway "
"workers."
msgstr "别这么拘束。待会儿还要帮忙修石道呢，不吃饱怎么行？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd like to ask... if you already have people working on this project, why would our "
"aid be needed, exactly?"
msgstr "我想问问……既然已经有人在修了，为什么还需要我们帮忙？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And not that we mind, but that's all it'll take to get us into the archives?"
msgstr "倒不是不愿意，不过，只要帮着修完，我们就能进典藏馆了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Good questions!"
msgstr "问得好！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The tunnel to excavate the Stoneway met with a bit of a... snag. There was a cavern "
"right near the middle of our kingdoms that seemed man or dwarfmade."
msgstr ""
"开凿石道隧道的时候，我们碰上了点……麻烦。就在两国之间，差不多正中间的位置，有一座洞窟，看"
"着像是人类或矮人开凿的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Not too uncommon considering the distance, but the cavern was guarded by beasts made of "
"the same magic I had you show me earlier."
msgstr ""
"这一路这么长，碰到这种地方倒不稀奇。可洞里有野兽守着，用的正是你们之前给我演示过的那种魔"
"法。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"For such scary beasties, they didn't put up much of a fight and we finished excavating "
"the route for the Stoneway. Not without some losses, though."
msgstr ""
"那些野兽长得吓人，倒没费多少工夫就解决了。石道的路线也顺利挖通了。不过，我们还是折了些人"
"手。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Seems a bit miraculous to stumble across a cavern filled with ancient beasts."
msgstr "偏偏就碰上一座藏着古老野兽的洞窟，未免太巧了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're on the same page, then."
msgstr "看来咱们想到一块儿去了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My father - bless the foolhardy man - is sure it was a trap set by the Flamberian "
"Dwarves, despite the fact the Stoneway is meant to connect us."
msgstr ""
"我父亲那个莽撞性子啊……一口咬定是弗拉姆贝里矮人设的陷阱。可这条石道，本来就是为了连接两国"
"才修的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...And help bury old grudges..."
msgstr "……也好让大家放下过去的仇怨……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You don't seem to share the sentiment though. You think it was someone else?"
msgstr "不过，你好像不这么想。你觉得另有其人？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I do. There was a war between our kingdoms long before my father was even a pebble in "
"his father's eye, but Dwarven grudges run deep."
msgstr ""
"没错。两国确实打过仗，那时候连我祖父都还没想着要我父亲这个孩子呢。可矮人记起仇来，哪有那"
"么容易忘。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Despite the years, our elders are worried something will go awry and are jumping at the "
"chance to reignite the old war."
msgstr "这么多年过去，长辈们还是总担心出岔子，一有风吹草动，就恨不得重燃战火。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The tunnel to excavate the Stoneway met with a bit of a... snag. There was a cavern "
"right near the middle of our kingdoms that seemed man or dwarf-made."
msgstr ""
"开凿石道隧道的时候，我们碰上了点……麻烦。就在两国之间，差不多正中间的位置，有一座洞窟，看"
"着像是人类或矮人开凿的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I've been working with their prince for half a decade on the Stoneway now, and he's an "
"honest man. This wasn't them."
msgstr "为了修这条石道，我和他们的王子已经共事五年了。他为人正直。这事不是他们干的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe something else, then? You remember the Soulsmiths from our stories earlier?"
msgstr "那，会不会是别的势力？还记得我们之前提过的炼魂师吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd be surprised, but it's not as though there's other Summoning clans running amok "
"nowadays, are there?"
msgstr "真是他们，我会有些意外。不过，如今四处作乱的召唤师氏族，应该也没有别家了吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If there are, we haven't had the misfortune of meeting them. Can you think of any "
"reason why they'd target your people?"
msgstr "就算有，我们也还没倒霉到碰上。你想得到他们为什么要对付你们吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No, I can't, and that's what worries me, and why I want the two of you there as we "
"complete the Stoneway."
msgstr "想不到，这才让我担心。所以石道竣工的时候，我希望你们也在场。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The rulers won't be there in person, but several high-ranking nobles - along with the "
"Flamberian Prince and myself - will hold a small celebration in the center of the "
"Stoneway as it's finished."
msgstr ""
"两国君主都不会亲自来，不过会有几位地位显赫的贵族出席。我和弗拉姆贝里王子也会到场，在石道"
"中段办个小型庆典，庆祝竣工。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And we're to be there incase something happens with the Soulsmiths."
msgstr "我们负责留意炼魂师，防着他们来捣乱。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Redilok nods, then leaves to let the two of you eat and get prepared. When she returns, "
"another magical doorway that she creates takes you to what she calls the Stoneway "
"Station. Several deep set rails of metal stretch along the ground, far, far into a "
"tunnel that stretches into the distance. The underground pathway is lit by blue-green "
"balls of floating light spaced evenly apart, giving as much light as if the Stoneway "
"was above ground instead of thousands of meters below it. \n"
"\n"
"Dozens of dwarves carry lengths of rails etched with glowing runes onto the stone "
"platform hovering above the metal path. Making sure you're not in the way, you step "
"upon the rectangular 'Slabglider' at Redilok's request. The Slabglider is the length of "
"several carts stacked end-to-end, with comfy seating along its outer edge, with plenty "
"of space for the rails and cargo between.\n"
"\n"
"Once fully loaded, Redilok smiles and snaps her fingers, sending the platform cruising "
"through the tunnel at dizzying speed. Despite how fast the three of you hurtle down the "
"path, the ride seems remarkably calm. Your body feels still, but the lights whizzing by "
"faster than your eyes can track show you're definitely moving.\n"
"\n"
"It's not long before the Slabglider begins to slow and then stop. You worry something "
"is wrong before Redilok confirms that you're near the center of the Stoneway, meaning "
"that you crossed nearly a fourth of the continent in minutes. It's hard to even wrap "
"your head around.\n"
"\n"
"Once you disembark, several dwarves - some Nalidasi, some Flamberian - jump aboard and "
"start unloading metal rails. You figure you 'ought to help instead of just standing "
"around waiting."
msgstr ""
"雷迪洛克点点头，随后离开，让你们安心吃饭，收拾妥当。等她回来，又开出一扇魔法门，带你们来"
"到她所说的石道车站。几条金属轨道深嵌在地面上，顺着隧道一直延伸到远处。蓝绿色的光球等距悬"
"在空中，将整条地下通道照得亮如白昼，几乎让人忘了这里是数千米深的地底。\n"
"\n"
"几十个矮人正把一段段刻着发光符文的轨道，搬上悬在金属轨道上方的石台。你避开忙碌的工人，按"
"照雷迪洛克的指示，登上那座长方形的“石板滑行者”。石板滑行者足有几辆车首尾相接那么长，四周"
"设着舒适的座位，中间则留出大片空间，装载轨道和其他货物。\n"
"\n"
"货物装齐，雷迪洛克笑着打了个响指，石台立刻沿隧道飞驰起来，快得令人目眩。虽然你们三人在通"
"道里疾速前进，坐起来却出奇平稳。身体感觉不到丝毫晃动，只有两旁飞掠而过、快得看不清的灯"
"光，提醒你们确实正在移动。\n"
"\n"
"没过多久，石板滑行者便开始减速，停了下来。你还以为出了什么问题，雷迪洛克却告诉你，这里已"
"接近石道中段。也就是说，你们只花了几分钟，就穿过了将近四分之一片大陆。你一时简直无法想"
"象。\n"
"\n"
"你们下了石台，几个矮人便跳了上去，开始卸下金属轨道。他们中既有纳里达西人，也有弗拉姆贝里"
"人。你觉得与其站着干等，不如搭把手。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Come on... Someone has to be out of place..."
msgstr "快找找……总有人不对劲……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "There!"
msgstr "看那儿！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're able to follow along with the dwarves quite well, and they're a bit impressed as "
"you and [Companion Name] keep up with laying the railings and locking them into place. "
"The Flamberians get to work as you set each in place and you finally take a good look "
"at them. Each appears almost molten lacking any traditional skin and instead seeming to "
"be made out of a stone-like material with bright red magma heating the rock as some "
"sort of vein system, serving a purpose you can't even begin to guess at. Among them is "
"their own royal, Prince Cintak.\n"
"\n"
"They grip the newly connected rails at heat it until it's red-hot, binding individual "
"sections together into one fully linked pathway. Once that's done, the Nalidasi etch in "
"a last set of runes, activating the section of rail. Both Redilok and Cintak are active "
"participants in the Stoneway creation, though you do note they do disappear alone "
"together more than a few times throughout your time working on the path.\n"
"\n"
"Construction goes on for a long time, and you end up returning to Koganusan several "
"times, eating, sleeping, and enjoying the luxuries of staying within the royal palace, "
"getting more acquainted with Redilok and several nobles within the kingdom's upper-"
"ranks.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, days after you began, the blue lights that light the corridor give way to red, "
"and the rail you lay connects to that of the Flamberian's side of the Stoneway. It "
"isn't sealed into place just yet, as this will be done at the ceremony Redilok informs "
"you is called the 'Linking'."
msgstr ""
"你们很快跟上了矮人的节奏，一段段铺好轨道，再固定到位。见你和[Companion Name]干得有模有"
"样，他们也有些佩服。你们每放好一段，弗拉姆贝里矮人便接手处理。这时，你才有机会仔细打量他"
"们。他们个个都像是半熔化的岩石，身上没有寻常的皮肤，取而代之的是石头般的外壳。鲜红的岩浆"
"沿着血管似的脉络流动，将岩石烘得灼热。至于这副身体究竟如何运转，你完全想不明白。他们的王"
"族，辛塔克王子，也在其中。\n"
"\n"
"他们握住刚刚接好的轨道，将其加热至通红，把一段段接缝熔合，连成完整的线路。随后，纳里达西"
"矮人再刻上最后一组符文，激活这一段轨道。雷迪洛克和辛塔克都亲自参与修建。不过，你也注意"
"到，干活期间，两人好几次单独溜走，不见了踪影。\n"
"\n"
"工程持续了很久，你们也几次返回科加努桑，吃饭、休息，享受住在王宫里的种种便利。其间，你们"
"渐渐熟悉了雷迪洛克，也结识了几位王国的大贵族。\n"
"\n"
"终于，开工数日后，通道里的蓝光变成了红光。你们铺下的轨道，与弗拉姆贝里一侧的石道接上了。"
"不过，最后的接缝还没有熔合。雷迪洛克告诉你，这一步要留到“接轨仪式”上完成。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Several years in the making... I can hardly believe we're done."
msgstr "修了好几年……真不敢相信，总算完工了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hopefully the first step among many in soothing the wounds of the past."
msgstr "但愿这是弥合旧日伤痕的第一步，往后还能有更多。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Though I'm surprised Redilok sought it fit to bring along two humans, I trust her "
"judgement."
msgstr "雷迪洛克竟会请两位人类来帮忙，确实让我有些意外。不过，我相信她的眼光。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...thanks, I think?"
msgstr "……那就，多谢了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're just happy we could help out."
msgstr "能帮上忙，我们也很高兴。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm sure... Though, I know you're here to ensure the Linking goes well. The royal "
"princess has informed me of such."
msgstr ""
"那是自然……不过，我知道二位来这里，是为了确保接轨仪式顺利举行。公主殿下已经告诉我了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You have my gratitude. Please ensure her safety over mine. I couldn't bare it to-"
msgstr "多谢二位。如果有危险，请优先保护她。我实在无法承受她……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Cinny, please! All this propriety is going to put them off."
msgstr "小辛，拜托！你这么一本正经的，会把他们吓跑的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Cinny?"
msgstr "……小辛？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's just a nickname of sorts the royal princess is fond of. It really doesn't mean "
"much, pay it no mind."
msgstr "只是公主殿下喜欢用的一个昵称。没什么特别的，不必在意。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Doesn't mean much, hm? You told me you loved it."
msgstr "没什么特别的，嗯？你明明说过很喜欢。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Of course I do my precious little cabochon! I-"
msgstr "当然喜欢，我的宝石小心肝！我……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...*ahem*."
msgstr "……*呃哼*。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The two of you are observant, I'm sure you've noticed the princess and I's..."
msgstr "二位这么细心，想必也注意到了，我和公主……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Disappearances off into the dark of the tunnels?"
msgstr "经常溜进隧道暗处？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Alone?"
msgstr "就你们两个？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Yes."
msgstr "是。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I am in no position to ask this of you, but I must do so anyway."
msgstr "我本不该向二位提出这样的要求，可还是得厚着脸皮开口。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Please keep this between yourselves for now. After the Linking the two of us intend to "
"announce..."
msgstr "请暂时替我们保密。接轨仪式结束后，我们打算宣布……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The royal princess and I-"
msgstr "公主殿下与我——"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh Cinny. I'm sure they figured it out on day one."
msgstr "哎呀，小辛。我看他们第一天就猜出来了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're in loveeeeee~"
msgstr "我们相爱啦～"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Neither of us have any reason to mind, but isn't that a bit..."
msgstr "我们当然没什么意见，不过，这是不是有点……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Scandalous? Daring? Risqué, maybe?"
msgstr "有伤体面？胆大包天？不太合规矩？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh it is. "
msgstr "可不是嘛。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Tell. Us. Everything."
msgstr "快。给我们讲讲。怎么回事。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...but the Linking."
msgstr "……可接轨仪式……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Cinny darling, it's a party! Drop a couple stones and lighten up, I've never gotten to "
"tell anyone about this~"
msgstr "亲爱的小辛，这可是庆典！别端着啦，放松点。我还从没跟别人说起过这件事呢～"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Prince Cintak simply holds his stony face in his hands as the princess starts to "
"divulge far more detail than you would have thought she'd offer up. The Slabglider "
"departs back towards Koganusan and comes back with half a village of dwarves, tables, "
"decor, and liquor. Then it speeds off towards the Flamberian capitol and brings back "
"even more. Just like that, the Linking is underway.\n"
"\n"
"You and [Companion Name] stroll about the thrown together party. The Stoneglider comes "
"and goes multiple times, bringing more people, food, and furnishings, all of which are "
"tucked into the carved out alcove you all reside in. The atmosphere is lively, "
"sometimes too much so. It'd seem the king isn't the only one with longstanding grudges, "
"and several scuffles break out through the celebration, but they're quickly quelled.\n"
"\n"
"You're on edge, waiting for any sign of the Soulsmiths. You scan every new arrival, "
"take stock of each good brought in, and... the small hint of blood left on one of the "
"chairs.\n"
"\n"
"With the small fights, rowdy dwarves, and free flowing alcohol, it's no wonder someone "
"could have gotten hurt, but the chair hadn't been unloaded from the Slabglider yet.\n"
"\n"
"Something is awry, you just don't know what yet."
msgstr ""
"辛塔克王子只能双手捂住自己那张石头脸。公主则兴致勃勃地讲了起来，细得远远超出了你的预料。"
"石板滑行者返回科加努桑，再回来时，带来了足有半个村子那么多的矮人，还有桌椅、装饰和酒。随"
"后，它又飞驰前往弗拉姆贝里都城，运回了更多宾客和物资。就这样，接轨庆典开始了。\n"
"\n"
"你和[Companion Name]在临时布置的会场里四处走动。石板滑行者来来回回，又带来更多宾客、食物"
"和桌椅，把你们所在的这处开凿出来的洞厅塞得满满当当。气氛热闹得很，有时甚至热闹过了头。看"
"来，放不下旧怨的不止国王。庆典上接连起了几场冲突，不过很快都被制止了。\n"
"\n"
"你始终绷着神经，留意着炼魂师的踪迹。每个新到的宾客，每批运来的物资，你都仔细看过。然后……"
"你发现一把椅子上沾着一点血。\n"
"\n"
"会场里有人打架，有人闹腾，酒更是一杯接一杯，磕破点皮本不奇怪。可这把椅子还没从石板滑行者"
"上卸下来。\n"
"\n"
"一定有哪里出了问题，只是你还没弄清楚。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh no..."
msgstr "糟了……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Where is the princess?!"
msgstr "公主在哪儿？！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You move through the crowds and finally spot who you were looking for. The Nalidasi "
"dwarf is almost indistinguishable from everyone else, except the fact that she's a bit "
"more pale, and seems far less into the festivities than anyone else. She carries a "
"large barrel draped in cloth and tucks it amongst many others at the back of the "
"alcove.\n"
"\n"
"You stop her by grabbing her arm, and the pale dwarf doesn't even react to your "
"presence. [Companion Name] pulls up the dwarf's sleeve and you see her arm coated by a "
"thick stream of blood. The woman drops the barrel, but stands motionless in your grip, "
"lifeless eyes staring up at you. Quickly checking the woman over, you peel back her "
"collar, you see that the blood on her arm must have come from her slit neck, which was "
"intentionally hidden under her bulky garb. The dwarf's blank look reminds you of Talm "
"controlling the Soulsmith back in the capitol, and judging by her state, you know she's "
"being controlled by someone. \n"
"\n"
"But it's too late. Volatile runes spill out from the dropped barrel, similar to those "
"you made with Gloob, though these look substantially better crafted.\n"
"\n"
"Another dwarf - this one Flamberian - breaks the top of a barrel at the back of the "
"room and sinks his hands inside of it before heating himself red hot.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] draws her bow and shoots at the dwarf, but the damage is done. You "
"hear the sizzling of the volatile runes and cry out to anyone nearby."
msgstr ""
"你穿过人群，终于找到了那个可疑的身影。那是个纳里达西女矮人，和其他人几乎没有区别，只是脸"
"色苍白了些，对周围的庆祝活动也远没有旁人那么热衷。她搬着一只蒙了布的大桶，将它放进洞厅后"
"方的一堆桶里。\n"
"\n"
"你一把抓住她的胳膊，将她拦下。这个脸色苍白的矮人却对你的出现毫无反应。[Companion Name]拉"
"起她的袖子，你看见一大股鲜血顺着她的手臂流了下来。女矮人松开手，桶掉在地上。她却仍一动不"
"动地任你抓着，用毫无生气的双眼仰望着你。你迅速检查她的身体，掀开衣领才发现，她的喉咙已被"
"割开。胳膊上的血显然是从那里流下来的，而厚重的衣服正好遮住了伤口。那副空洞的神情，让你想"
"起塔尔姆在都城操控的那个炼魂师。看她这模样，你知道，她也正受人操纵。\n"
"\n"
"但一切都太晚了。不稳定的符文从落地的桶中滚了出来，跟你和格鲁布制作过的相似，只是这些的做"
"工明显精良得多。\n"
"\n"
"另一个矮人，这次是弗拉姆贝里人，砸开洞厅后方的一只桶，把双手探了进去，随即浑身烧得通"
"红。\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name]拉弓射他，可已经来不及了。符文发出嘶嘶声，你扯开嗓子，朝周围的人大喊。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Everyone! Get down!"
msgstr "所有人！趴下！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're under attack!"
msgstr "有人袭击！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You see several dwarves by the wall turn towards you, startled by the arrow whizzing in "
"their direction and your shout. They disappear as the runes in the barrel and several "
"others nearby explode with a burst of magical energy, swallowing them entirely in a "
"flash of white light.\n"
"\n"
"The whole world heaves upward. [Companion Name] grabs you as you're sent careening out "
"of the alcove and down the tunnel, crashing to the ground with a sickening series of "
"cracks then rolling several meters.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you stagger towards your feet and rush back inside to see that half the "
"cavity has been reduced to rubble, and many of those attending were killed instantly by "
"the blast. The cleared out section is... far larger than it should be, as a large "
"cavern is revealed by the blast. Soulsmiths adorned with gold trimmed robes and long, "
"black metal weapons begin to flood out from the hole and descend on the Dwarves "
"alongside their dark summoned monsters. \n"
"\n"
"The sight is horrifyingly similar to that dark night in Azamire.\n"
"\n"
"Behind the cultists is a slug-like monster that pulls itself along the ground on "
"countless sets of arms, pulling itself into the opening with sickening, twitchy "
"movements. The creature is nearly as long as the Stoneglider, and twice as tall. A "
"large black metal vessel protrudes from the beast's back, seemingly fused to it. You "
"watch the device on its back begins to glow as it pulls itself towards the dead dwarves "
"on the ground.\n"
"\n"
"A pulse of dark green light washes over the bombed-out alcove.\n"
"\n"
"Then the dead begin to move again. "
msgstr ""
"墙边的几个矮人被飞来的箭和你的喊声惊动，转头望向你。下一刻，那只桶和附近几只桶里的符文同"
"时炸开，魔力喷涌而出。白光一闪，他们便被彻底吞没了。\n"
"\n"
"整个世界猛地向上一掀。[Companion Name]一把抓住你，你们一起被抛出洞厅，飞进隧道，重重砸在"
"地上。接连几声脆响令人心惊，你们又滚出了好几米。\n"
"\n"
"你们挣扎着站起来，赶紧冲回洞厅。里面已有一半被炸成废墟，不少宾客当场丧命。爆炸后露出的空"
"间……大得不对劲。原来，岩壁后还藏着一座巨大的洞窟。身穿金边长袍、手持黑色金属长兵器的炼魂"
"师从洞口蜂拥而出，带着他们召唤的黑暗怪物，一同扑向矮人。\n"
"\n"
"这一幕，与阿扎米尔遇袭的那个黑夜像得令人胆寒。\n"
"\n"
"那些邪教徒身后，一头蛞蝓般的怪物正用无数条手臂拖着身体前进，一抽一抽地挤进洞口，看得人直"
"犯恶心。它几乎与石板滑行者一样长，高度却足有两倍。一个巨大的黑色金属容器从它背上凸出，看"
"起来已经与它的身体长在了一起。它朝地上的矮人尸体爬去，背上的装置随之亮起。\n"
"\n"
"一道暗绿色光芒扫过被炸毁的洞厅。\n"
"\n"
"一道暗绿色光芒扫过被炸毁的洞厅。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"When the dwarves that remain see you crash against the Soulsmiths, any who are able "
"follow close behind you, burning with unbridled rage. You do your best to defend those "
"too dazed or injured to help or run, but many are cut down by the Soulsmiths who weave "
"through the crowd of undead.\n"
"\n"
"This entire attack was planned out meticulously, maybe even your presence was accounted "
"for. You try to intercept a group that head towards the Stoneglider, but the horde of "
"undead stop you each time. Several Soulsmiths board the Stoneglider, load barrels of "
"volatile runes onto the platform, then send it hurtling towards Koganusan. There's "
"nothing you can do, there's too many things to deal with at once.\n"
"\n"
"In the heat of battle you catch a glimpse of Prince Cintak standing over Princess "
"Redilok, who clutches the new stump of her arm and tries to stem the bleeding. You try "
"to reach them, but there's simply too many undead between you. It's not long before the "
"prince is run through by one of the Soulsmith's black metal blades. He's then hefted "
"into the air and unceremoniously pinned onto the back of the horrific slug creature who "
"cries out as it's blubbery flesh is pierced. \n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] is much closer, she reaches the princess just in time to spare her "
"from the same fate as the prince. Moments after she cuts down the Soulsmith, those that "
"remain call out to one another, escaping with the body of the prince, following after "
"their beast who now scampers deeper into the cavern.\n"
"\n"
"The undead remain, but without the threat of the gold-robed Soulsmiths probing for "
"weaknesses or distractions, you're able to cut down the rest of them in short order. "
"You rush to the princess's side. Undeterred by her missing arm, she stands, eyes "
"piercing the dark of the cavern and staring towards those who took the prince. She "
"claims that it'd take more than that to kill him, and that the Soulsmiths wanted him "
"alive. [Companion Name] tries to stop the princess from following into the cavern, but "
"she's undeterred.\n"
"\n"
"Only thing you can do is follow after."
msgstr ""
"幸存的矮人见你冲向炼魂师，凡是还能战斗的，都满腔怒火地紧随其后。你竭力护住那些受伤太重，"
"或仍未回过神来、无法战斗也来不及逃跑的人。可炼魂师穿梭在亡者之间，还是杀死了不少人。\n"
"\n"
"整场袭击显然经过周密策划，或许连你们在场，都早已被算在其中。一队炼魂师朝石板滑行者奔去。"
"你几次想拦住他们，却都被成群的亡者挡了回来。几个炼魂师登上石板滑行者，把一桶桶不稳定的符"
"文搬上石台，随后让它朝科加努桑疾驰而去。你根本无力阻止。眼前要应付的敌人，已经太多了。\n"
"\n"
"混战中，你瞥见辛塔克王子正护在雷迪洛克公主身前。她一只手臂已被斩断，正紧紧按着断口，试图"
"止血。你想赶到他们身边，可中间隔着太多亡者。没过多久，一名炼魂师便用黑色金属利刃刺穿了王"
"子的身体。他将王子挑到半空，狠狠钉在那头恐怖的蛞蝓怪物背上。怪物肥厚的血肉被刺穿，发出一"
"声惨叫。\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name]离他们近得多。她及时赶到公主身边，才没让公主也遭受同样的厄运。她刚斩倒那"
"名炼魂师，剩下的敌人便互相呼喊着撤退。野兽驮着王子的身体，飞快爬向洞窟深处，他们紧随其"
"后。\n"
"\n"
"亡者仍在攻击，但没了那些金袍炼魂师伺机偷袭，你们很快便将它们全部解决。你冲到公主身旁。即"
"使失去一条手臂，她还是站了起来，目光直直望向黑暗深处，盯着掳走王子的那群人。她坚称，辛塔"
"克没那么容易死，炼魂师要的是活口。[Companion Name]试图拦住她，不让她追进洞窟，可她心意已"
"决。\n"
"\n"
"你们能做的，只有跟上去。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ23"
msgstr "MQ23"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Prince Procurement - After the Soulsmith attack on the Linking, you and [Companion "
"Name] follow after Princess Redilok who is out for blood. Will you find the prince at "
"the end of the path, or lose another royal in the process?"
msgstr ""
"营救王子——接轨庆典遭到炼魂师袭击后，你和[Companion Name]追着一心复仇的雷迪洛克公主，深入"
"洞窟。此行能否救回王子，还是连公主也会搭上性命？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll focus on breaking up the bigger rocks."
msgstr "大块的石头交给我来敲碎。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Light? We're close to the surface?"
msgstr "有光？快到地面了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You hold a lantern aloft as the three of you jog through the cavern, barely "
"illuminating the ancient tunnels. [Companion Name] continually tries to stop the "
"princess - at least long enough to properly tend to her missing arm - but Redilok "
"forces herself onward.\n"
"\n"
"Another blast echoes down the winding passage in front of you, the sudden rush of wind "
"nearly knocking you off your feet. You find the source not long after. The Soulsmiths "
"collapsed the cave behind them, the rubble still settling as rocks shift into place."
msgstr ""
"你高举提灯，勉强照亮古老的通道，三人一路小跑着穿过洞窟。[Companion Name]不断劝公主停下，"
"至少先把断臂的伤口好好处理一下，可雷迪洛克仍咬牙往前赶。\n"
"\n"
"前方又传来一声爆炸，轰鸣沿着蜿蜒的通道回荡。紧接着，一股气浪迎面扑来，险些把你掀翻。没走"
"多远，你们便找到了爆炸的位置。炼魂师炸塌了身后的通道。碎石堵住去路，还在不断滑落、堆积。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Those damn cowards!"
msgstr "这群该死的懦夫！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Both of you, give me a hand, will you?"
msgstr "你们两个，搭把手行不行？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I seem to have just lost one. And then some."
msgstr "我刚好缺只手。还缺了大半条胳膊。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We want to, princess, but we can't."
msgstr "公主，我们也想帮忙，可不能再追了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're injured, and by the time we cut through this, they'll be long gone."
msgstr "你还伤着，等我们挖通这里，他们早就跑远了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We should go back to Koganusan, regroup, and come back."
msgstr "先回科加努桑，召集人手再来吧。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "If they took [Companion Name] would you say the same?"
msgstr "要是被抓走的是[Companion Name]，你也会这么说吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I see your point."
msgstr "……我明白了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Can you do one of those doorway thinggies you did before to get us to the other side of "
"these rocks?"
msgstr "你能不能像之前那样开扇门，让我们直接到这些石头后面去？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I can only set the destination to somewhere I've been before, it won't help here."
msgstr "门只能通往我去过的地方。这里不行。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Then we'll have to go through. When we rescue the prince, can you get us back to the "
"capitol?"
msgstr "那就只能挖过去了。等救出王子，你能带我们回都城吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't think so. The further the destination, the more magic it takes out of me. We're "
"quite a ways from home."
msgstr "恐怕不行。目的地越远，耗费的魔力就越多。这里离家太远了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If we're lucky, some of the survivors will realize I'm a bit limited and will wait for "
"us."
msgstr "运气好的话，幸存者里会有人想到，我的本事也有个限度，留下来等我们。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Or... they'd be sensible and get themselves home, leaving us out here to this foolish "
"mission alone."
msgstr "也可能……他们都够理智，已经自己回家了，只剩咱们三个还在这里犯傻。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do you want to rest while we get this stone moved, then?"
msgstr "那你要不要先歇会儿？我们来搬石头。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hey now. I said I can't make a doorway through it, I didn't say I was gonna sit around "
"and let you do all the work."
msgstr "喂，等等。我只是说没法开门过去，可没说要坐着看你们干活。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You set your jaw and take out your tools. The rock is dense and you're worried about a "
"cave-in, but Redilok extends her hand and begins moving stone with her magic. Smaller "
"boulders lift into the air and are thrown backward, crashing into the cavern walls far "
"behind you."
msgstr ""
"你咬紧牙关，取出工具。岩石坚硬密实，你又担心会再次坍塌。这时，雷迪洛克伸出手，开始用魔法"
"搬动石块。小一些的石块浮到空中，被抛向后方，重重撞在远处的洞壁上。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Please don't blow up, please don't blow up, please don't blo-"
msgstr "千万别炸，千万别炸，千万别……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Whew..."
msgstr "呼……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The three of you make short work of the blockage and climb out of the caverns through "
"what appears to have been a natural entrance to the cave system. The sun is just "
"beginning to set over the western horizon, which initially gives you pause. It'd taken "
"a while to get out of the caves, but the Soulsmiths are on foot as well, many of which "
"are injured. There's a good chance they'd have to stop nearby.\n"
"\n"
"You and [Companion Name] see it at the same time. A thin trail of smoke in this "
"distance, not too far from you. A camp, it has to be."
msgstr ""
"三人合力，很快清开了堵路的碎石，随后沿着一处似乎是天然形成的洞口，爬出了地下洞窟。西边的"
"太阳刚开始落下。你望着天色，心里一沉。从洞里出来确实耽搁了一阵，可炼魂师也只能靠双脚赶"
"路，其中不少人还受了伤。他们很可能得在附近停下来。\n"
"\n"
"你和[Companion Name]几乎同时看见了。不远处，一缕细烟正袅袅升起。营地。一定是他们的营地。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Either of you any good at trackin'?"
msgstr "你们谁会追踪？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... ugh. This is all a bit overwhelmin' for me."
msgstr "我……唉。这外头真让我有点吃不消。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The sun's so bright... grass is too smelly. Dwarves belong in the ground, not out in "
"all this mess."
msgstr "太阳太晃眼……草味儿也太冲。矮人就该待在地下，不该跑来这种乱七八糟的地方。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Yes, but we don't need to be. They clearly didn't think they'd be followed, because "
"they've set up camp just over the hill."
msgstr "会，不过眼下用不着。他们显然没想到有人会追来，就在山坡那头扎了营。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well then, let's get after 'em!"
msgstr "那还等什么，追上去！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We will. You're going to stay put. I promise you we'll get him back."
msgstr "我们去。你留在这里。我保证，一定把他带回来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're giving me an order?"
msgstr "你在教我做事？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm fine. Don't need any babyin'."
msgstr "我没事。用不着把我当小孩子照顾。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm not asking. It seems like you'll hardly make the trek to their camp, let alone be "
"ready for another fight."
msgstr "这事没得商量。你连走到他们营地都够呛，怎么再打一场？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Well, course I'm a little tired. I got my arm blown off and half the royal court got "
"butchered in front of me, then they stood back up and tried to gnaw on me."
msgstr ""
"是，我当然累了。胳膊被炸没了，半个皇室的人死在我眼前，接着又爬起来，想扑过来啃我。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Speaking of you arm... you should tend to that wound, because your wrappings are "
"already coming undone."
msgstr "说到胳膊……你该重新包扎了，布条都快散了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We've got this, alright?"
msgstr "交给我们，好吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Redilok jabs her stump towards [Companion Name] and looks like she's about to say "
"something protest before she realizes she's dripping blood on her boot. She sits with a "
"grumble and waves you off. That's about as good of a blessing as you figure you're "
"going to get.\n"
"\n"
"As you get closer to camp, the two of you start to move more carefully, crawling on "
"your stomachs through the plain's waist-high grass. The Soulsmiths may not have "
"expected you to make it through the cave-in, but that didn't stop them from protecting "
"themselves by littering the ground with volatile runes. [Companion Name] crawls towards "
"one, trying to slowly pry it out of the ground with her knife.\n"
"\n"
"Slowly but surely, she wiggles it out of the ground, then passes it back to you, then "
"moves onto the next one. As tempting as it may be to keep it for later, keeping a small "
"pile of bombs in your backpack it bound to lead to an untimely end. You'll have to "
"carefully destroy them.\n"
"\n"
"You roughly know how the magic works from your time creating similar charges with Gloob "
"way back in Azamire, but these are far more complex."
msgstr ""
"雷迪洛克朝[Companion Name]一挥断臂，正要反驳，却发现血正滴在自己的靴子上。她嘟囔着坐下"
"来，挥手让你们走。能让她这样点头，已经算不错了。\n"
"\n"
"靠近营地后，你们放轻动作，伏在地上，穿过平原上齐腰高的草丛。炼魂师或许没想到你们能穿过坍"
"塌的通道，却也没有疏于防备，沿途埋了不少不稳定的符文。[Companion Name]爬到其中一枚旁边，"
"试着用小刀将它慢慢撬出来。\n"
"\n"
"她一点点松动符文，小心取出，递到你手里，又爬向下一枚。留着以后用确实不错，可背着一包炸弹"
"到处跑，迟早要把自己送上天。你得小心地毁掉它们。\n"
"\n"
"当初在阿扎米尔，你和格鲁布做过类似的爆炸符文，大致知道其中的魔法原理。可眼前这些，复杂得"
"多。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They have to pay."
msgstr "他们必须付出代价。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Who... was that?"
msgstr "那……是谁？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As [Companion Name] very delicately extracts the volatile runes and passed them off, "
"you slowly wither away their power. It's a nerve-wrecking process, and you feel time "
"moving by glacially slow as you crawl closer and closer towards the Soulsmith's camp.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually, you find yourself just outside the camp. You look over the wretched "
"summoners, and one stands out among the elites: An elderly woman whose robes are "
"instead lined with light strips of blue and green instead of gold. Someone important, "
"doubtlessly, though you don't remember seeing her during the attack on the Linking. "
"Dozing by the fire, patrolling around the slug monster, and even cozying up with a few "
"resting cultists are a dozen or so large wolf-like creatures the Soulsmiths seem fond "
"of. These ones are a lot larger than those they attacked Azamire with, though. Watching "
"one of them nuzzle one of the murderers and seemingly beg for a scrap of food... makes "
"you feel strange. These creatures may be summoned beasts, but they are alive and maybe "
"even close with those who brought them to life. \n"
"\n"
"Back in the tunnels, the monsters ended the lives of dozens of dwarves, but it's not "
"like they had a choice. You know as much from the creatures you've summoned yourself. "
"You will them to do something, and they obey. \n"
"\n"
"You'll try to end them quickly.\n"
"\n"
"You pry your eyes away and find Prince Cintak's corpse, still pinned to the slug "
"creature by the black metal blade he was stabbed with. [Companion Name] scoots close "
"and whispers to you."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name]小心翼翼地挖出符文，递给你，你则一点点消去其中的魔力。每一步都让人提心吊"
"胆。你们缓缓爬向炼魂师的营地，只觉得时间慢得难熬。\n"
"\n"
"终于，你们来到了营地外围。你扫视着那些可憎的召唤师，发现精锐之中有个人格外显眼。那是个年"
"老妇人，长袍上镶着浅蓝与浅绿色饰边，而非其他人的金边。她无疑是个重要人物，可你不记得在接"
"轨庆典遇袭时见过她。营地里还有十几头硕大的狼形生物，看来炼魂师对它们颇为偏爱。有的在火堆"
"旁打盹，有的绕着蛞蝓怪物巡行，还有几头亲昵地依偎在休息的教徒身边。不过，这些比当初袭击阿"
"扎米尔的那些大得多。你看着其中一头蹭着一个杀人凶手，像是在讨食，心里……有种说不出的滋"
"味。\n"
"\n"
"在隧道里，这些怪物杀死了几十个矮人，可它们也没有选择。你自己召唤过生物，清楚这一点。你要"
"它们做什么，它们就会照办。\n"
"\n"
"你会尽量给它们一个痛快。你移开视线，找到了辛塔克王子的躯体。他仍被那把黑色金属利刃钉在蛞"
"蝓怪物身上。[Companion Name]挪近了些，在你耳边低声问道。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Why'd they take him, and only him?"
msgstr "他们为什么抓他，而且只抓他一个？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't know. The Soulsmiths were able to control those dead Dwarves during the "
"Linking, maybe it has something to do with that?"
msgstr "我不知道。接轨庆典上，炼魂师能操控那些死去的矮人，也许跟这个有关？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Figure they'll tell us if we ask?"
msgstr "你说，问他们会说吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'd have to leave one alive for that."
msgstr "那就得留个活口了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Guess not then."
msgstr "那还是算了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hey, [Player Name]?"
msgstr "喂，[Player Name]？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I didn't want to ask in front of the princess..."
msgstr "刚才当着公主的面，我没好意思问……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do you think the prince is still alive?"
msgstr "你觉得王子还活着吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...Well, we lived through the explosion and we're made of flesh. He's made of stone and "
"magma..."
msgstr "……咱们是血肉之躯，爆炸都没把咱们炸死。他可是岩石和岩浆做的……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Guess it's a good thing we didn't save some of those explosive runes then, huh? "
"Wouldn't have minded putting them to good use."
msgstr "这么说，刚才没留下几枚爆炸符文，倒是好事了？我还真想拿那些东西好好招呼他们一下。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "If he is alive, and then we blew him up..."
msgstr "万一他还活着，却被咱们炸死了……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well... we'd be lucky if we were only banished from both Dwarven kingdoms."
msgstr "那……两国要是只把咱们驱逐出境，都算走运了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"[Companion Name] grimaces at the thought. After a moment, she turns her attention "
"towards the camp. She nods towards the Soulsmiths, and you nod back. No point in "
"waiting."
msgstr ""
"[Companion Name]一想到那场面，便龇了龇牙。片刻后，她重新望向营地。她朝炼魂师的方向点点"
"头，你也点头回应。没必要再等了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You clash against the Soulsmith Elites, knowing that they're going to use their "
"summoned creatures to frontline for them like they did with the undead back during the "
"Linking. As the elites fall, the vessel attached to the slug monster whirrs to life and "
"bathes the area in flashes of green light, and the elites rise again. It doesn't stop "
"you.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually, the monster runs out of bodies to throw at you, and the leader of this band "
"of Soulsmiths throws herself at you directly, but even she falls. As you strike the "
"killing blow, she commands the slug beast to escape, then falls silent in the tall "
"grass of the plains. Following the orders of its master, the beast tears through the "
"field, slimy arms tearing chunks out of the ground as it scuttles north. You keep pace "
"with it, barely, but when you or [Companion] strike it, your weapons bounce off it, "
"it's thick flesh seemingly resistant to conventional weaponry.\n"
"\n"
"Suddenly, Prince Cintak stirs. It's hard to tell if the man is trying to free himself, "
"or if his corpse is just being flung about, but sure enough, he is able to sink his "
"feet into the monster's meat and push. The black metal sword that pinned him to the "
"beast slides out from it's body with a nauseating squelch and the prince tumbles to the "
"ground. Both you and [Companion Name] let the monster run, quickly attending to the "
"prince instead. He lives, though the weapon that bound him to the slug is still firmly "
"stuck within his stone body. For now, you're just happy he's in one piece. You watch as "
"the Soulsmith's Shambling Beast drags itself far to the north and wish you could give "
"chase, but it's a problem for another day.\n"
"\n"
"Both of the royals support one another as the four of you head back down into the "
"tunnels to reunite with the rest of the survivors. The molten Flamberians cheer with "
"relief at the sight of their prince and surround him, offering to help tend his wounds "
"or swear revenge on those who attacked the Linking. The Nalidasi greet the princess "
"much the same. The wounded have been tended to through a mix of cauterization and "
"sterilization from the party's booze, and many of the decorative tapestries have been "
"torn to fashion bandages.\n"
"\n"
"Once everyone is settled, the magically inclined amongst the Nalidasi join together and "
"open a large doorway in the wall of the Stoneway tunnel, bringing you right to the "
"smoking crater that was once the station you left from. Stone buildings all around you "
"have been leveled by a blast that far outweighs the Soulsmith's attack on the Linking. "
"Now you know what they did with the Stoneglide.\n"
"\n"
"Both the Archivist and king Oyadazminis look upon the blast sight with anger and pain, "
"but then relief upon seeing your group step out from the ashes. The man's eyes are wet "
"with tears as he embraces his daughter, originally having feared the worst. He pulls "
"you aside after breaking apart from the princess, and begs for your aid. He promises "
"access to the Archive, the treasury, and whatever else you may desire in exchange for "
"purging the Soulsmith blight from the land. Despite the Archivist trying in vain to "
"slightly temper the king's impassioned promises of remuneration, his resolve is "
"similarly hardened.\n"
"\n"
"Koganusan is going to war, and you will help guide them to victory."
msgstr ""
"你冲向炼魂师精锐，知道他们一定会像接轨庆典上驱使亡者那样，让召唤兽挡在前面。精锐们接连倒"
"下，蛞蝓怪物背上的容器却嗡嗡启动，绿光不断扫过营地，让他们再次站了起来。可你没有停手。\n"
"\n"
"终于，怪物再也找不到能驱使的尸体。这队炼魂师的首领亲自扑了上来，却也没能撑住。你给出致命"
"一击时，她命令蛞蝓野兽逃走，随后倒在平原的高草中，再无声息。野兽遵从主人的命令，飞快地向"
"北逃窜。黏滑的手臂不断扒扯地面，掀起一块块泥土。你们勉强追得上它，可无论你还是"
"[Companion]，武器砍上去都会被弹开。那身厚实的血肉，似乎根本不怕寻常兵刃。\n"
"\n"
"忽然，辛塔克王子动了。起初，你分不清他是在挣扎，还是身体被怪物颠得乱晃。可很快，他便将双"
"脚蹬进怪物的血肉里，用力一撑。钉住他的黑色金属剑从野兽体内拔了出来，发出一声令人作呕的黏"
"响。王子随即摔落在地。你和[Companion Name]顾不上再追怪物，赶紧去查看王子的情况。他还活"
"着，只是先前将他钉在蛞蝓身上的武器，仍牢牢插在他的岩石身躯里。眼下，能把他完整地救回来，"
"你已经很庆幸了。你望着炼魂师那头跛行兽一路向北逃远，恨不得追上去。可它的账，只能留到以后"
"再算。\n"
"\n"
"王子和公主互相搀扶着，你们四个重返地下通道，与其他幸存者会合。见王子平安归来，岩浆流动的"
"弗拉姆贝里矮人终于松了口气，欢呼着围上前。有的要替他处理伤口，有的发誓要向袭击庆典的凶手"
"讨回血债。纳里达西矮人也同样围住了公主。伤员已经得到了救治：伤口用灼烧止血，再拿庆典上的"
"酒消毒，许多装饰用的挂毯也被撕成了绷带。\n"
"\n"
"等众人安顿妥当，纳里达西人中擅长魔法的几位合力施法，在石道隧道的墙上打开一扇大门，将你们"
"直接带回出发的车站。可那里如今只剩下一个冒烟的大坑。周围的石砌建筑全被夷为平地。这场爆"
"炸，比炼魂师在接轨庆典上制造的那场猛烈得多。现在你知道，他们把石板滑行者开回来做什么"
"了。\n"
"\n"
"典藏官和奥亚达兹米尼斯国王望着废墟，满脸愤怒与悲痛。见你们一行从灰烬中走出来，两人才终于"
"露出释然的神情。国王原本已做好了最坏的打算，此刻一把抱住女儿，眼里满是泪水。松开公主后，"
"他把你拉到一旁，恳求你出手相助。只要能将炼魂师这祸害从世上铲除，他愿意向你开放典藏馆、国"
"库，答应你想要的一切。典藏官试图劝国王冷静些，别一时激动许下太多报酬，却没能劝住。不过，"
"论起对付炼魂师的决心，他也丝毫不逊。\n"
"\n"
"科加努桑即将开战，而你将协助他们赢得这场战争。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ24"
msgstr "MQ24"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Repairing What Remains - The Soulsmiths successfully hijacked the Stoneglide and loaded "
"it with explosives while those attending the Linking were preoccupied on all sides by "
"assailants. Their efforts resulted in a massive swathe of Koganusan being reduced to "
"rubble. Any amount of relief will go a long way towards caring for the populace."
msgstr ""
"重建家园——接轨庆典遭到围攻时，炼魂师趁众人无暇分身，劫走石板滑行者，在上面装满了爆炸物。"
"科加努桑大片城区因此被炸成废墟。如今，能多帮上一点，就能让受灾的民众少吃一点苦。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Her house simply isn't enough. How about a proper cookhouse? Maybe she'll be able to "
"get some help then, too?"
msgstr ""
"光靠她家那间厨房，实在忙不过来。不如建个像样的食堂？这样也方便别人来搭把手，对吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Hopefully this will work a bit better than her home."
msgstr "希望这里能比她家更施展得开。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"King Oyadazminis and the Archivist move with purpose through the ruined market district "
"of Koganusan, handing out food to those who lost their homes and businesses, comforting "
"others, and lending a hand where they can. Though it's a small comfort to those "
"figuring out how to go on, it's still more than enough to get some following in their "
"footsteps if they're able. The pair catch your eye and rush over after excusing "
"themselves from a small group of young dwarves."
msgstr ""
"奥亚达兹米尼斯国王和典藏官正忙着在受灾的集市区奔走。他们给失去住所和店铺的人分发食物，安"
"慰惊魂未定的民众，哪里需要，就去哪里搭把手。对那些连往后日子该怎么过都不知道的人来说，这"
"些或许还远远不够。但看见他们忙前忙后，一些尚有余力的民众也跟着行动起来。两人看见你们，便"
"向身旁的几个矮人孩子告辞，快步走了过来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I never thought there'd be a day where I'm pleased to see two humans waiting for me, "
"but these are trying times. "
msgstr "没想到啊，我居然也有这么盼着见到两个人类的时候。不过，如今确实是难关当头。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I haven't had the chance to properly thank you for returning my daughter to me, and "
"unfortunately I am rather tied down at present."
msgstr "你们把我女儿平安带了回来，我还没来得及好好道谢。可眼下，实在脱不开身。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We can see that. It feels rare to see someone of your station handling a crisis hands "
"on."
msgstr "我们看得出来。像您这样身份的人，出了事还能亲自来帮忙，确实少见。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Would you rather I leave it to those beneath me?"
msgstr "难道你更希望我把事情全丢给手下？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"No, not at all. If anything, I find it refreshing, and it's clear your people do too."
msgstr "不，当然不是。恰恰相反，我觉得这样很好。您的子民显然也这么想。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just wish I could have prevented it in the first place..."
msgstr "只可惜，我没能阻止这一切……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...I wish [Companion Name] and I could have done more."
msgstr "……我也希望，当时我和[Companion Name]能多做些什么。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Excuse me for speaking out of turn, but from the reports I've seen, it sounds as though "
"there wouldn't have been a single survivor were it not for your efforts."
msgstr "恕我插一句。根据我看到的报告，要不是二位奋力相救，恐怕一个人都活不下来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We owe you quite the debt, but it'll be some time before we can properly return the "
"favor."
msgstr "这份恩情，我们记着。只是要报答二位，恐怕还得等一阵子。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We're not worried about it in the slightest, we're just trying to do what we can to "
"prepare to drive the Soulsmiths out of here for good."
msgstr "不用惦记着报答。我们只想尽力做好准备，把炼魂师彻底赶出去。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You have my blessing and what I can spare of my men, though free hands are in short "
"supply."
msgstr "我全力支持。能抽出来的人手，都可以交给你们，不过眼下实在是处处缺人。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Speaking of which... If you find yourself in need of a bit more than I can offer..."
msgstr "说到这个……要是我这边的人手不够……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm sure that the townsfolk would be even more willing to lend a hand with a bit of "
"food in their bellies, or if you're able to help cure what ails them."
msgstr "不妨先帮镇民们填饱肚子，治好伤病。等缓过劲来，他们一定也愿意出份力。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm sure we can figure something out, can't we [Player Name]?"
msgstr "咱们总能想出办法的，对吧，[Player Name]？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Not sure where to start, you decide on the easiest of the options you can think of. "
"Food. Easy to make in bulk, and something that everyone needs. You ask around until you "
"hear of a kindly woman named Zotty, who has been taking care of as many of the "
"districts kids as she can. From what you gather, she was a baker, but her business was "
"destroyed in the attack, a story like many others in Koganusan. When you visit her "
"house on the edge of the ruined district, you see a line of several kids line up by the "
"door, each of them getting a small but well-seasoned portion of stew and a bit of "
"bread.\n"
"\n"
"Zotty is a bit wary of you at first, but your reputations proceed you both, and she "
"simply says that any help you can offer is more than enough. It's clear she doesn't "
"expect much, but you hope to prove her wrong."
msgstr ""
"你一时不知道从哪儿入手，便决定先做件最容易想到的事。给大家弄些吃的。一次能做上许多，又是"
"人人都缺不了的。打听了一圈，你们听说有位叫佐蒂的好心妇人，正在尽力照顾这一带的孩子。她原"
"本开着一家面包店，袭击过后，店没了。如今的科加努桑，像她这样的人还有很多。她家就在受灾街"
"区边上。你们找到那里时，门口正排着几个孩子。每人都领到一小份香喷喷的炖菜，外加一点面"
"包。\n"
"\n"
"佐蒂起初还有些提防你们，不过也早就听说了你们的事。她只说，不管能帮多少，她都领情。她显然"
"没指望你们能做太多。你想，这回可得让她刮目相看。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#. Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Do we just plant these in the ground or..?"
msgstr "这些直接埋进土里就行，还是……？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The devastation left by the Soulsmith attack has both fortunately and unfortunately "
"left behind no small number of plots free of their original buildings. All it takes is "
"a small chat with the king and one of them is requisitioned from its deceased owner and "
"then attributed to the two of you. You draft up and begin construction on a sizeable "
"cookhouse, capable of feeding a large portion of those displaced by the attack, and "
"giving new purpose to a few as well, should they choose to help Zotty.\n"
"\n"
"Building the structure goes much faster than expected. When townsfolk see you working "
"on the structure, many come to help for any number of reasons. Dwarven pride, giving "
"back to their community, or even trying to help the two of you in return for saving as "
"many as you could at the Linking. Before you know it, the dwarven cookhouse stands tall "
"amidst the rubble, ready to feed those in need. Zotty admires the building with her "
"hands on her hips, save for a couple small dabs at her eyes when she thinks you aren't "
"looking."
msgstr ""
"炼魂师毁掉了不少房屋，倒也留下了大片空地。虽然眼下用得上，你却实在高兴不起来。你跟国王简"
"单说了说打算，他便将一块主人已经遇难的地皮征用，交给你们。你们画好图纸，动手建起一间大食"
"堂。有了它，许多因袭击而无家可归的人便能吃上饭。愿意来帮佐蒂的，也能重新找点事情做。\n"
"\n"
"房子盖得比预想中快得多。镇民们见你们忙活，纷纷赶来搭手。有的不想让矮人的本事输给人类，有"
"的想为街坊做点事，还有的听说你们在接轨庆典上救了许多人，想借此还一份人情。没多久，一座食"
"堂便在废墟间立了起来，只等开火做饭，招呼有需要的人进门。佐蒂叉着腰，望着新食堂看了又看。"
"趁你们不注意，她还偷偷抹了几下眼角。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"When I said I wanted a spot of help, I was expecting a bag of tubers, or maybe a scrap "
"of meat."
msgstr "我说想请人帮点忙，想着能拿来一袋薯块，或者拿点肉来，就挺好了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Didn't expect you to drop a whole bleedin' building on my head!"
msgstr "谁知道你们一出手，竟给我盖了整栋房子！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Hopefully it'll be a good starting point. Lots of folks from around town pitched in, "
"and there's a ton of cookware and raw foods as well."
msgstr "有了这个开头，往后应该就好办了。城里不少人都来帮过忙，厨具和食材也备了不少。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's more than I'll be able to handle alone. You two bring an army to help me keep the "
"place runnin' too?"
msgstr "这么大的地方，我一个人可顾不过来。怎么，你们还给我备了一大帮人，等着来干活？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Not quite, but we figure if it's anything like building the place, once you start "
"whipping up meals, others will start leaping over the counter to help you out."
msgstr "那倒没有。不过盖房子的时候，大家不都来了？等你这边一开火，肯定又有人抢着来搭手。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You think I'm lettin' just any schmuck make food for the town?"
msgstr "你当我这厨房是谁都能进的？做出来的饭，可是要给大家吃的！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm pleased the Nalidasi have left such an impression on you as to make you think we "
"can do anything."
msgstr "你们觉得纳里达西人无所不能，我听着是挺高兴。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But let me tell you, cooking is not a strongsuit of our kind."
msgstr "可唯独做饭这事，我们还真不在行。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We've seen a few displays of... less proper ettique, but you all seem to take such "
"pride in your craftsdwarfship, I almost find it hard to believe the Nalidasi don't "
"treat food the same."
msgstr ""
"我们是见过你们吃饭时……不怎么讲究。不过，你们那么看重自己的手艺，我还以为做饭也不会含糊"
"呢。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Let's just say that there's a reason you've seen our crafts and not our fine dining "
"experiences."
msgstr "这么说吧，你们听说过纳里达西的好手艺，可听说过纳里达西有什么好菜吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I swear, folks are more inclined to start chewing gravel and wash it down with ale than "
"to enjoy a proper meal half the time."
msgstr "这里的人啊，有时候宁可嚼把碎石，再灌口麦酒，也懒得好好吃顿饭。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I was tryin' to do my best to fix that before my bakery got blown to bits."
msgstr "面包店还没被炸掉的时候，我一直想改改他们这毛病。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Any ideas on where we could find you some help, then?"
msgstr "那该去哪儿给你找帮手？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We just gotta give folks something they cannot possibly mess up. Cobblestone Soup."
msgstr "得先找道菜，简单到谁来都做不坏。卵石汤。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...doesn't seem all that much better than the gravel you mentioned..."
msgstr "……听着跟吃碎石也没好到哪儿去……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Zotty lets out a hearty chuckle before digging in her pocket and handing over a pouch "
"of what looks like small bits of quartz. She assures you that they'll grow into "
"Stonemelons, which are used in a soup that's hearty and filling, and practically "
"impossible to mess up."
msgstr ""
"佐蒂哈哈大笑，从口袋里掏出一只小袋子递给你。袋子里的东西，看着像一小粒一小粒的石英。她让"
"你放心，说这些种下去就能长出石瓜。拿石瓜煮汤，味道好，又顶饱，几乎不可能失手。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "This feels a little unorthodox."
msgstr "这做法还真没见过。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I should probably wash my pickaxe."
msgstr "我是不是该先洗洗镐头？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The stonemelons grow strong with little supervision, which doesn't surprise you based "
"on the name. Continuing to live up to their title, these small boulder-like melons look "
"nearly identical to any ordinary rock you'd see out and about, except that they're "
"almost perfectly spherical orbs. They're heavy, but you manage to lug your harvest back "
"to Zotty's new cookhouse."
msgstr ""
"石瓜不用怎么照料，就长得结结实实。想到它们的名字，你倒也不觉得奇怪。它们长得也确实像石"
"头。要不是一个个圆得出奇，混在路边的石块里，你大概根本认不出来。这些瓜沉得很，你们还是把"
"收成一趟趟搬回了佐蒂的新食堂。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Proper dwarven farmers, the lot of you! Hardly seen any Stonemelons this size in my "
"days, almost as good as my ol' pappy Xon could grow."
msgstr ""
"行啊，你们都能当矮人农夫了！这么大的石瓜，我可没见过几回。都快赶上我老爹克森种的了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm glad you're impressed, though almost surprised you could tell them apart from any "
"old rock."
msgstr "你满意就好。不过说真的，你怎么认得出这些是瓜，不是石头？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Clear as day to my dwarvern eyes, surprised you don't see it."
msgstr "我们矮人一眼就看得出来，跟大白天看东西一样清楚。你们看不出来才奇怪呢。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Clear as day? But we don't get any sunlight down here..."
msgstr "大白天？可这底下也晒不着太阳啊……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's awfully clear though, ain't it?"
msgstr "反正看得清清楚楚，不是吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I guess so..."
msgstr "也是……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, how do we get these open? Should have plenty of knives around."
msgstr "那这些瓜怎么打开？这里总不缺刀吧。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Our knives are for cuttin' up veggies and carvin' out meat. Step aside."
msgstr "刀是拿来切菜切肉的。让开点。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Zotty grabs a pickaxe from the wall she seems to have brought out for just this "
"purpose. She brings it down on the melon several times to no avail - to the point "
"you're concerned you brought her an actual rock - until eventually, the melon cracks "
"open like a geode. Inside, the stonemelon is filled with white flesh, which Zotty then "
"extends out to you. You scrape a bit off and are surprised by its rubbery texture, and "
"the fact that it's almost savory, like smoked meat. Zotty waves her hand towards your "
"pile and gets to work cutting open a few more herself."
msgstr ""
"佐蒂从墙上取下一把镐头，看样子早就为这一刻准备好了。她举镐连敲了几下，石瓜却没什么反应。"
"你正担心自己不会真搬了块石头回来，瓜壳终于裂开，像剖开了一块晶洞石。里面是白色的瓜肉。佐"
"蒂递给你，让你尝尝。你刮下一点放进嘴里。瓜肉弹韧得出奇，竟还带着一股近似熏肉的鲜香。佐蒂"
"朝剩下的石瓜一指，自己也继续动手，又敲开了几个。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "A bit of this, and a bit of that..."
msgstr "这个放一点，那个添一些……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And serve!"
msgstr "上桌！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You do a better job of mashing the stonemelons to bits than splitting them perfectly in "
"half like Zotty does in the beginning until she gives you a few pointers. You slowly "
"but surely make your way through the pile, leaving behind a crime scene that'd inspire "
"fear in all but the bravest of produce."
msgstr ""
"刚开始，你只会把石瓜砸得七零八落，根本做不到像佐蒂那样整整齐齐地劈成两半。经她指点几句"
"后，你才渐渐摸到了门道。你们一点点处理完那堆石瓜，留下一地碎壳残肉。要是蔬果也会害怕，看"
"到这惨案现场，恐怕早就吓得四散奔逃了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The two of you done makin' a mess?"
msgstr "你们俩，霍霍完了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Think so! What do ya do with 'em now?"
msgstr "差不多了！接下来呢？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I ain't just gonna tell ya, I'm gonna show ya."
msgstr "光说你们哪会啊，来，我做给你们看。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I know the two of ya' got some proper worldsaving to go do, but if everyone here "
"starves by the time you get back, what's it for?"
msgstr ""
"我知道，你们还赶着去拯救世界。可要是等你们回来，大伙儿都饿死了，救下来又有什么用？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I won't keep ya long, promise."
msgstr "放心，耽误不了多久。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Zotty starts the stoves and begins carving out the melon flesh, dicing and seasoning it "
"with a handful of herbs. Once her pot of water begin to boil, she tosses the prepared "
"flesh back in, then combines it with some meat and veggies and stirs. Once done, she "
"pours it into the hollowed out shell of the stonemelon and pushes it towards the two of "
"you.\n"
"\n"
"The Nalidasi may not value cooking much, but with food like this, it's sure to change."
msgstr ""
"佐蒂点起炉火，挖出瓜肉，切丁，再抓上一把香草调味。锅里的水一开，她就把备好的瓜肉倒进去，"
"加上肉和蔬菜，一起搅匀。煮好后，她将汤盛进掏空的瓜壳，推到你们面前。\n"
"\n"
"纳里达西人以前或许不把做饭当回事，可吃过这样的东西，想来就该改主意了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Before either you or [Companion Name] can finish cooking your first pots, both Nalidasi "
"and many of the Flamberian survivors from the Linking start trickling into the "
"cookhouse, asking how they can help - in exchange for a bit of food of course - and "
"Zotty begins barking out orders like a trained general. Flamberians heat their bodies "
"and are used as stoves, much to the amusement of both races of dwarves. Zotty moves "
"through the kitchen with purpose, correcting well-intentioned helpers and directing "
"them to watch you and [Companion Name] as examples.\n"
"\n"
"It takes a while, but those in the cookhouse start to produce Cobblestone Soup that "
"Zotty is willing to serve to the long line of hungry survivors of the market district "
"disaster. The two of you do so well Zotty is reluctant to let you go, until King "
"Ozadazminis himself offers himself and the Archivist as replacements during a visit to "
"the building's opening night. Zotty grumbles and mentions that good help is hard to "
"find, but allows to you go after making sure you've both eaten your fill."
msgstr ""
"你和[Companion Name]连各自的第一锅汤都还没做好，就陆续有人走进食堂。既有纳里达西人，也有"
"不少从接轨庆典上逃过一劫的弗拉姆贝里人，都是来问能不能帮忙换口饭吃的。佐蒂立刻指挥起来，"
"架势活像个带惯了兵的将军。弗拉姆贝里人把身体烧热，直接充当炉子。这主意把两边的矮人都逗乐"
"了。佐蒂在厨房里来回忙碌，见谁做得不对就上前指点，还不时让他们看看你和[Companion Name]是"
"怎么做的。\n"
"\n"
"又忙活了一阵，帮手们终于煮出了让佐蒂满意的卵石汤，可以端给门外排着长队、饥肠辘辘的灾民"
"了。你们干得太好，佐蒂实在舍不得放人。直到开张当晚，奥扎达兹米尼斯国王亲自过来，提出由他"
"和典藏官接手你们的活儿，她才答应让你们走。她嘴里还念叨着“好帮手不好找”，又非要看着你们吃"
"饱了饭，才肯放行。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ25"
msgstr "MQ25"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Slug Slayer - There's only one thing you've seen that can pierce the Soulsmith slug "
"monster's thick flesh, and it's currently embeded within the chest of the Flamberian "
"Prince. Surely he's willing to part with it... if he can."
msgstr ""
"蛞蝓屠杀者——炼魂师那头蛞蝓怪物皮肉厚实，你只见过一样东西能刺穿它。偏偏那东西现在还插在弗"
"拉姆贝里王子的胸口。想来王子很乐意把它交给你……只要拔得出来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Should come to a point here, maybe a handle made of..."
msgstr "这头得打尖。至于柄，用什么好呢……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Looks sharp enough to me."
msgstr "我看够锋利了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You wander outside of the room Prince Cintak has been being kept in, but were blocked "
"by Princess Redilok before you could see the man.You and [Companion Name]'s plan is "
"absurd, but if you intend to take down the Shambling Beast, you see no other path "
"forward. You lay it out in detail to Princess Redilok, who blanches at the thought."
msgstr ""
"你来到辛塔克王子的房门外，还没见到他，就被雷迪洛克公主拦了下来。你和[Companion Name]想的"
"这个办法确实离谱，可要杀死那头跛行兽，你们也实在想不出别的路子。你把打算从头到尾说了一"
"遍。雷迪洛克越听，脸色越白。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You want to what?"
msgstr "你们想干什么？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll be careful, I promise."
msgstr "我们会小心的，我保证。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, right. You'll carefully rip the spike of unknown material out of Prince Cintak's "
"chest and close him up before he bleeds out."
msgstr ""
"哦，对。你们要“小心”地从辛塔克王子的胸口拔出一根连是什么做的都不知道的尖刺，再赶在他的血"
"流干之前把伤口合上。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Which of you is the surgeon, hm? I'm sure my father has an axe or something you could "
"use..."
msgstr "敢问二位，哪位会做手术？我父亲那儿肯定有斧子，你们借一把用不就好了……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"...I know the concept is scary, but we're going to ask the prince what kind of... wound "
"care his people even use."
msgstr "……我知道这事听着吓人。我们打算先问问王子，他们族人受了伤……通常都是怎么治的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We've banadaged ourselves up countless times, but I'm not really sure where we'd start "
"with someone made of stone and lava."
msgstr ""
"咱们给自己包扎过多少回了，可要给一个浑身都是岩石和熔岩的人治伤，我还真不知道该从哪儿下"
"手。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And we're not going to be the ones operating on him, don't worry."
msgstr "你放心，主刀的也不是我们。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I remember being introduced to someone at the Linking that seemed to be a big-shot in "
"Flamberian society because they were a doctor."
msgstr "我记得接轨庆典上，有人给我介绍过一位弗拉姆贝里医生。看得出来，他在族里很有分量。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If he's still around, he would have come back with the rest of the survivors. He'd be "
"the surgeon."
msgstr "他要是还活着，应该已经跟其他幸存者一起回来了。到时候请他主刀。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...fine."
msgstr "……好吧。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"But if the prince doesn't make it, I'll see you both tried for treason. You won't leave "
"Koganusan alive."
msgstr ""
"但王子要是有个三长两短，我就以叛国罪把你们两个送上法庭。你们别想活着走出科加努桑。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Redilok seems to mull on the idea, before stepping aside and opening the door to his "
"room. Prince Cintak is in rough shape. He put on a brave front while trekking back to "
"the Dwarven capital, but the events of the Linking have doubtlessly worn away at the "
"man. His breaths are labored, and the twisted black metal rod peircing his chest seems "
"to have fused more with him. Despite his state, he still manages a smile as the three "
"of you enter the room. After catching him up on current events, you detail your reason "
"for visiting. You want to pry the metal from his chest and fashion it into a weapon to "
"kill the Shambling Beast the Soulsmiths attacking the Linking with.\n"
"\n"
"He digests the words for only a moment before praising the idea, reiterating that it "
"seems to be the only thing that's pieced the beast's flesh, and that he's more than "
"willing to help and details what he knows. First-aid for Flamberians seems to be more "
"akin to working on a forged good than a living being, but you suppose that that makes "
"sense for a being comprised of stone and magma. His people use emerald-tipped blades "
"that are magically enhanced to cut into thier rocky exteriors. Then, for a wound "
"that'll be as severe as his, a concoction of golden stardust and sporlyle would be able "
"to help his body seal the wound, but he'd need to be hammered closed, like working on a "
"platebody.\n"
"\n"
"Princess Rodilok nearly faints as the man details beating on his chest with hammers to "
"close the wound.\n"
"\n"
"You decide to search for your doctor first. He's easy to find, as the man has been "
"helping treat some of the more severely wounded folks in the Nalidasi market district, "
"which has gone a long ways towards lightening some of concern that the Flamberians were "
"behind the attack. When you detail your plan for working on the prince, Doctor "
"Hacksmith is able to draw up a detailed schematic for this emerald blade that Cintak "
"mentioned, but all of the doctor's handwriting is next to indesipherable. At least the "
"diagram is detailed enough for you to work on."
msgstr ""
"雷迪洛克思量片刻，终于让到一旁，替你们打开了房门。辛塔克王子的情况很不好。一路走回矮人都"
"城时，他硬撑着没让人看出异样。可接轨庆典上那一番折腾，终究还是耗尽了他的力气。他每喘一口"
"气都很吃力。穿透胸膛的那根黑色金属杆弯曲扭结，似乎比先前更深地长进了他的身体。即便如此，"
"见你们三人进来，他还是挤出了一丝笑容。你先把近来的事告诉了他，随后才道明来意。你们想取出"
"他胸口的金属，拿来打造一件武器，杀死炼魂师在接轨庆典上放出的那头跛行兽。\n"
"\n"
"王子只想了一会儿，便说这是个好主意。毕竟，据他所知，刺穿过野兽皮肉的也就这么一样东西。他"
"很乐意帮忙，当即把自己知道的一一道来。听他说来，给弗拉姆贝里人治伤，倒更像是在修补一件锻"
"造好的器物。不过，想到他们的身体本来就是岩石和岩浆，这也说得通。要切开他们坚硬的外层，得"
"用经过魔法强化、刀尖嵌着绿宝石的刀。至于王子这样的重伤，得把金色星尘和斯波里尔调成药水，"
"帮助伤口愈合。光靠药水还不够，还得像修补胸甲那样，用锤子把伤口一点点敲合。\n"
"\n"
"听辛塔克仔细讲到该怎么往他胸口抡锤子，雷迪洛克公主差点没晕过去。\n"
"\n"
"你决定先去找那位医生。人倒是不难找。他一直在纳里达西的集市区救治重伤员。见他这么忙前忙"
"后，原本怀疑袭击是弗拉姆贝里人所为的人们，也渐渐打消了疑虑。你把救治王子的打算告诉哈克史"
"密斯博士，他便照辛塔克的描述，画出了那把绿宝石刀的详图。只是博士写的那些字，你几乎一个也"
"认不出来。好在图纸画得够细，光看图也能把刀打出来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I wonder how Flamberian bodies handle stardust..."
msgstr "也不知道弗拉姆贝里人的身体碰上星尘，会有什么反应……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Can't imagine something like this would have a regenerative effect on human flesh... "
"Maybe the opposite."
msgstr "换作人，这东西恐怕没法让伤口愈合……没准还会起反作用。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"When king Oyadazminis said that you'd have the backing of the whole kingdom when it "
"came to getting them ready to go against the Soulsmiths, you didn't expect the level of "
"support he decided to show. When one of his aids found you and [Companion Name] "
"hammering out prototypes of the emerald tool in the palance courtyard, Oyadazminis "
"himself had his people gather your things and walked you through the capitol until you "
"found a lovely, well-stocked workshop built within the stalk of a large plant that "
"you've never seen anywhere outside of the cavern. The workshop itself is outfitted with "
"dozens of tools and workstations you couldn't even begin to guess at the function of. "
"He bought the workshop from the owner, who tried to protest up until the kings' aids "
"draped him in jeweled necklaces and sacks of gold were dropped in front of him until he "
"couldn't see over the pile. In exchange, him and his workers found a perfect balance of "
"handing you tools before you even asked for them, pointers in working with emerald, and "
"giving you space when you needed it.\n"
"\n"
"After a few dozen failed attempts, you finally create a blade that was strong enough to "
"chip away at stone with nary a scratch, and that is without the magical enhancements "
"the prince mentioned. The former workshop owner - an older dwarf with gold-blonde hair "
"who introduced himself as Kajc -  takes the blade and plunges it into the wall, before "
"leaning back and stroking his chin."
msgstr ""
"奥亚达兹米尼斯国王说过，只要是为迎战炼魂师做准备，整个王国都会支持你们。你却没料到，他竟"
"肯帮忙帮到这个地步。一名侍从看见你和[Companion Name]在王宫庭院里试打绿宝石刀，国王便亲自"
"赶来，叫人收拾好你们的东西，领着你们穿过都城，来到一间精巧的工坊。工坊就建在一株巨型植物"
"的茎干里，材料工具一应俱全。那种植物，你还没在这座洞窟以外的地方见过。工坊里足有几十种工"
"具和工作台，许多你连用途都猜不出来。国王当场买下了工坊。坊主起初还想推辞，可侍从已经把宝"
"石项链一串串挂到他脖子上，又把一袋袋金币往他面前摞。等他连钱堆后面的东西都看不见了，也就"
"不再推辞了。有坊主和工人们搭把手，你干起活来顺手多了。往往还没等你开口，要用的工具就递到"
"了手边。打磨绿宝石有什么窍门，他们会顺口提点几句；看你想自己试试，便由着你慢慢琢磨。\n"
"\n"
"试坏几十把之后，你终于做出一把能削下石屑、刀刃却几乎不留划痕的刀。这还没算上王子所说的魔"
"法强化。工坊原来的主人是个上了年纪的金发矮人，自我介绍时说叫凯克。他接过刀，一把扎进墙"
"里，随后退开些，摸着下巴端详起来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Now, that's a fine tool you've got there, folks."
msgstr "好家伙，你们这把刀打得可真不错。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What'd you say it was for, again?"
msgstr "刚才你们说，这是拿来做什么的？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Eh... it might be better if you don't know."
msgstr "呃……这个嘛，你可能还是不知道的好。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Fine then, keep your secrets."
msgstr "成，不说就不说。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Make sure you come on back here though if you've got more stuff to work on."
msgstr "下回还有东西要打，可得记着上我这儿来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I suppose my workshop is more the king's workshop, so it's not like I'd be able to stop "
"you even if I wanted to."
msgstr "不过，这工坊如今该算国王的了。你们真要来，我想拦也拦不住。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And how do you feel about that?"
msgstr "工坊就这么成了别人的，你舍得吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Oh, it's wonderful! Do you know how long its been since I've had to help make something "
"important?"
msgstr "我？高兴还来不及呢！你们知道，我有多久没帮着做过一件真正要紧的东西了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's just been random bits and bobs for years. A ring here, a golden egg that'll sit on "
"a shelf collecting dust for ages there."
msgstr ""
"这几年，净做些零零碎碎的小玩意儿。今儿打一枚戒指，明儿做一颗金蛋，往架子上一摆，也就剩下"
"落灰了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"At least this fancy poker you've got is going to be used for something. Makes me feel "
"useful."
msgstr "你们这根漂亮的尖家伙，好歹是真要派上用场的。我这把老骨头也算还有点用。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You head back to the palace with your emerald tool and hand it off to the princess, who "
"promises she'll make it capable of withstanding the staggering heat of Cintak's blood. "
"She mentions few things can handle someone as hot as him, and you get the feeling that "
"she stopped talking about his blood a long while ago, but you let her babble, as she's "
"clearly nervous about the whole ordeal of cutting open her not-so-secret love. "
"Eventually she shoos you away, to get you working on the potion that should help seal "
"up the prince once Hacksmith is done cutting the metal out of his body."
msgstr ""
"你把绿宝石刀带回王宫，交给公主。她答应替刀施法，好让它经得住辛塔克血液的惊人高温。她还"
"说，像辛塔克这样火热的，能招架得住的可没几个。听到这里，你觉得她早就不只是在说他的血了。"
"你由着她说下去。她对辛塔克的心意，大家早就看出来了。眼下心上人就要挨这一刀，她紧张得话都"
"停不下来。过了一会儿，她便催你们去配药水。等哈克史密斯从王子体内切出那块金属，还得靠这药"
"水帮伤口愈合。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Just... stay still!"
msgstr "别……别动啊！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Finally."
msgstr "总算好了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You come back with the sparkling concoction and bring it into the bedroom-turned-"
"surgery suite. A few Flamberians have joined Doctor Hacksmith, their purpose seemingly "
"to be there to heat up the Prince's body, and then help hammer him closed afterward. "
"The princess presents your emerald blade, now with glowing runestones etched into its "
"hilt. Hacksmith presses one and the blade glows red, waves of heat scorching the air "
"around it. The doctor tests the blade lightly on his own leg, then takes your potion "
"and dribbles a few drops on the wound. Just as easily as the blade cut stone, your "
"elixir quickly helps his rocky flesh knit back together."
msgstr ""
"你带着调好的药水回来，瓶中的药液闪着微光。王子的卧房如今已经成了手术室。几名弗拉姆贝里人"
"也来给哈克史密斯博士搭手。看样子，他们得先让王子的身体热起来，等手术结束，再帮忙把伤口敲"
"合。公主拿出你们打造的绿宝石刀。如今，刀柄上已嵌着几枚刻有符文的石头，正微微发光。哈克史"
"密斯按下其中一枚，刀刃随即烧得通红，扑面而来的热浪连四周的空气都烤得灼烫。博士先在自己腿"
"上轻轻划了一刀，又接过药水，往伤口上滴了几滴。刀刃切开岩石毫不费力，药水也同样见效。转眼"
"间，那道石质皮肉上的伤口便重新合拢。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I think we're about ready to begin."
msgstr "我看，可以开始了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Prince, I apologize that we hardly have an ideal room, staff, or tools to treat you."
msgstr "殿下，这间屋子、我们这点人手，还有手边的器具，都算不上理想，还请您见谅。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Your family is well known to mine, I know I'm in good hands."
msgstr "咱们两家是老相识了。由你来做这个手术，我放心。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'll do my best."
msgstr "我会尽力的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You'd better be alright, Cinny. "
msgstr "小辛，你可不能有事。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You say that when you're worse off than me. You're missing a whole arm."
msgstr "你还说我？你伤得比我重。整条胳膊都没了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But I'm stable. They're practially cutting your heart out!"
msgstr "可我的伤已经稳住了。他们这都快把你的心挖出来了！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Cintak pulls the princess close and whispers something in her ear, which seems to help "
"her settle, and blush. You turn away to let the two of them have their moment, but soon "
"enough, everyone's ferried out of the room.\n"
"\n"
"The surgery is long. Several times you and [Companion Name] have to settle Princess "
"Redilok from interrupting, but she hardly seems that intent on entering. Just the idea "
"of having to wait outside and feeling like she can't help further drives her up the "
"wall.\n"
"\n"
"After multiple hours, you begin to hear loud thuds from the Prince's room. Hammering "
"Cintak's chest back closed sounds lightly terrifying, but you trust the Flamberians "
"know their own anatomy better than you do. Eventually, the door swings open, and "
"Hacksmith declares his work done, before handing you the rock of dark twisted metal. "
"After a quick peek to check in on the Prince, you let Redilok stay with him herself, "
"then head back to the workshop to fashion a weapon out of the weird material."
msgstr ""
"辛塔克把公主拉到身边，在她耳边低声说了几句。她似乎安心了些，脸也红了。你转过身，让他们单"
"独待一会儿。没多久，其余人就都被请到了门外。\n"
"\n"
"手术一直没有结束。好几次，雷迪洛克公主都像是要冲进去，你和[Companion Name]只好劝她冷静。"
"其实，她也未必真想进去打断手术。让她难受的是只能在门外干等，再也帮不上忙。\n"
"\n"
"几个小时后，王子的房间里终于响起一声声沉重的锤击。一想到他们正用锤子把辛塔克的胸口敲回原"
"样，你多少有些心惊。不过，弗拉姆贝里人总比你懂得该怎么医治自己的族人。门终于开了。哈克史"
"密斯宣布手术结束，把取出来的那块黑色金属交到你手上。它扭作一团，看着倒像块石头。你往房里"
"看了一眼，见王子没有大碍，便不再打扰，让雷迪洛克单独陪着他。你带着那块古怪的金属回到工"
"坊，打算把它锻成一件武器。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#. [待复核] Excel 里该行原文已被破坏，译文按行序对应，请核对
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you beat the metal rod into a speartip, something becomes distrubingly clear. The "
"metal that was burried inside the prince is alive. [Companion Name] suggests the name "
"Soulsteel, keeping in line with the Soulsmiths' unoriginal naming conventions, and the "
"name sticks. The dwarves in the workshop are more fascinated than horrified by the "
"material and frequently suggest... unconventional smithing methods to combat the "
"metal's unwillingness to take shape the way you want it to. You try hammering it for "
"hours on end, taking turns with [Companion Name] and Kajc. You try etching it in acid, "
"heating it and cooling it in a way that'd make any other metal crack, all to no avail. "
"The only thing that works is when you... speak with it. The Soulsteel doesn't speak "
"back, but it wavers in all sorts of fashions, communicating in a language you haven't "
"got the slightest clue on how to begin desciphering.\n"
"\n"
"Eventually, you manage to learn its version of positive and negative wiggles, you're "
"able to tell it that you intend to kill off the beast it originally came from, to which "
"it seems thrilled. At least, you think that's what it is trying to communicate to you. "
"It stops resisting being shaped and you're able to use it to make the cutting edge of a "
"long, curved blade. You don't like how the metal seems to shiver whenever it is close "
"to something, but you can't think of any other way to cut through the beast it came "
"from. For now, this will have to do."
msgstr ""
"你一锤一锤地敲着那根金属杆，想把它锻成矛尖。可锤子每落下一次，你心里那个不安的猜测就更真"
"切一分。从王子体内取出的这块金属，是活的。[Companion Name]说，照炼魂师那套没什么新意的取"
"名法，就叫它“魂钢”好了。这个名字就这么定了下来。工坊里的矮人倒没怎么害怕，反而对魂钢着了"
"迷。见它怎么都不肯成形，大家纷纷出起主意，只是那些锻造的法子，一个比一个……别出心裁。你、"
"[Companion Name]和凯克轮流挥锤，一连敲了好几个钟头。你试过用酸蚀刻，又试着把它烧热、骤"
"冷。换了别的金属，这么折腾早就裂了，魂钢却还是老样子。唯一管用的办法，竟然是……跟它说话。"
"魂钢不会开口，却能以各种方式扭动回应。它似乎有一套自己的语言，而你压根不知道该从哪里学"
"起。\n"
"\n"
"摸索了一阵，你总算分得清，怎样扭是点头，怎样扭是摇头。你设法让它明白，你打算杀死它原先寄"
"身的那头野兽。听到这话，它似乎高兴极了。至少，你觉得它想表达的是高兴。这回它终于肯顺着你"
"的锤子成形了。你用它打出一道锋刃，做成了一把长长的弯刀。只要挨近什么东西，魂钢就会微微颤"
"动。这一点你实在喜欢不起来。可要破开那头野兽的皮肉，你也想不出除了用它身上取下的东西，还"
"能有什么别的办法。眼下，就靠这把刀了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ26"
msgstr "MQ26"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Misty Mystery - The Soulsmith's Shambling Beast was last seen dragging its pitiful form "
"north from the center of the Stoneway. As long as it didn't change directions, that'd "
"place it somewhere within the Misty Thicket... an incredibly dense bog covered in a "
"perpectual blanket of mist. The perfect place to go searching for a monster."
msgstr ""
"迷雾寻踪——你最后一次见到炼魂师的跛行兽时，它正拖着身子，从石道中段狼狈地向北逃去。要是它"
"一路没拐弯，现在多半就在迷雾丛林。那是片草木丛生的沼泽，终年不见雾散。要找怪物，这地方可"
"真是再合适不过了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What's going on up here?"
msgstr "上面出什么事了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh my."
msgstr "哎哟。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It feels good to be outside the caverns that hold the Nalidasi capital, but "
"unfortunately, it's not like your planned adventure is going to be particularly fun. "
"You take in a deep breath of fresh air and wipe off a layer of dust that you're sure "
"has been perptually stuck to your body during your subterranean stay, despite your "
"adherance to basic hygenie. You and [Companion Name] take the time to map out the area, "
"lining up your current position with where the Linking took place, and then plotting "
"the trajectory of where the Shambling Beast could have shuffled off to, assuming it "
"stayed the same course across an unknown amount of distance. It should be somewhere "
"within the Misty Thicket, though you can't begin to wager where, you'll just have to "
"deal with that once you get there.\n"
"\n"
"A long shot, but the best you've got, considering the current circumstances."
msgstr ""
"走出纳里达西都城所在的洞窟，能到外面透口气，确实舒服。可惜，接下来要办的事，恐怕没这么让"
"人愉快。你深吸了一口新鲜空气，抹掉身上的一层灰。在地底住的那些日子，你明明也没少洗，可这"
"层灰像是从来就没洗掉过。你和[Companion Name]画出附近的地形，在图上标明你们现在的位置，又"
"找出举行接轨庆典的地方。野兽当时是从那里往北逃的。只要它没换过方向，你们就能循着这条线，"
"大致推算出它的去向。至于它到底走了多远，谁也说不准。照这个方向走，野兽多半进了迷雾丛林。"
"至于它藏在哪儿，只能等到了林子里再慢慢找。\n"
"\n"
"指望这点线索找到它，机会不大。可眼下你们也没有更好的办法。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's... quite a ways away, isn't it?"
msgstr "这地方……够远的啊。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I don't suppose the Nalidasi have a second, smaller, portable Stoneglider, that doesn't "
"need rails, huh?"
msgstr "你说，纳里达西人就没有另一台石板滑行者？小一点，能带着走，最好还不用铺轨道。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It'd be a mix of amazing and terrifying if they did. If I was moving that fast over "
"land, it'd only be a matter of time before I hit something a little too big."
msgstr ""
"真有那东西，坐起来肯定既过瘾又吓人。要是让我开着它在野地里跑，照那个速度，早晚得撞上什么"
"大家伙。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I imagine it'd look a little like a balloon filled with red paint hitting a wall."
msgstr "想想那场面，跟一只灌满红颜料的气球拍在墙上差不多。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe it is best they keep those on rails, eh?"
msgstr "……那还是让它在轨道上跑吧。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's so much distance to cover on foot. We'll have to keep ourselves stocked up along "
"the way."
msgstr "可这么远，全靠两条腿走啊。路上还得随时补给。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Just like travelling to the capitol! Feels like that was so long ago. I won-"
msgstr "跟咱们当初去都城一样！总觉得那都是好久以前的事了。不知道……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Both of you drop into combat position as you hear a shout from the cliffs up above you. "
"Several loud growls and snarls follow, followed by several swears and exclamations of "
"'bad doggy'. You look to [Companion Name] who shrugs and starts climbing the cliffside."
msgstr ""
"上方的崖顶突然传来一声喊叫，你们俩立刻摆出迎战的架势。接着是几声低沉的咆哮，夹杂着骂声，"
"还有人一个劲儿地喊：“坏狗！坏狗！”你看向[Companion Name]。她耸耸肩，动手往崖上爬。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Who's a good monster?"
msgstr "谁是最乖的小怪物呀？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You are! Yes you are!"
msgstr "是你呀！对，就是你！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You weren't too sure what you'd find when you climbed the cliffface, but it wasn't a "
"young Flamberian dwarf being chased by half a dozen Rockwolves. The young man dangles "
"from a twiggy looking tree growing out of the mountainside while Rockwolves jump up to "
"nip at his heels, trying to grab a bite.\n"
"\n"
"The moment that the two of you pull yourselves up over the side, the Rockwolves turn "
"towards you. They snarl and start angling towards the pair of you instead, until a "
"brief moment of familiarity washes over them. A Rockwolf with an outer shell of a sandy-"
"looking stone carefully approaches you, then flips over at your feet in submission. "
"These wolves must have been from the same pack as the one you fought when you first "
"arrived at the Perilous Peaks, it's the only thing that explains their current "
"behavior. The large rock-covered wolves gaze down at you, seemingly waiting for your "
"next move. Some yawn and lay down, or snarl at the Flamberian as he tries to push his "
"way over to you. The Rockwolves are immense creatures, easily twice your size, which "
"make the Flamberian look even smaller in comparison."
msgstr ""
"往上爬的时候，你也说不准崖顶会有什么。可一个年轻的弗拉姆贝里矮人被六头石狼追得四处躲，这"
"你还真没想到。山壁上斜长着一棵细瘦的小树，小伙子就吊在上面。石狼在底下蹿来蹿去，张口去咬"
"他的脚后跟，都想从他身上咬下一块肉。\n"
"\n"
"你们刚翻上崖边，石狼便齐齐转过头来。它们龇着牙朝你们逼近，却又慢慢收了声，像是认出了你"
"们。一头披着砂岩般外甲的石狼试探着走近，往你脚边一躺，翻过身露出了肚皮。你们初到险恶山脉"
"时，曾跟一群石狼打过一架。这几头准是那一群里的，不然怎么解释它们见了你就这么老实？这群披"
"着石甲的巨狼低头望着你，似乎在等你下一步动作。有几头打了个哈欠，就地趴下了。那个弗拉姆贝"
"里小伙子想从狼群中挤到你身边，另外几头又冲他龇起牙来。这些石狼个个都有你两倍大。那小伙子"
"本来就矮，站在它们中间，看着更小了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Um... Good doggies?"
msgstr "嗯……乖狗狗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I figured they'd be out for revenge after we..."
msgstr "我还以为它们会来报仇呢，毕竟咱们……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Took care of the big one."
msgstr "把最大的那头给收拾了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Seems that we're the big ones, now."
msgstr "看来这回轮到咱们当老大了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We are? You hardly come up to the things' shoulder."
msgstr "咱们？你站直了都够不着它的肩膀。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Tell that to it. Seems pretty supplicant to me."
msgstr "这话你跟它说去。我看它服气得很。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "How in the names of the Great Flame did you two do that? "
msgstr "圣焰在上，你们俩到底是怎么做到的？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We had a run in with their leader a while back, and it seems that they aren't too mad "
"that we... turned it into jerky."
msgstr ""
"前阵子，我们碰巧跟它们的头狼打了一架。看来，就算咱们把头狼……做成了肉干，它们也没怎么往心"
"里去。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Incredible. Animal Behaviorial Specialist Brunite at your service. Humans are a rarity "
"in these parts..."
msgstr ""
"真不可思议。我叫布鲁尼特，专门研究动物习性，很高兴为二位效劳。这一带可难得见到人类……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, normally they are, at least. The last time I saw some was actually..."
msgstr "嗯，至少平时很少见。说起来，我上回见到人类，还是在……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Wait. You were at the Linking! You saved our prince!"
msgstr "等等。接轨庆典那天，你们也在！就是你们救了我们的王子！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, we helped out a bit."
msgstr "我们也就帮了点忙。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Please, please, you're far too modest. I doubt any of us would have gotten out of there "
"alive were it not for your efforts."
msgstr "哎呀，二位太谦虚了。那天要是没有你们，我们这些人恐怕一个也逃不出来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "And... me doubly so, it'd seem. Thank you for saving me once again."
msgstr "至于我……看来已经是第二次靠你们捡回一条命了。多谢二位，又救了我一次。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We didn't have to do much, we're able to get a better vantage up here anyway."
msgstr "没费什么事。再说，爬到这里也好，能看得远些。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh? And what are you scouting out, if I may ask?"
msgstr "哦？冒昧问一句，二位在找什么？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We're headed out to the Misty Thicket. It'll be quite the journey."
msgstr "我们打算去迷雾丛林。一趟挺远的旅程。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What'd you learn about the behaviors of the Rockwolves? That they're hungry?"
msgstr "倒是你，研究石狼研究出什么来了？它们饿了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, actually, yes."
msgstr "呃，说起来，你还真说对了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They seem to designate members of their pack to hunt, while others serve other purposes."
msgstr "我发现狼群里似乎有分工。有些专门负责捕猎，其他的也各有用处。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"For example, the one at your feet there, its stone hide is closely related to "
"sandstone. Hunters will sharpen their teeth by gnawing on its hide, like you'd sharpen "
"your blade on a whetstone."
msgstr ""
"就拿你脚边这头来说，它身上那层石甲，质地跟砂岩很像。负责捕猎的狼就啃它的石甲磨牙，跟你用"
"磨刀石磨刀一个道理。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Sounds... useful, actually."
msgstr "这么一说……还真挺管用。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They metabolize both meat and stone, with different Rockwolves prioritizing different "
"stone and mineral types to change their hides in accordance with what the pack needs."
msgstr ""
"石狼既吃肉，也能消化石头。不同的石狼会挑不同的岩石和矿物来吃。狼群需要什么样的石甲，它们"
"就能长出什么样的石甲来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'd imagine you were acting in self-defense when you fought against the pack earlier. "
"Well, it seems they're missing a handful of crucial roles now."
msgstr ""
"你们之前跟它们动手，想来也是为了自保。不过眼下看来，狼群里有几样要紧的活儿，已经没狼能干"
"了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Maybe there's something that can be done for your journey..."
msgstr "说不定……我倒有个办法，能让你们这趟少走点路。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Brunite details his plans. He'd originally wanted to use the wolves as mounts to help "
"his people return back to their home once things were sorted with the Soulsmiths, but "
"maybe with your help, he could expidite his plans, in exchange for letting you bring "
"some of the wolves with you. They already seem plenty docile with you around, what's "
"the harm in trying, right? \n"
"\n"
"You return to the capitol, and run the idea of starting a breeding program for the "
"Rockwolves to the king, who simply laughs and waves his hand, seemingly letting the "
"Archivist write down and deal with aquiring the materials to set up a place to store, "
"raise, and train wolves, assuming they don't break out and eat you."
msgstr ""
"布鲁尼特说起了他的打算。他原本想把这些狼驯成坐骑。等炼魂师的事告一段落，族人们就能骑着它"
"们回家了。现在有你们帮忙，说不定能早点把这件事办成。作为回报，你们可以带上几头石狼赶路。"
"你们一来，它们就这么听话。试试又何妨？\n"
"\n"
"你们回到都城，把繁育石狼的打算说给国王听。国王哈哈一笑，大手一挥，典藏官便提笔记下，看来"
"筹集物资的事又落到了他头上。得先给狼群安个家，往后才好饲养、训练。当然，这一切的前提是，"
"它们别先跑出来把你们吃了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I feel soggy and miserable."
msgstr "我浑身都湿透了，真难受。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just want to find the beast and get back home."
msgstr "我只想赶紧找到那头野兽，早点回家。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The wolves are equal parts stone and organic, and with sufficent meat and sources of "
"minerals, they grow much faster than you'd ever expect. In conjunction with preparing a "
"route to the Misty Thicket, you frequently stop in to help Brunite with the Rockwolf "
"study, creating wolves that didn't seem to appear naturally before. Soon enough, by the "
"time you're ready to head out, you have three wolves with hides made of a material "
"similar to quartz, hoping it'd be light enough for travel but hard enough to protect "
"the beasts from any kind of dangerous monsters you may come across in the countryside."
msgstr ""
"石狼身上一半是血肉，一半是岩石。只要肉和矿物管够，它们长得比你想象中快得多。筹划前往迷雾"
"丛林的路线时，你也常去帮布鲁尼特研究石狼。你们甚至培育出了几种在野外似乎从未见过的石狼。"
"等到准备出发时，你们已经有了三头披着石英般外甲的狼。但愿这层甲够轻，跑长途时不碍事，又足"
"够结实，万一在野外撞上什么凶险的怪物，也护得住它们。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I can't believe it! Rockwolves feel like they were made to be domesticated. Most of "
"them are generally of good temperment, and they're so friendly too!"
msgstr "简直不敢相信！石狼简直天生就适合驯养。大多脾气都好，还特别黏人！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Milkbone here hardly stops licking me! I'm shocked at how fast they can grow under "
"controlled conditions, too, it reminds me of growing crystals as a boy."
msgstr ""
"就说奶骨吧，你看，她都舔我半天了！能控制饲养条件以后，它们竟然长得这么快。倒让我想起小时"
"候养晶体的事了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Are you sure that Milkbone isn't just seeing if you'd be a good addition to her hide? "
"Flamberians are mostly stone, right?"
msgstr ""
"你就这么肯定，奶骨舔你，不是在尝尝你这身石头适不适合拿来长石甲？你们弗拉姆贝里人身上，不"
"是大半都是石头吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I... hadn't considered that."
msgstr "我……这个我倒没想过。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "[Companion Name] be nice, I'm sure she's just a friendly, mostly feral wolf."
msgstr "[Companion Name]，别吓唬人家。奶骨肯定就是喜欢你。虽说野性是还没怎么褪。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Are you sure you want to join us though, Brunite? The Misty Thicket is a long ways away."
msgstr "不过，布鲁尼特，你真打算跟我们一起去？迷雾丛林可远着呢。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We're just scouting a path and locating that monster that attacked the Linking, but "
"we'll almost definitely get into some trouble at some point."
msgstr "这回虽说只是探路，找找袭击接轨庆典的那头怪物，可这一趟十有八九要碰上麻烦。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"And miss the opportunity to see how the first wolves we've bred behave in uncontrolled "
"conditions? Not a chance!"
msgstr ""
"这可是咱们养出来的第一批石狼。我还想亲眼看看它们在野外都会是什么表现呢。说什么我也得去！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Atop the quartz rockwolves, you make extrodinary time. The beasts are fast, incredibly "
"easy to care for, and defend themselves well enough that you feel comfortable sleeping "
"through the night without anyone on watch. Despite his shaky introduction, Brunite "
"proves to be quite capable while travelling to the Misty Wetlands with you, though he "
"does still jump a bit whenever Milkbone licks him, wondering if [Companion Name]'s joke "
"held any truth.\n"
"\n"
"Finding the Shambling Beast will be like finding a needle in a haystack - and that's if "
"it's even here in the first place - but you trudge into the wetlands regardless. The "
"Misty Wetlands have both mist and wetland in abundance, and you frequently have to stop "
"and cut your way through underbrush or use lumber to cross particularly deep stretches "
"of water, especially with your heavy Rockwolves accompanying you."
msgstr ""
"骑上这几头披着石英外甲的石狼，你们赶路快了许多。它们跑得快，好照料，也有本事保护自己。到"
"了夜里，你们连守夜的人都不用留，尽管踏踏实实睡到天亮。别看头一回见面时布鲁尼特那么狼狈，"
"去迷雾湿地的路上，他可一点儿没拖后腿。就是奶骨一舔他，他还是会吓得一缩，忍不住琢磨"
"[Companion Name]那句玩笑里会不会有几分真。\n"
"\n"
"要在这里找到跛行兽，无异于大海捞针。何况这根“针”究竟在不在这里，都还说不准。你们还是迈开"
"步子，走进了湿地。迷雾湿地倒真是名副其实，雾和水一样都不少。没走多远，你们就得停下来劈开"
"挡路的灌木。遇上水深的地方，还得伐木搭路，尤其是身后跟着这么几头沉甸甸的石狼。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "They started it."
msgstr "可是他们先动的手。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I wonder what they may have..."
msgstr "也不知道他们身上都带了些什么……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you sink your axe into yet another tree to cross another endless stretch of water, a "
"flaming bolt glances your shoulder and sinks into the thick bark. You drop your axe and "
"whip your head around to see the burning shilloette of a Flamberian far behind you, "
"with a hefty crossbow held aloft. You cry out and everyone dives into the water, "
"narrowly avoiding further projectiles. A volley of similar bolts follows soon after, "
"peppering the ground and trees around you, your party, and mounts. You poke your head "
"out of the water and see [Companion Name] fire a bolt of magic that freezes the water "
"in the air, providing a thin shield against the attacks' bolts."
msgstr ""
"前面又是一大片望不到头的积水。你的斧子刚砍进树干，一支燃烧的弩箭便擦过你的肩头，一头扎进"
"厚实的树皮。你扔下斧子，猛地回头。远处有个浑身冒着火光的弗拉姆贝里人，手里高举着一把重重"
"的十字弩。你大喊一声，众人齐齐扑进水里，险险避开接连射来的弩箭。紧接着又是一阵齐射，一支"
"支弩箭扎进你们和坐骑身旁的泥地与树干。你从水里探出头，只见[Companion Name]打出一道法术，"
"半空中的水顷刻间冻成了一面薄薄的冰盾，挡住了飞来的弩箭。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Those look like Flamberians!"
msgstr "那些好像是弗拉姆贝里人！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I fear you're right. I hope the two of you are... capable of dealing with them?"
msgstr "恐怕你没看错。二位……能对付得了他们吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"If we have to. Any clue on why they're out here, and what problem they'd have with us?"
msgstr "真要动手的话，肯定是能。你知道他们为什么在这儿，又为什么要袭击我们吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I mean, you're one of them, no?"
msgstr "你也是弗拉姆贝里人，对吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Not all Flamberians were too interested in peace with the Naladasi."
msgstr "不是所有弗拉姆贝里人都愿意跟纳里达西人讲和。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I'm sure the defectors have some way of identifying one another, and I'm sure I don't "
"look the part."
msgstr "那群叛逃者肯定有办法认出自己人。我嘛，一看就跟他们不是一伙的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Any idea on if this will cause any problems for us later on down the line?"
msgstr "那咱们跟他们动手，回头会不会惹出什么麻烦？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh, I highly doubt it! There's a reason why they're hiding all the way out here."
msgstr "哦，你说这个，我看不会！他们躲到这么偏远的地方，可是有原因的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Those that are willing to reject the Naladasi with violence aren't welcome in our "
"kingdom."
msgstr "我们王国不欢迎那些非要跟纳里达西人动武的家伙。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Plus, they fired first."
msgstr "再说了，也是他们先放的箭。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"That's enough for the two of you. Brunite gets your mounts to cover while you and "
"[Companion Name] do your best to move towards the Flamberians as quietly as you can "
"through the wetland bogs. Shrouded by the mist and setting sun, you're upon them before "
"they even know it. You reach up from the water and drag one of the attackers under, "
"silencing them as quickly as you can. The Flamberian next to him cries out, and the "
"group is thrown into chaos."
msgstr ""
"有这句话，你们俩心里就有数了。布鲁尼特带坐骑去找地方躲避。你和[Companion Name]则尽量放轻"
"动作，蹚过泥沼，朝那些弗拉姆贝里人摸去。暮色渐深，又有雾气遮掩。直到你们摸到跟前，他们都"
"没察觉。你从水下伸出手，拽住其中一个袭击者，将他拖进水里，没让他再出声。他身旁的弗拉姆贝"
"里人惊叫起来，人群顿时乱了套。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Has to be what we're looking for."
msgstr "准是我们要找的东西。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Here we are."
msgstr "到了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You and [Companion Name] pant in the mist, happy to be done with such messy work. "
"Killing monsters is one thing, but it's always a little bit different to be fighting "
"against human - or human adjacent - opponents, even if they're the aggressors. Brunite "
"brings your rockwolves over once the sounds of fighting die down, trying to avert his "
"eyes from the dead dwarves in the water."
msgstr ""
"你和[Companion Name]站在雾里直喘气。这场厮杀总算结束了，你也松了口气。杀怪物是一回事。可"
"当对手是人，或是跟人相差无几的矮人，动起手来，心里总归不一样。哪怕先动手的是他们。打斗声"
"一停，布鲁尼特便带着石狼走了过来。他转开视线，尽量不去看水里的矮人尸体。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You two are... efficient."
msgstr "你们两个……下手可真利落。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm sorry. They didn't seem to be too interested in talking through things."
msgstr "抱歉。看他们的样子，根本没打算跟我们谈。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We didn't have much choice in the matter."
msgstr "我们也没得选。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh, don't get me wrong, I won't shed any tears for them."
msgstr "别误会，我可不会为他们掉眼泪。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"They probably feared we'd give them up to Flamberian authorities if we found them out "
"here, and thought it'd be better to silence us."
msgstr "多半是咱们撞见了他们，他们怕咱们回去报信，就想干脆杀人灭口。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The two of you are just... "
msgstr "只是你们俩……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I can't think of many people who could move that quickly and leave that much death in "
"their wake. Regardless of the reason."
msgstr "这么一会儿工夫，竟然就能杀这么多人。我还真想不出有几个人办得到。不管是为了什么。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Brunite grimaces as Milkbone starts to sniff the corpse of one of the attackers, and "
"pulls her away from the body. You and [Companion Name] start to go through the "
"defectors' posessions and find a map and various plans they'd made. Several drafts of "
"ransom notes which lead you to believe they intended to kidnap Prince Cintak at some "
"point... they were ambitious if nothing else. They seemed to have a nearby camp, but "
"what interests you far more is an old ruined castle, the Flamberians had marked, "
"circled, and drawn several warnings of \"Death\" and \"Stay away\" around. Seems like a "
"good place to start your search. As you get closer to the old ruined castle, you find "
"tracks that stick out in the murk. Tracks made by hundreds of pairs of arms."
msgstr ""
"奶骨凑到一名袭击者的尸体旁嗅了嗅。布鲁尼特皱起脸，把她拉开。你和[Companion Name]翻了翻叛"
"逃者的东西，找到一张地图，还有几份行动计划。光是勒索信就打了好几份草稿。看来，他们还打过"
"绑架辛塔克王子的主意……别的不说，胆子倒是不小。地图上标着一处营地，看来那些叛逃者就驻扎在"
"附近。可真正让你在意的，是一座废弃的古堡。他们特意把古堡圈了出来，还在旁边反复写着“致命"
"危险”“别靠近”。看来，要找那头野兽，就该先去这座古堡看看。离古堡越近，泥地里的痕迹就越显"
"眼。那是几百双手臂爬过时留下的。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The Shambling Beast made a mess of a trail through the Misty Thicket, and you wager "
"you'd be able to follow it all the way out pretty easily, now that you've found its "
"trail. Downed trees, a huge gouge through the ground thats already filled with water, "
"and occasional lumps of flesh are pretty telling that you're on the right track. As you "
"get closer and closer to what you presume would be the castle, the stench of death "
"seems to hang in the air, which is impressive for such a horrid bog that already "
"doesn't smell like a bundle of roses.\n"
"\n"
"The two of you leave Brunite and the Rockwolves behind, trusting in your ability to "
"move more quietly and take up less space than huge beasts with stone for fur. You "
"follow the trail until you find what the Flamberians detailed on their map. Row upon "
"row of corpses are pinned to the outer walls of a ancient castle. All of the bodies are "
"seemingly frozen in space, but doubtlessly alive, since the wall adornments seem to "
"moan and twitch from time to time. The mist-shrouded moat surrounding the castle does "
"little to brighten the image in your mind. You let out an involentary shiver as you "
"gaze up at the macbre sight.\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name] pulls you away, sure that the monster you're looking for is within the "
"walls. This is definitely not something you can take on alone. It's time to see just "
"how serious King Oyadazminis is about going to war, because it'll take quite the siege "
"to bring down these walls. The journey back is much faster than your journey in, "
"perhaps in part due to the back you know you'll have dry feet for the first time in a "
"while. It's still quite the trek to return to the capitol, but it's comparatively "
"smooth sailing than your trip to the Misty Thicket."
msgstr ""
"跛行兽一路穿过迷雾丛林，把沿途搅得一片狼藉。如今找着了它的踪迹，哪怕一路追出林子，想来也"
"不会跟丢。沿途的树倒了一片，地上被拖出一道深沟，沟里已经积满了水。偶尔还能看见几块掉落的"
"血肉。你们走对了。你估摸着，古堡就在前面了。越往前走，空气里的腐尸味就越浓。这片沼泽本来"
"就够臭的了，那股味道居然还能盖过去。\n"
"\n"
"你们让布鲁尼特和石狼留在后面。两个人悄悄摸过去，总比带着几头浑身披着石甲的庞然大物容易藏"
"身。你们沿着痕迹继续前行，终于看见了弗拉姆贝里人在地图上标出的那座古堡。古堡的外墙上，密"
"密麻麻钉着一排又一排尸体。那些身体仿佛被定在了墙上，可分明还活着。隔一会儿，墙上的这些"
"“装饰”就会抽动几下，发出呻吟。城堡四周还有一道护城河，雾气沉沉地压在水面上，更添了几分阴"
"森。你仰头望着这一幕，不由得打了个寒战。\n"
"\n"
"[Companion Name]把你拉开。她确信，你们要找的怪物就在城墙里面。光凭你们俩，这回肯定应付不"
"来。要打下这座城堡，少不了一场硬仗。奥亚达兹米尼斯国王说过要出兵，是时候看看他究竟有多大"
"决心了。回去时，你们的脚程比来时快多了。说不定是因为一想到总算能离开这片沼泽，让湿透的双"
"脚干一干，你们就不由得加快了脚步。回都城还有很长一段路要走。好在比起来迷雾丛林时的跋涉，"
"这一路顺当多了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.DisplayName
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "MQ27"
msgstr "MQ27"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Bring Down The House - The weapon to defeat the Shambling Beast is ready, and a path to "
"the Soulsmith's Ruin is cleared. Prince Cintak and Princess Redilok will lead their "
"people into battle, with you and [Companion Name] at the head. "
msgstr ""
"攻破迷雾要塞——斩杀跛行兽的武器已经备好，通往那座被炼魂师占据的古堡的路也已打通。辛塔克王"
"子和雷迪洛克公主将率领族人出征，由你和[Companion Name]打头阵。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I can't wait to see them in action."
msgstr "真想早点看看它们上阵是什么样。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We should get some rest."
msgstr "咱们该歇会儿了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The path to the Misty Keep is plotted, a weapon to slay the Shambling Beast is strapped "
"to your back, and things are slowly returning to normal in Koganusan. As you walk "
"through the outer courtyard of the palace, you notice a large number of guards out and "
"training against one another, with the occasional Flamberian even dotting their ranks - "
"holdovers from the Linking that haven't been able to start the trek back to their "
"homeland yet, and have decided to accompany the prince until he sees it fit to return.\n"
"\n"
"When you enter the throne room, King Oyadazminis looks down from his seat with a "
"knowing expression."
msgstr ""
"前往迷雾要塞的路线已经摸清，能杀死跛行兽的武器就背在你身上。科加努桑也在一点点恢复往日的"
"模样。你穿过王宫外院，看见大批守卫正在两两对练，队伍里偶尔还能瞧见几个弗拉姆贝里人的身"
"影。他们都是接轨庆典后留下来的，一时没能启程返乡，索性决定跟着王子，等他认为时机合适了，"
"再一道回去。\n"
"\n"
"走进王座大厅，奥亚达兹米尼斯国王从座上低头看向你，像是已经猜到了你的来意。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "You're ready, aren't you?"
msgstr "都准备好了，是吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I believe we are."
msgstr "应该差不多了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"It's been many long years since we actively sought dealings with your kind, but what "
"transpired at the Linking has given me much to think about."
msgstr "我们已经很多年没主动跟人类打过交道了。不过，接轨庆典上发生的事，让我想了很多。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Though I doubt most humans would be willing to help even a fraction as much as the two "
"of you have, perhaps we've been... avoidant, for far too long."
msgstr ""
"我不指望大多数人类都能像你们一样帮我们这么多，哪怕帮上十分之一也好。不过，也许是我们……关"
"起门来太久了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Once those who attacked my people are burried in thier marsh, we'll send an envoy or "
"two around. Let your people know that we'd be willing to entertain more than a few "
"tourists, from time to time."
msgstr ""
"等把那些袭击我族人的家伙埋进他们自己的沼泽里，我打算派一两位使节出去走走。也让你们的人知"
"道，我们愿意跟你们多些来往，不必总是偶尔来几个游客就算了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The world would be much better off for it."
msgstr "那样一来，对大家都有好处。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You know they would be. We'll see if your fancy nobles can stay standing after a single "
"glass of fine Naladasi liqour."
msgstr ""
"那当然了。到时候倒要看看，你们那些贵族老爷喝上一杯上好的纳里达西烈酒，还能不能站得稳。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "But, as much as I'd like to, I can't entertain the thought of festivities yet."
msgstr "不过，虽然我也想热热闹闹地办一场，但眼下还不是庆祝的时候。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We've read over your reports and path to the Soulsmiths' keep."
msgstr "你们送来的报告，还有通往炼魂师要塞的路线，我们都看过了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As the king has so kindly promised, our people are at your disposal, though we'll be "
"joining you as well."
msgstr "国王既已应允，我们的人手就听二位调遣。我们也会随你们一道出征。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As will my daughter... Try as I might, she refuses to stay off the battlefield, despite "
"her injuries. The..."
msgstr "还有我女儿……我怎么劝都不管用。伤成这样，她还是非上战场不可。那位……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "...Prince, seems to have taken a liking to my daughter, and is joining her. "
msgstr "……王子，看来是喜欢上我女儿了，也要陪她去。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We'd be fortunate to have the four of you alongside us, but wouldn't that be... "
"dangerous for you all?"
msgstr "有四位跟我们并肩作战，是我们的荣幸。可这对各位来说……会不会太危险了？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "What kind of father would I be if I let my daughter fight my battles for me?"
msgstr "要我躲在后面，让女儿替我上阵？那我还算什么父亲？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "The king has also expressed interest in making sure nothing... untoward occ-"
msgstr "国王还说，他得亲自看着，免得有些事……不太合乎分……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Ahem. We've prepared several wagons. I hear that your little breeding program with the "
"Rockwolves has gone well?"
msgstr "咳。我们已经备好了几辆大车。听说，你们养石狼的事进展不错？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We feel they'd be far better for handling any outdoor excursions than our current "
"beasts of burden. Brunite was more than happy to help create some wolves that could "
"help."
msgstr ""
"要在野外拉车，它们应该比我们现在用的驮兽更合适。布鲁尼特一听说能帮上忙，高高兴兴地就去培"
"育适合拉车的石狼了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It sounds like we're just about ready then, yes?"
msgstr "这么说，咱们也算万事俱备了吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We'll head out to prepare."
msgstr "那我们这就去准备出发。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"As you leave the palace, the most of training guards have already mobilized, with the "
"remainer saluting the two of you as you pass by. You meet Brunite at the caverns set "
"aside for the Rockwolf breeding program, and even he dawns an axe and simple armor. He "
"brings the two of you your wolves, then takes a seat upon Milkbone and takes off down a "
"long line of pens, cutting open the fences as he runs along, a growing pack of "
"Stonewolves following behind him as he charges through the caverns and out of the "
"caverns.\n"
"\n"
"It's a little startling to see just how many wolves can be made in the right "
"conditions, and hope that Brunite hasn't made too much of a fuss in the capitol. "
"Despite the sight, many citizens cheer after you as you race through the city and out "
"into the fresh air above. The pack slows as you step outside to see a large procession "
"of Naladasi with armed wagons, some topped with braziers you imagine are to ward off "
"the mists of the thicket.\n"
"\n"
"There are numerous shouts as you arrive, but not because of you, it's because of the "
"similarly sized horde growing in the distance. A large, orderly rank of Flamberians "
"march towards the Naladasi, carrying large waving banners that make the whole army "
"appear as if they're on fire. You spot Prince Cintak flag down king Oyadazminis, and "
"the two of them march out to meet the army. An hour passes before the army continues "
"its advance, banners now down. Hopefully that's a good thing?\n"
"\n"
"The Prince announces that due to the silence that followed after the Linking, the "
"Flamberians had reason to suspect the Naladasi had attacked the procession and "
"kidnapped him, but he's informed his mother - the queen - of the full situation, and "
"the army that was sent to attack the Naladasi are instead joining them to attack "
"Soulsmiths. Apperently.\n"
"\n"
"The journey back out to the Misty Thicket starts tense, but as more and more stories "
"are traded between the rank and file, the dwarves stoke one another's passion towards "
"their shared enemy, and find themselves growing closer in the process.\n"
"\n"
"The wagons are pulled around to create a wall of sorts a few hours out from the Misty "
"Keep, and you and [Companion Name] keep yourselves busy by helping to prepare the "
"massive bolts that'll be loaded into the ballista-carrying wagons."
msgstr ""
"你们离开王宫时，方才还在操练的守卫大多已经动身。余下的人见你们经过，纷纷抬手致意。你们去"
"饲养石狼的洞窟找布鲁尼特。连他也披上了简易的护甲，带上了一把斧头。他把你们的坐骑牵来，自"
"己翻身骑上奶骨，沿着一长排兽栏疾驰而过，边跑边劈开栅栏。石狼一头接一头地跟上他，狼群越聚"
"越大，跟着他一路穿过洞穴，冲向洞外。\n"
"\n"
"你知道条件合适，石狼就长得快，却没想到布鲁尼特已经养出了这么一大群。只盼他带着狼群穿过都"
"城时，别闹出太大的动静。不过，看见这么一群石狼奔过街头，倒有不少市民沿途为你们欢呼。你们"
"一路冲出城，迎面吹来了地上清新的风。狼群出了洞口，渐渐放慢脚步。前方是纳里达西人的大队人"
"马，随行的战车都装着武器，有些车顶上还架着火盆，想来是为了驱散林中的浓雾。\n"
"\n"
"你们刚到，队伍里便响起一阵呼喊。众人看的却不是你们。远处正有另一支人马逼近，看那阵势，人"
"数恐怕和这边不相上下。那是一支弗拉姆贝里大军。他们列着整齐的队伍，朝纳里达西人开来。大旗"
"迎风招展，远远望去，整支军队像是一片移动的火海。你看见辛塔克王子朝奥亚达兹米尼斯国王招了"
"招手，两人一同上前，迎向那支大军。一个小时后，弗拉姆贝里大军才重新开拔。方才还高高飘扬的"
"旗帜，这会儿都降下来了。这算是好兆头吧？\n"
"\n"
"辛塔克王子告诉大家，接轨庆典过后一直没有消息传回去，弗拉姆贝里人有理由怀疑，是纳里达西人"
"袭击了赴会的队伍，又掳走了王子。他刚刚已将来龙去脉告诉母亲，也就是弗拉姆贝里女王。原本奉"
"命前来攻打纳里达西的大军，如今要和他们并肩作战，一同讨伐炼魂师。至少，按王子的说法是这"
"样。\n"
"\n"
"重返迷雾丛林的路上，两军起初还互相提防着。可走着走着，士兵们聊起各自的遭遇，你一言我一"
"语，对炼魂师的怒火越烧越旺，有了共同的敌人，两支队伍不知不觉熟络了不少。\n"
"\n"
"离迷雾要塞还有几个小时路程时，大军停下来，将车辆围成一道屏障。你和[Companion Name]也跟着"
"忙活起来，帮弩手备好战车上的重弩要用的大箭。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I just have to reel them in before the shadows do."
msgstr "得抢在那些黑影前头，把人拉上来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "We did what we could."
msgstr "我们尽力了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You're pleased to take a bit of time to yourself, even if it is to do more work. The "
"journey over had been long and tiring, constantly riding between the ranks and guiding "
"troops. The Flamberian queen has repeatedly called for your attention, but with as many "
"moving parts as this war procession has had, you simply haven't had the time. "
"Thankfully, Prince Cintak has reassured you that his mother is aware of the stakes and "
"your part in keeping everything moving, and is more than happy to wait. You lay down "
"after having earned your rest, and try to calm your nerves before finally falling to "
"sleep.\n"
"\n"
"After nowhere near enough time, you open your eyes to the daylight, you realize... "
"there shouldn't be daylight. You were in a covered wagon. You look around and notice "
"that four Flamberians have lifted your cot and carried you out in front of the queen. "
"[Companion Name] is in a similarly dazzed, groggy state as yourself, both of you "
"seemingly having been tired and secure enough to sleep through the... basically "
"kidnapping. Prince Cintak stands beside his mother, mortified, and shoots you an "
"apologetic look."
msgstr ""
"虽说手上还有活儿，你倒很高兴，终于能有片刻清静。这一路实在够累的。你骑着石狼在队伍之间来"
"回奔走，不断给部队指路。弗拉姆贝里女王已经几次派人来找你，可这么大一支队伍要协调，你实在"
"抽不开身。好在辛塔克王子让你放心。母亲明白这一仗关系重大，也知道你一路忙着给大军带路。等"
"你得空了再见面，她不介意。忙完这一切，你总算能躺下了。你努力让紧绷的神经放松下来，好一会"
"儿才睡着。\n"
"\n"
"感觉才睡了没多久，你一睁眼，便看见了天光。等等……这里怎么会有天光？你明明睡在一辆带篷的大"
"车里。你四下一看，这才发现，四个弗拉姆贝里人把你连人带床抬了出来，一路抬到了女王面前。"
"[Companion Name]也是一脸茫然，睡眼惺忪。看来你们俩都累坏了，又睡得实在安心，竟然连这么一"
"场……几乎算得上绑架的事都没察觉。辛塔克王子站在母亲身旁，窘得不知如何是好，只能递给你一个"
"歉意的眼神。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It is a pleasure to finally see the faces of my son's saviors. "
msgstr "总算见到救我儿子的两位恩人了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I apologize for disrupting your sleep, but I wished to make myself known to you before "
"we are to head into battle alongside one another."
msgstr "扰了二位清梦，还请见谅。只是马上就要并肩上阵，我想在那之前，先跟二位打声招呼。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I- I- Good morning, your excellency, queen..."
msgstr "我……呃，早安，女王陛下……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Rest, child. I've done away with my name long ago, like all those who ascend to my "
"rank. You may refer to me as the Flame. "
msgstr ""
"别拘束，孩子。和历代登上王位的人一样，我早已舍弃了从前的名字。你们可以称我为“圣焰”。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I tried to get her to hold off a while longer, but she was insistant."
msgstr "我劝过母亲，让你们再睡一会儿，可她执意要见你们。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Pleased to meet you, your grace, but... may I ask why you've brought us here?"
msgstr "很荣幸见到您，陛下。不过……您特意把我们带到这里，是有什么事吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "From what I've heard, the two of you are the reason my son still breathes. "
msgstr "我听说，我儿子如今还活着，全是多亏了你们两个。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My nation is in your debt, as am I. Were it not for your efforts, my people would have "
"surely clashed against the Naladasi, and we'd be all the worse for it."
msgstr ""
"我和我的国家，都欠二位一份恩情。要不是你们，我的族人早就和纳里达西人打起来了，那样只会两"
"败俱伤。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"We were just doing what is right. The Soulsmiths... they've torn apart so many homes, "
"our own included."
msgstr "我们只是做了该做的事。炼魂师……他们毁了太多人的家，我们自己的家也在其中。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "I'm just glad we were able to get to him in time."
msgstr "能及时赶到，把王子救下来，我已经很庆幸了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "As am I."
msgstr "我也是。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"I just wanted to bring it to your attention that I'm endlessly thankful for your "
"assistance, and for your efforts, I wish to reward you once we return to our homeland. "
"I'd like to-"
msgstr ""
"把二位请来，就是想让你们知道，我有多感激你们的帮助。等回了弗拉姆贝里，我要好好答谢二位。"
"我打算……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"She wants to show off that she can give you more than the Naladasi and keep you around "
"as my personal bodyguards."
msgstr "母亲是想让你们看看，她出手比纳里达西人阔绰，好把你们留在我身边，当我的贴身护卫。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Well, we're flattered, but..."
msgstr "这……我们很荣幸，不过……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"My darling little lava rock is right! You're heroes and should be treated as such! AND "
"I find it outrageous that that cheapskate king has you sleeping in a cart!"
msgstr ""
"我的小熔岩宝贝说得没错！你们是英雄，就该有英雄的待遇！那个抠门的国王竟让你们睡大车？简直"
"不像话！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Are you sure the two of you want to be on the front lines?"
msgstr "二位当真要上前线吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Perhaps the three of you, or four since my precious son seems to have a thing for that "
"cute little Naladasi princess, can wait back here while we level the castle of those "
"rotten Soulsmiths for ever daring to-"
msgstr ""
"不如你们三个留在后面等着？哦，该是四个，我的宝贝儿子好像看上了那个可爱的纳里达西小公主。"
"你们就在这儿等着，看我们把那帮混账炼魂师的城堡夷为平地。竟敢对我儿子……"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Oh Flames, mother!"
msgstr "圣焰在上，母亲！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Shush dear, you can't fault a mother for trying to keep her baby safe."
msgstr "好啦，亲爱的。当妈的想护着自己的孩子，总没错吧？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Since you're all so determined to join us on the battlefield, see to it that he's safe, "
"will you?"
msgstr "既然你们一个个都铁了心要上战场，就替我保护好他，好吗？"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Of course, we'll do our best to make sure as many people make it back alive as we can."
msgstr "当然。我们会尽全力，让尽可能多的人活着回来。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Please do... I can't lose my son a second time."
msgstr "拜托了……我不能再失去他了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"The queen seems to be at least partially assuaged by this and nods her head. The "
"Flamberians that carried you out now pick your cots up and carry you back to the wagon, "
"and you try to digest what just happened.\n"
"\n"
"After a couple more hours, the camp begins to shuffle once more. The dwarves break down "
"camp and begin to move out once more. You and [Companion Name] mount your Rockwolves "
"and lead the way, guiding the group across the more percarious bits of terrain and "
"waiting for them to create paths to get wagons across large stretches of water when "
"required. The castle looms in the distance, almost seemingly a source of the Misty "
"Thicket's fog itself. The walls covered in corpses only shake the resolve of the "
"dwarves for a moment, though you hear several utterances of how sick the people inside "
"must be.\n"
"\n"
"Soulsmiths line the walls, along with summoned beasts that remind you of bats, with "
"mouths that are far too large.\n"
"\n"
"Wagons are pulled up to form an armored wall, and then, everyone bursts into motion. "
"Several large balls of energy soar over the walls of Misty Keep, but are burned away by "
"Flamberian mages, or sent far off course by Naladasi mages interferring with their "
"course. Four of the wagons' walls fall away to reveal giant ballista, which are loaded "
"with bolts created just last night. You and [Companion Name] move through the ranks and "
"direct their fire, and the balista shots land true. When they sink into the wall, "
"glowing runestones across their surface glow bright, then explode, ripping large "
"sections of the ancient castle apart. You hear and see King Oyadazminis let out a "
"battlecry as he hefts a large javilen towards the ramparts and snaps his fingers just "
"before contact, causing the bolt to explode in a dazzling ball of light that blows "
"twenty Soulsmiths apart. The Archivist twists his staff in the air and halts another "
"ball of green energy above the army before sending it back over the wall towards "
"whatever sent it in the first place, causing the entire castle to shake with the "
"impact.\n"
"\n"
"Soulsmiths fire all manner of bolt, arrow, and magic towards the dwarves, and they "
"return fire, but the evergrowing swarm of bat-like creatures harass the them. You watch "
"as several dwarves are picked up by the beasts and are dropped into the moat around the "
"castle, where large, dark shadows quickly pull the soliders under the water. Bats are "
"burned away, and more balista shots are loosed at the walls, but with the force you're "
"now taking, one of the balls of green energy makes it through your defenses and crashes "
"into one of the wagons, leaving it a smoldering pile of scrap. The bats grow further in "
"number, and your find a startling number of dwarves being carried away, while the "
"Flamberian Queen seems to be frozen in shock. You grab a length of rope with a hook on "
"the end, meant to scale the walls, and instead use it to fish out a dwarf from the "
"water. Many others around you follow suit, while the back ranks cover you."
msgstr ""
"女王听了这话，似乎总算安心了些，轻轻点了点头。刚才抬你们来的几个弗拉姆贝里人又抬起行军"
"床，把你们原样送回车里。你躺在床上，还有些回不过神来。\n"
"\n"
"又过了几个小时，营地里重新有了动静。矮人们拔营，再次出发。你和[Companion Name]骑上石狼，"
"在前头带路，领着队伍穿过几处难走的地段。碰上大片积水，你们便停下来，等后面的人搭好路，让"
"车辆通过。远处，城堡的轮廓隐约浮现。迷雾丛林里的浓雾仿佛都是从那座城堡里涌出来的。望见挂"
"满尸体的城墙，矮人们也只迟疑了片刻。你听见好几个人低声咒骂，干得出这种事，城里那帮家伙得"
"有多丧心病狂。\n"
"\n"
"炼魂师沿着城头一字排开。它们身旁的召唤兽形似蝙蝠，一张张嘴却大得出奇。\n"
"\n"
"战车向前靠拢，连成一道铁壁。下一刻，所有人都动了起来。几个巨大的魔法光球从迷雾要塞的城头"
"飞来。弗拉姆贝里法师用火将它们烧尽，纳里达西法师则施法改变它们的方向，让它们远远偏离了目"
"标。四辆大车的侧板落下，露出里面的巨弩。昨晚刚做好的弩箭，此刻已架在弩上。你和"
"[Companion Name]穿行在队伍间，指挥弩手瞄准。射出的弩箭支支命中城墙。箭身深深射入墙体，嵌"
"在上面的符文石骤然亮起，随即炸开。古堡的城墙一下就被炸塌了好几段。一声战吼传来。你转头看"
"去，只见奥亚达兹米尼斯国王举起一支大标枪，朝城垛掷去。标枪即将击中城头时，他打了个响指。"
"一团耀眼的强光炸开，当场将二十名炼魂师炸得粉碎。典藏官凌空一转法杖，将又一颗绿色光球定在"
"大军头顶，随即原路送了回去。光球越过城墙，正中发出攻击的地方，震得整座城堡都在摇晃。\n"
"\n"
"炼魂师朝矮人射来弩箭、羽箭和各式法术。矮人立即还击，可那群蝙蝠般的怪物越聚越多，不断俯冲"
"下来，搅得他们难以招架。你眼看着几名矮人被野兽抓到半空，丢进城堡周围的护城河。几个硕大的"
"黑影迅速游来，把落水的士兵拖进了水底。一群蝙蝠被烈火烧尽，又一轮重弩射向城墙。可敌人的攻"
"势越发猛烈，一颗绿色光球穿过防线，正中一辆战车。转眼间，那辆车就只剩一堆冒烟的残骸。蝙蝠"
"还在增加，被抓走的矮人越来越多，多得叫你心惊。弗拉姆贝里女王却站在原地一动不动，像是被眼"
"前的惨状惊呆了。你抓起一条原本用来攀上城墙的钩索，甩进河里，把一名矮人拉了上来。周围许多"
"人见状，也纷纷效仿。后排的士兵则掩护你们救人。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Description
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Today, the beast dies."
msgstr "今天，那野兽非死不可。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.CompletedDescription
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's over."
msgstr "结束了。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"You do what you can, hauling as many dwarves out of the water as you have time for. "
"Tons of hooks fly into the water once the others catch wind of your idea. You haul up "
"more dwarves than you can count, but as you reel in another, your rope goes taught and "
"is ripped from your hands, then goes slack. Whatever is in the water is very, very, "
"big.\n"
"\n"
"The Flame is ripped from her trance-like state. It wasn't shock, the woman was "
"preparing. The thicket behind the dwarves cracks and screams as a wave of golden fire "
"washes overhead like a wave crashing on the beach. The sky is blotted out by golden "
"flame that sweeps through the air and rips through the majority of the Soulsmiths' bats "
"and crashes against the wall, lighting the corpses ablaze. Where they were still "
"before, the living wall now screams at your forces, with many of them tearing away bits "
"of their body and turning it into balls of black magic which they then pelt you with.\n"
"\n"
"Each one explodes in black flashes with concussive force, sending those they hit to the "
"ground. Another wagon is destroyed as a volley of green magic comes over the wall once "
"more. Soulsmiths atop the wall fire at the undefended dwarves, but both races return "
"with their own bolts in turn. Princess Redilok stands atop one of the balista wagons "
"and charges the bolt that is fired from it. It connects with the south-western tower, "
"and explodes with startling force. The tower groans and collapses due to the damage, "
"Soulsmiths try in vain to jump from its collapsing weight, but land in the water "
"amongst whatever monster they have patrolling the depths."
msgstr ""
"你抓紧时间往上拉人，能救一个是一个。众人见你用钩索救人，也纷纷效仿，转眼间，无数铁钩从岸"
"上飞进了河里。你已经记不清拉上来多少人了。正要再拉一个，手里的绳索突然绷紧，一股巨力猛地"
"将它从你手中扯走，紧接着，绳子又松了下来。水底下那东西，大得吓人。\n"
"\n"
"圣焰终于动了。她不是吓呆了。她一直在蓄势。矮人身后的密林发出一阵刺耳的爆裂声。金色烈焰掠"
"过众人头顶，如同巨浪轰然拍岸。金焰遮天蔽日，横扫半空，将炼魂师召出的蝙蝠烧去了大半，随后"
"猛撞上城墙，点燃了钉在墙上的尸体。刚才还一动不动的尸体，此刻齐齐朝你们尖叫。许多尸体从自"
"己身上撕下血肉，揉成漆黑的魔法光球，劈头盖脸地砸来。\n"
"\n"
"每颗光球都在一闪而过的黑光中炸开，被击中的人当场便被震倒在地。又一轮绿色魔法越过城墙，再"
"次摧毁了一辆战车。城头的炼魂师瞄准失去掩护的矮人开火，两族矮人各自举弩还击。雷迪洛克公主"
"站上一辆弩车，将魔力注入弩箭。巨弩应声而发。那支箭正中西南角的塔楼，轰然炸开，威力惊人。"
"塔楼发出不堪重负的呻吟，随即轰然倒塌。炼魂师们纵身跳开，想躲过坠落的巨石，却落入护城河"
"里，掉进了那些在深水中来回游弋的怪物之间。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "It's time! Their forces are scattered!"
msgstr "就是现在！他们的阵形散了！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "Ready the rope bolts!"
msgstr "准备绳索弩箭！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "For those who died at the Linking!"
msgstr "为接轨庆典上的死难者报仇！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid "For all the lives the Soulsmiths have claimed!"
msgstr "为所有惨遭炼魂师毒手的人报仇！"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.Steps.Dialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"Only two of the four balista carts still stand, but it's enough. Ropes are already tied "
"to the large bolts which are launched and burried into the top of the drawbridge. "
"Brunite sees to the Rockwolves and orders them to charge away from the keep, pulling "
"the ropes taught. Another pair of bolts are launched. Then another. Then another. You "
"lose another of the carts to a group of Soulsmiths that has flown over the wall atop "
"giant versions of the bats that swarmed you before the golden flames burned the from "
"the sky, but they're eventually cut down.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, the drawbridge gives and comes crashing down. The path into the Misty Keep is "
"open.  Wolves are unteathered and then sent back towards the keep, their stony bodies "
"deflecting some of the smaller projectiles as they crash into the ranks of Soulsmiths "
"on the other side of the gate. Flamberian and Naladasi charge side-by-side across the "
"bridge, some stopping to pull up comrades from the water. As dwarf and Soulsmith fall, "
"an all too familiar sight that brings back memories of the Linking washes over you. A "
"pulse of green light, then the dead begin to move once more. The Shambling Beast is "
"here.\n"
"\n"
"You charge amongst the dwarves with [Companion Name] at your side, and you find "
"yourself face-to-face with a Soulsmith. A butcher. A monster. She raises her staff "
"towards you, but is carved down by Prince Cintak, who leads the charge. The man yells "
"to those around him to clear a path.\n"
"\n"
"The Shambling Beast crawls towards you, endless rows of arms churning the earth beneath "
"it. You lift your Soulmetal-lined Blade and charge through the crowd."
msgstr ""
"四辆弩车如今只剩两辆，不过，两辆也够了。绳索早已系在巨型弩箭上。弩箭接连射出，深深扎进吊"
"桥顶端。布鲁尼特指挥石狼掉头，向远离要塞的方向猛冲，绳索顿时绷得笔直。又有两支弩箭飞向吊"
"桥。弩弦再响，两箭齐发。紧跟着，又是一轮。一群炼魂师骑着巨蝠越过城头。那些巨蝠与先前被金"
"焰烧死的怪物一模一样，个头却大得多。你们最终将这一队炼魂师斩落，却也又损失了一辆弩车。\n"
"\n"
"终于，吊桥再也撑不住，轰然砸落。通往迷雾要塞的路打开了。石狼身上的绳索一解开，便被驱向要"
"塞。小些的箭矢打在它们的石甲上，纷纷弹开。它们一头撞进了城门另一侧的炼魂师阵中。弗拉姆贝"
"里矮人和纳里达西矮人并肩冲过吊桥，不时有人停下，伸手把落水的战友拉上来。矮人和炼魂师相继"
"倒下。眼前忽然出现了再熟悉不过的一幕，你一下子想起了接轨庆典。一道绿光扫过，死者又动了起"
"来。跛行兽就在这里。\n"
"\n"
"你随矮人们一同冲锋，[Companion Name]紧跟在侧。混战中，一名炼魂师迎面挡住了你。一个刽子"
"手。一个怪物。她举起法杖对准你，却被一马当先率军冲锋的辛塔克王子挥刃斩倒。王子向四周高"
"喊，让众人为你清出一条路。\n"
"\n"
"跛行兽向你爬来。它身下那一排排望不到头的手臂翻搅着泥土，一寸寸逼近。你高举镶着魂钢刃的长"
"刀，冲过人群。"

#. TRANSLATORS: Quest.CompletionDialogue.DialogueText
#: Data/Packages/MelvorBase.json
msgid ""
"With each stroke of your blade, its Soulsteel edge seems to quiver with delight. You "
"find the blade actively pulling towards its source and relishing in the pain it "
"inflicts upon the Shambling Beast. You carve through the beast, the blade pulls you "
"further, and you climb atop the spongey flesh of the creature. \n"
"\n"
"Hundreds of arms grasp at you as it tries in vain to pull you off, but [Companion Name] "
"batters them away, ripping a spike of Soulsteel from the monster and weilding it like a "
"mallet, repeatedly crashing down upon the beast. Your sword continues to delight in "
"cleaving through flesh, but you wrest control of it long enough to drive the sword into "
"cage fused with the back of the Shambling Beast.\n"
"\n"
"With that, another pulse of green light is unleashed and you're thrown from the "
"creature, leaving your sword wedged in the metal of the cage. As you sail through the "
"air, you see the undead begin to drop, but the Soulsmiths fight on. However, without "
"support from the undead, they're far outnumbered by the dwarves. \n"
"\n"
"The Shambling Beast is dead. You've won.\n"
"\n"
"You feel nothing but relief as you crash into the ground, and everything goes dark."
msgstr ""
"每一刀劈下去，魂钢刀刃都在颤动，仿佛在欢喜。刀竟主动往跛行兽身上拽。它原本就是从那头野兽"
"身上取下来的，如今每让野兽多受一分痛苦，它就越发欢欣。你一刀劈开野兽的皮肉，刀还在牵着你"
"往前。你顺势攀上了它绵软如海绵的身躯。\n"
"\n"
"上百条手臂伸来抓你，想把你拖下去。[Companion Name]挥开那些手臂，又从怪物身上硬生生拔出一"
"根魂钢尖刺，当作大锤，一下接一下地往野兽身上砸。你的刀还贪恋着劈开血肉的滋味。你跟它较着"
"劲，总算暂时夺回了控制，将刀狠狠刺进跟跛行兽脊背长在一起的金属笼中。\n"
"\n"
"又一道绿光猛然迸发，将你从野兽背上震飞。你的刀还牢牢嵌在金属笼上。你还没落地，就看见那些"
"死而复起的亡者纷纷倒下。炼魂师却还在战斗。可没了亡者助阵，炼魂师的人数就远不及矮人了。\n"
"\n"
"跛行兽死了。你们赢了。\n"
"\n"
"你重重地摔在地上，心里只觉得如释重负。随即，你眼前一黑，什么也不知道了。"

